(Phnom Penh): This Monday, February 4, 2019, at the National Gendarmerie Command, General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Chairman of the National Committee. To prevent and suppress natural resource crimes, chaired a meeting of the National Committee for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes.
The meeting was also attended by the Chairman, Vice-Chairman, members of the Committee, representatives of the Ministry of Justice, representatives of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, the Director General of the General Department of Immigration, the delegation of the Royal Government in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise, officers of Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, National Police Chief and many other officers of the Royal Gendarmerie.
During the meeting, the Commander of the National Gendarmerie ordered the following plans to prevent and suppress natural resource crimes as follows:
1: Prevent and effectively suppress natural resource crimes such as deforestation, illegal timber transportation and export, illegal hunting, and illegal wildlife exports. Invasion and occupation of state land, as well as illegal mining throughout the country.
2. Investigate the perpetrators and those involved in deforestation and illegal timber transportation, as well as those who commit natural resource crimes.
3. To arrest suspects and gather all exhibits related to natural resource crimes and prepare a case to send the suspects to court in accordance with the procedures of the law in force in Cambodia.
4: Concentrate forces to intervene, prevent and suppress all natural resource crimes that may occur, especially in the Northeastern provinces.
General Sao Sokha also requested the National Committee for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes as follows:
1. All relevant units must mobilize forces, means, equipment and manage all professional measures to cooperate to implement this plan successfully.
2. Cooperate with all professional units to exchange information and use all mechanisms and means to seize all information situations related to natural resource crimes. And through this information, it is necessary to see and analyze clearly before taking action to crack down on crime and arrest suspects to build a case to send to court.
3. All relevant units must be regularly inspected, commanders responsible for managing forces, ready to crack down on natural resource crimes, and all means and equipment must be available to ensure compliance with the above objectives.
4. The commanders of all units must pay attention and cooperate in the successful implementation of this plan.
