Chinese New Year is a traditional Chinese festival held at the beginning of the Chinese New Year, also known as Spring Festival in modern Chinese. On this occasion, Chinese tailors are often seen displaying Mars flowers on homes, companies and other businesses.
If you look at the flower sales around the roundabout of Wat Sampov Meas, traders are very busy selling flowers on Tuesday. People of Chinese descent also flocked to buy the flowers.
As for Ms. Chantha, who has been selling flowers for 7 years, she said that a Tuesday flower costs from 10 US dollars and up. She said that flowers with a lot of flowers can sell up to 50 US dollars, which is expensive to sell flowers.
According to Ms. Chantha, during the Chinese New Year, the sales of flowers are so high that this means that she has to set up a place to sell from 4 am, and the sale will continue until 9 pm or 10 nights to rest.
Ms. Chanthy, who also sells flowers nearby, said that the flowers she sold were brought from Pursat province, but the retailer said that because of the high cost, she took them back from Dey Huy market to resell. . The 12-year-old florist claims she has never lost a sale.
The Chinese people's belief in the flower of Mars dates back to ancient times. It is believed that Mars flowers are a kind of flower that marks the zodiac sign and the yin yang, so it is used to decorate the Chinese New Year.
On the occasion of Chinese New Year, in addition to flowers on Tuesday, people also buy oranges and flowers to decorate. Mr. Tieu Chhun Eang pointed out that oranges represent good fortune and fortune to Chinese families, while the veil represents gold and silver.
