CamControl finds fresh shrimp and squid containing chemicals for sale at a concert in Stung Treng province and confiscates and burns them
(Stung Treng): CamControl Stung Treng Branch collected 38 kilograms of squid and shrimp containing the chemical "Fox Malin" and burned them after confiscating them from some vendors who sold them at a concert in the provincial town. Stung Treng also continued to introduce food safety to traders and some people.
The above activities were held on the evening of February 2, 2019 under the leadership of Mr. Kim Pros, Branch Manager of CamControl Stung Treng, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce and local authorities.
Mr. Kim Pros said that this is a message to warn people to be careful with food. As for traders, if they continue to sell food containing such chemicals, the relevant officials will be fined according to the law.
He said that the confiscation of shrimp and squid containing folic acid, the authorities have improved the health of consumers and prevent tourists or people in the province or rural areas to eat these foods have a health impact, especially during Which traders bring to sell in this exhibition.
He confirmed that this is the fourth time that officials have used food to test for chemicals such as meatballs, fish, beef, shrimp, crab and squid that traders sell some food is good quality and some are nutritious. High levels of folate can affect consumers.
Mr. Chon Pheap, a trader selling all kinds of seafood and meatballs in this exhibition, applauded with the inspection activities and explanations from CamControl branch officials, because when there is inspection and understanding, it seems to increase awareness and improve care. Keep healthy.
The trader claims that in the past, he used to buy goods without inspection, some goods are out of date, difficult to use and difficult to sell. At the border, help look.
