(Battambang): The water source in Stung Mong and in Bassac Reservoir, which is an important water source and used to serve crops and use in daily life, has almost dried up and can sustain use for about another week. Only in Mo Russey district, Battambang province.
In response to this challenge, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, assigned a team led by Secretary of State Chan Yutha to prepare the infrastructure to bring water from other locations to supply Mo Russey district, with water from Rattanak Mondul district. Distance of more than 100 kilometers.
Mr. Chan Yutha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, who is leading the team, confirmed to Fresh News on the night of February 2, 2019 that for Battambang province, the district facing water shortage has three districts: Rukkiri, Maung Russey and Koas Kralor districts, but Koas Kralor district has already been resolved.
He also claimed that Maung Russey district may face a challenge within the next week, but the Ministry has also examined this issue in advance and has already prepared for a step-by-step intervention. Currently, the team has been signing and restoring only about 4 more canals.
The senior official of the Ministry of Water Resources added that the water brought to help Maung Russey district now comes from a multi-purpose dam in Rattanak Mondul district, which is dumped into Stung Sangke and reaches Kanghat Dam. More than 40 kilometers just arrived in the town of Maung Russey district.
Mr. Chan Yutha stated that the total distance from the water source to the place of use is more than 100 kilometers, but the team is determined to do the best work so that people can have enough water. As usual, back.
