Minister Veng Sakhon inspects Praman artificial cattle breeding farm in Traing district, Takeo province, which earns more than 10,000 USD per year!
(Takeo): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on the afternoon of February 2, 2019, after inspecting the dry season rice collection in Angkor Borey district, the Minister and his colleagues continued to inspect the breeding of cows. Artificial Praman species in Kampong Chrey village, Smaong commune, Traing district.
Speaking to the Minister of Agriculture in a happy mood, Mr. Sem Sangvat confirmed that after retiring as a civil servant, he started raising cows three years ago.
Currently, his family has a prosperous life, his children have a bachelor's degree, a job, and a decent income due to the income from raising 23 cows. He added that an adult cow can sell for more than $ 3,000 on average per year and can earn between $ 10,000 and $ 15,000 combined with rice.
At the same time, the Minister praised Mr. Sangwat's efforts to raise cattle as a good source of income to change the family life. This high income makes the family a better life, this happy family is a good result of the development of agriculture.
Minister Veng Sakhon instructed the Office of Animal Production and Animal Health to make more efforts on cattle breeding and to change the production system from family to semi-industrial in order to improve the quality of production, ensure the quality of hygiene and Security.
In particular, the General Department of Animal Production and Animal Health must organize a competition for outstanding farmers who have good animal husbandry and creativity by providing certificates or incentives to promote animal production to grow, ensure the supply of local markets and Lead to reduce imports. Currently, more than 1,000 cows have been artificially bred in Takeo province.
During the visit, the Minister instructed the Office of Animal Health and Animal Production to provide him with new techniques aimed at improving productivity, quality, hygiene and the environment to ensure the health of consumers and neighbors.
