Former JICA Cambodia Interns Association holds its annual meeting to share information on the association's achievements so far
(Phnom Penh): The Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia on February 1, 2019 held its annual meeting to share information on the achievements of the Association in the past. Hundreds of association members also attended.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Ieng Onny, President of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia, said that the Jaika Cambodian Ex-Servicemen Association always organizes its annual meeting every year for the purpose of Share information among all members as well as the general public about the results achieved by the association in the past year.
Dr. Ieng Ounny added that the activities of the Association of Ex-Trainees JICA Cambodia is also to collect ideas and input from all members to be able to improve and determine the upcoming annual action plan. Effectively respond to the aspirations of the association members as well as be able to respond to the actual situation of the association and of Cambodia.
At the same time, Mr. San Vathana, Undersecretary of State and Representative of Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports expressed his strong hope that all members of the Board of Directors of the Association will continue to cooperate with each other and further strengthen the network. Close friendships between all association members and continue to enhance the role and activities of the association more effectively and fruitfully.
Mr. San Vathana added that the association will continue to play its important role in strengthening the relationship and friendship between Japan and Cambodia, as well as other associations in the ASEAN region.
In addition, Mr. TANAKA Kotaro, Deputy Director General of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia, said that today's meeting was held to report on activities carried out in 2018 to exchange information. And feedback, review challenges, and gather input to guide action plans for next year.
It should be noted that the JICA Alumni Association of Cambodia was established by former interns who have participated in JICA training programs in Japan in various fields. JICA's training program is part of the Technical Cooperation Assistance Program, which is implemented under the technical cooperation between the Government of Japan. Cambodia, Myanmar discuss establishing direct flights to increase tourists
(Phnom Penh): At the invitation of Mr. Char Tin, Minister of International Cooperation of the Republic of the Union of Myanmar, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, led a delegation to co-chair the Joint Commission Meeting. The second Cambodia-Myanmar Bilateral Cooperation (JCBC) was held from January 31 to February 1, 2019 in Nay Pyi Taw, Myanmar.
During the meeting, Cambodia and Myanmar discussed the establishment of direct flights between the two countries to increase the number of tourists. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on February 2, 2019.
"In order to strengthen tourism cooperation, Cambodia and Myanmar have agreed to promote the" Angkor-Bagan or two ancient cities of the same destination "campaign, according to the press release. The two sides also discussed the possibility of establishing direct flights connecting Siem Reap and Bagan to increase the number of tourists visiting the two countries, as well as strengthen people-to-people contacts.
Regarding cooperation in the field of education, the Meeting agreed to expedite the implementation of the Agreement on Cooperation in the Field of Education 2017-2021 to build youth capacity and self-development. In the field of religious cooperation, the two sides also agreed to consider signing a memorandum of understanding on cooperation between the two Buddhist countries.
Noting the increase in bilateral trade volume in 2018, the two sides agreed to discuss the possibility of establishing a new bilateral agreement on economic cooperation and speeding up negotiations on an agreement on avoidance, according to the statement. Double taxation and prevention of tax evasion related to income tax as well. Ministry of Foreign Affairs Releases the Results of the Second Joint Commission Meeting on Cambodia-Myanmar Bilateral Cooperation
