Minister of Agriculture inspects dry season rice harvest of farmers in Takeo province and tells farmers that after the Chinese-Vietnamese New Year, rice prices may recover
(Takeo): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, together with his colleagues, this morning, February 2, 2019, inspected the cultivation and harvesting of dry rice in Phnom Da village, Kork Thlok commune, Angkor Borey district. .
According to the report of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Takeo Province, there are more than 100,000 hectares of dry season rice fields in the province, of which Angkor Borei district has 1,900,000 hectares, with an average yield of 7 to 7.50. Tons per hectare Today, rice costs 720 riel per kilogram.
The Minister also stated that the fall in rice prices was due to the Sino-Vietnamese New Year, when Vietnamese traders did not collect rice together with our farmers, lacking warehouses, drying kilns and the time required to collect. The results provided an opportunity for brokers to lower the price of rice. However, the current decline in rice prices has not yet reached a level where there is a loss of profit, just that the income is less compared to 2018.
