Svay Rieng Mayor Inspects Fire Testing System at Veal Yon Market
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Nop Chamroeun, Governor of Svay Rieng City, on the afternoon of February 1, 2019, inspected the fire protection system at Veal Yont Market to prepare for the eventual fire during the dry season, with the participation of the organizing team. Municipal Order, Municipal Police Inspector, Municipal Gendarmerie Commander, President of Municipal Water Supply Authority and Svay Rieng Sangkat Council.
The mayor advised all vendors to be careful of lighting candles and incense on Chinese New Year and to take care of the fire protection system together.
It should be noted that the fire protection water system at Veal Yon Market was initiated by Mr. Dy Vichea and Ms. Hun Mana, which was organized on July 17, 2015 by the Provincial Water Supply Authority as a contractor. Krong Pali ceremony was presided over by Mr. Dy Vichea and Mr. Men Vibol, Provincial Governor.
Veal Yun Market Vendors expressed their deep gratitude to Dy Vichea and Mrs. Men Vibol and all the provincial leaders who spent their own money to build a fire protection system at Veal Yun Market for traders and residents to use their time. Fires eventually occur free of charge. Vendors consider this noble act invaluable to the care of the management.
Senior CPP official visits 2 Thnou commune, Kratie province, calls on people to use water properly as the drought lasts
(Kratie): The National Assistance Team for 2 Thnou Commune, Snoul District, Kratie Province, led by Mr. Yang Moniroth and Mr. Meas Pich, on February 1, 2019, met with the Chairman of District Council, Commune Chief and Village Chief. Receiving requests from people in the villages to repair damaged pump wells and dig new wells.
Mr. Yang Moniroth said that in the afternoon of the same day, the national team from 2 Thnou commune, Snuol district, Kratie province, inspected the location of the pump well. In fact, the working group promised to make a repair project in the near future in response to the Royal Government's circular on the upcoming drought and solve it in time so that local people do not run out of water.
In addition, the team advised all people to save water to use in the future, while the drought may be prolonged.
The Royal Government has called on the authorities and the people to take measures to conserve water for use. This is according to the circular on water conservation measures against drought, released on January 17, 2019.
Through this circular, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has set out three important measures to deal with this problem.
Ministry of Tourism selects trainees to attend tour guide training courses in response to current and future tourism growth
(Siem Reap): The Ministry of Tourism has authorized Build Bright University, Siem Reap Branch to hold the entrance exam for the 6th generation national and regional tour guide training course in Siem Reap and the 27th generation with 771 candidates.
Mr. Pak Sakhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, Chairman of the Joint Commission in charge of Training Tour Guides, attended the selection and opening ceremony.
The exam was held on February 1, 2019 at Build Bright University, Siem Reap Branch for 12 specialized languages: Chinese, Japanese, Korean, Thai, Vietnamese, English, French, Italian, Spanish, German, Italian and Malaysian.
Candidates who pass the written exam now will be allowed to take the oral exam in the next specialized language, and candidates who pass both exams will be required to attend a four-month training course at Build Bright University and a two-year internship. Months by tour company.
Successful graduates will receive a Certificate of Study to apply for a national and regional tour guide license in Siem Reap and the surrounding area.
At the invitation of the Ministry of Tourism, the written examination was attended by the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU), representatives of the Cambodian Association of Travel Agents, representatives of the Association of Tour Guides and other stakeholders.
Skills training and job creation for young people is one of the strategic goals of the Ministry of Tourism to develop tourism in Cambodia sustainably. Tour guides have a role to play in enhancing national prestige and promoting Cambodia's tourism potential to the international stage. Therefore, tour guides must have extensive knowledge, advanced skills and good character.
Please be reminded that Cambodia currently has more than 5,000 tour guides. To meet the growth of more than 7 million tourists by 2020, Cambodia needs a total of about 10,000 tour guides. Currently, Cambodia's tourism sector is providing direct employment to about 620,000 people and is projected to create 1 million direct jobs by 2020, about 1.2 million by 2025 and 1.7 million by 2030.
Po Sen Chey District Police Arrest Couple for Distributing Drugs
(Phnom Penh): The Narcotics Police Force, in cooperation with the Security and Special Intervention Force of Po Sen Chey District Inspectorate, arrested two drug traffickers and a couple in a rented room, and found 11 packages of drugs and exhibits. Other as well.
The arrest of the suspect took place on the night of February 1, 2019 at Prey Boeung village, Sangkat Kantoek, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Sok Panha, Deputy Chief of Security Police, said that the operation was carried out under the direct command of Mr. Yim Saran, Inspector of Po Sen Chey District.
He added that the two suspects, along with exhibits, have been sent to the Drug Section of the Po Sen Chey District Police Inspectorate for further proceedings.
