Minister of Agriculture urges leaders of all units to increase the sense of responsibility in managing natural resources sustainably
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on the afternoon of February 1, 2019, presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the fisheries sector in 2018 and the direction of implementation in 2019. Office of the Ministry of Agriculture, with the participation of ministry leaders and about 400 members.
Mr. Eng Chea San, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Fisheries Administration, read out the summary report and evaluated the results achieved on the work of the fisheries sector in 2018 to the briefing ceremony, which focused on:
* Freshwater and saltwater aquaculture development work * Community development work * Flooded forest management and post-breeding of fish sanctuaries * Training, research and dissemination of techniques * Incubation of fish fry, fish product processing * Letter preparation Some other important legal standards and cooperation with development partners and the private sector, etc.
Minister Veng Sakhon thanked for the presence of the members who attended the ceremony and commended the hard work, dedication and high dedication of the leaders and civil servants. His duties were very good and in particular, he highly appreciated the new ideas, experiences and measures that the meeting achieved in the past two days.
He added that this effort is at the same time that the Royal Government has been carrying out in-depth reforms in the fisheries sector, which is a testament to the contribution to the promotion of the fisheries sector in Cambodia to grow with pride.
Separately, the report of the Fisheries Administration also shows the difficulties of the fisheries sector to professional officers in the performance of both legal and technical implementation, as well as the suppression of crime, but all of you have worked hard to overcome obstacles. To achieve great results in 2018 and hope that in 2019 will get even better results.
At the same time, Minister Veng Sakhon also recommended 15 points to the management as well as fisheries officials to strengthen the leadership, management, administration, technical and law enforcement to effectively lead to the development of sustainable fisheries.
