The report accuses Cambodia of "Cambodia's independence leading to the CPP retaining power and full coverage of the national legislature, paving the way for constitutional amendments that could lead to a Chinese military presence in the country."
The statement quoted the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as saying that although Cambodia is now able to amend its constitution, it will not change its constitution to allow foreign military bases or deployments. The Cambodian military goes abroad in addition to missions with the United Nations.
The Department of Defense also used sarcasm against the United States, saying that Cambodia always welcomes the US National Intelligence Service, which intends to find out the truth about any suspicions regarding foreign military bases on Cambodian territory and constitutional amendments on this issue. On the other hand, if no clear evidence or argument is found, let the United States immediately stop fabricating, inciting, painting and interfering in Cambodia's internal affairs.
Local vegetable growing is gaining momentum! Cambodia needs an additional 573 tons per day to produce 400 tons domestically and import 170 tons from Vietnam, Thailand and China!
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries confirmed that every day, Cambodia needs an additional 573 tons per day, of which Cambodian farmers can produce about 400 tons and the rest import 170 tons from Vietnam, Thailand and China.
"The driving force behind the increase in domestic vegetable production is due to the additional investment in the vegetable sector by the Royal Government of Cambodia, development partners and the private sector through development programs focused on strengthening "Production capacity, subsidies, use of modern technology and equipment, and market linkages between producers and buyers."
The Food Production Promotion Project focuses on the production of fragrant rice seeds and safe vegetable production by supporting financial resources, infrastructure, irrigation systems, water saving and technology to 2,000 professional vegetable farmers, including 40 large-scale farmers. Families in 8 target provinces.
He added that all farmers were organized into 138 groups to produce safe vegetables (an average of 15 families per group) to produce safe vegetables according to the Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) principles. Established a safe vegetable farming community.
As a result, by the end of 2018, the target farmers of the project to promote food production to 2,000 families produce 22,900 tons of vegetables or 62.7 tons per day. This is the additional emphasis of Dr. Ngin Chhay, Director General of the General Department of Agriculture.
Currently, the project to promote food production has been encouraging farmers to practice cultivation according to the principles of Good Agricultural Practices (GAP), a mechanism that can make our products safe and quality can compete with products from neighboring countries and markets. Districts, regions and international markets.
