Mr. Thong Khon and Mr. Yon Min chaired a meeting of the Working Group to Strengthen Tourism Management and Development in Preah Sihanouk Province
(Preah Sihanouk): After handing over the beach cleaning equipment to the coastal provincial administration on the afternoon of January 31, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, continued to chair the meeting. Help strengthen the management and development of tourism in Sihanoukville "to summarize the results and recommend further work.
Following the report of the expert, Minister Thong Khon introduced some recommendations, including:
* Continue to pay more attention to sanitation, garbage, environment, security and order in Sihanoukville, especially to prevent dirty water from flowing into the sea, to clean the beaches on a daily basis.
* Accelerate the preparation for registration, application for renewal of tourism business license online as soon as possible to facilitate the registration of traders, as well as the application and renewal of tourism licenses.
* Establish a beach management office on Koh Rong and more tourist information booths in Sihanoukville.
* Continue to work with the provincial authorities, the Provincial Department of Tourism must add more staff to work in the Department of Tourism of Sihanoukville.
* Provide public toilets in conjunction with adequate tourist information counters and pay attention to the cleanliness of public toilets on a regular basis.
After introducing the above work, Minister Thong Khon stated that all work activities must be prepared as a clear strategy or work plan and must be implemented effectively to contribute to the development of Sihanoukville to become A modern tourist destination of the future.
In addition, the Minister also urged the provincial authorities, relevant departments, units and the above 5 working groups to work hard in their respective departments properly to prepare for the 9th Sea Festival Round 3 in 2020. To be more solemn than previous years.
As a result of these concerns, the NCDD has handed over three beach cleaning machines worth a total of $ 417,900 to the administration of three coastal provinces, including Sihanoukville, with two. Kampot and Kep provinces received one unit together to serve the beach cleaning work.
The handover ceremony was held at Sihanoukville Provincial Hall on January 31, 2019, presided over by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Permanent Deputy Chairman of the NCC on behalf of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, in the presence of Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, Deputy Governor of Kampot and Kep Provinces, as well as some government officials.
On that occasion, Minister Thong Khon mentioned the progress of tourism, especially the development in Sihanoukville, which is attracting a large number of tourists to visit the province by land, rail, air and water. Therefore, the authorities also need to keep the beach clean.
Mr. Thong Khon said that under the guidance of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Chairman of the National Committee for Coastal Management and Development of Cambodia, this committee decided to provide three beach cleaning machines. The administration of these three coastal provinces.
The Minister introduced the mechanism for managing the use and maintenance of these machines, and he assigned each provincial Department of Tourism as a staff for each provincial level CEC to manage and use these machines effectively. Experts also need to have a high sense of responsibility in the maintenance of these machines.
He called on all relevant ministries and institutions to prevent dirty water from flowing into the sea, to control and clean the beach, but all beaches that belong to the public must be clean, any beach that is privately owned must cooperate to clean. Also clean to ensure that the sea and the beach must be clean.
In addition, local authorities, departments, units and law enforcement forces must cooperate to maintain effective security and order in the city. This is to ensure sustainable development in the future and to attract more tourists.
According to Minister Thong Khon, in the next three or four months, four temporary sewage pumping stations to prevent sewage from flowing into the sea in Sihanoukville will be built.
The Minister called on people, traders and tourists to join these beach cleaning machines to pay attention to garbage, hygiene and take into account all environmental issues. All that has been done is to prepare for the Sea Festival in 2020 together.
