Cambodia-Thailand Hospital Shares Experience in Cerebral Palsy
(Phnom Penh): The Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital and the Institute of Neurology of Thailand on January 31, 2019 opened a training course to share experiences from the treatment of "cerebrovascular accident".
The sharing of experiences took place during the ASEAN Neuroscience Training 2019 on the treatment of "cerebrovascular accident" to train participants to better understand the current state of the nervous system and treatment.
The collaboration between the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital and the Institute of Neurology of Thailand was attended by Prof. Ngy Meng, Director of the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital, and Dr. Suchai Tovanabut, former President of the Neurological Institute of Public Health.
On that occasion, Professor Ngy Meng said that the organization of this training will provide more experience and knowledge to our Cambodian doctors. In addition, this training will help strengthen and expand the relationship between Cambodian-Thai hospitals better. Another level.
Cambodia to host 5th Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics Festival in mid-February
Mr. Hang Chuon Narong, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, said in a press conference on the afternoon of January 31, 2019 that the festival will have about 5,000 participants and will take place from 21 to 23 February 2019. .
For this festival, the Minister also said that the Ministry will invite both private and public higher education institutions to participate in the festival to show the special work, invite professional teachers to participate to show his skills.
The minister stated that the festival, which will be held at the Olympic Stadium, is expected to have about 50,000 participants. In order to increase the number of students, the Ministry will use buses to transport students from school, as well as volunteer cards at schools.
"So we have volunteers from the Cambodian Stem team, as well as scientific researchers to facilitate the participants," he said. We see that young people are interested and the British Embassy will also provide buses to transport students in the provinces.
Science, technology, engineering and mathematics are widely recognized around the world as key sectors / factors and potential drivers of priority and importance for national development, especially in the fields of economy, industry, health, agriculture. Agro-industrial and commercial services for the development of prosperous, equitable, environmentally friendly and sustainable development.
The 5th festival aims to: Maintain the partnership between the Ministry of Education and relevant institutions to show the expansion of the scope of work. Demonstrate involvement as a ministry with development partners. Encourage all parties and institutions to pay attention to education, skills or careers in the field. Attract high school students to college or career card.
Activities to be presented and performed at the 2019 Festival include: Stem Exhibition, National Robotics Competition in Cambodia, Stem Project Demonstration, which gives participants the opportunity to experiment and practice on their own, launching a campaign "Stem for the future, I am Stem for Cambodia", Stem championship cards, technology quizzes and big concerts.
