Dr. Sok Touch: The Royal Academy will research the meaning of Apsara to show people all over the world to understand the meaning of Khmer culture
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the Royal Academy of Cambodia plans to study all the Apsara sculptures in the Angkor area in order to document them for the Cambodian people and people around the world. From the values of Khmer culture, while Apsara statues are an important part in the sculptures on the ancient Khmer temples that show the character of Khmer women.
Mr. Sok Touch said that the Royal Academy of Cambodia, in collaboration with the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, will start studying Apsara sculptures on the walls of Khmer ancient temples from the beginning of 2019. As a first step, researchers have started to study Apsara hairstyles and for the project to study Apsara hairstyles in the Angkor area, it is planned to spend more than 200 million riels, which is the national budget.
He added that in the future, after compiling the documents, the Royal Academy of Cambodia will request a budget from the Royal Government to carve the Apsara statues according to the default of each statue and put it in the museum, along with an explanation of Those images to make it easier for Cambodians and tourists to know the meaning of those apsaras.
Tbong Khmum Governor Holds First Meeting with Provincial Journalists
(Tbong Khmum): In order to increase the close cooperation and understanding between the provincial administration and the provincial information sector, on January 30, 2019, at the meeting hall of Tbong Khmum Provincial Hall, a press conference was held under the chairmanship of Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor Tbong Khmum Province.
Including the participation of the Deputy Governor, Deputy Director of Administration and Director of Provincial Office, leaders of departments around the province, the three types of armed forces, directors, deputy directors and officials of Tbong Khmum Provincial Information Department, radio, television and journalists in the province. More than 100 people organized by Tbong Khmum Provincial Information Department.
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan stated that the development in Tbong Khmum province is very much under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, but in the past the scope of dissemination was limited, so today organized a meeting with journalists in the province. This is to better understand each other and increase the coverage to all media outlets. Recently, there was also a meeting between Samdech Techo and about 5,000 journalists from all over the country.
On that occasion, Mr. Cheam Chansophoan stated that today is the first meeting and not the end, he will set up a meeting between journalists in the province with the provincial governor for at least three months or a semester. Once.
The Governor of Tbong Khmum Province emphasized that journalists are the fourth most important power, as the eyes, nose, eyes, eyes, ears, and ears can reflect the realities of development or any negative problems that have occurred in the entire provincial administration.
The provincial governor stated that he would accept all publications, both positive and negative, and he requested the media before covering any inactive issues that subordinates have a small gap or a handful of corrupt officials. In doing so, he also managed to align it in accordance with the five Samdech Techo approaches and the other two mottos, relying on the media to be the messenger to orient.
In addition, the provincial governor asked the media to help spread the word about the development in Tbong Khmum, as well as in our country, especially to respond to all provocative information affecting the head of the Royal Government and the peace and development of the country. The wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
He stated that a handful of people outside the society always pollute all the media as journalists must dare to write a response to attack that person or that newspaper that exaggerates the facts and incites the desire to divide Cambodia, this is a necessary factor. Most. He also distributed 50,000 Riels to each of them and ate together in a friendly manner.
According to Mr. Sar Sina, Director of the Tbong Khmum Provincial Information Department, the Provincial Information Department is the information officer for the provincial administration, the Ministry of Information and the Royal Government, and is a bridge to bring the Royal Government's policy widely disseminated to the people and Bring all the concerns of the people to the Royal Government to find a solution for them.
(Kampong Thom): The Royal Government, through the Land Allocation for Social Affairs and Economic Development Project Phase 2 (LASED II), held a lottery to hand over the numbers of residential and agricultural plots, which are the Royal Government's social land concessions to the landless poor. There are less than 700 families living in Doung commune, Prasat Balong district, Kampong Thom province.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province on January 31, 2019 at Wat Chey Rattanak Rainsy (called Wat Krabao).
Residents who participated in the lottery now received 30-by-40-meter residential plots and 2-hectare agricultural plots per family.
The social land concession in Doung commune, Prasat Balang district, Kampong Thom province covers an area of 1992.79 hectares, divided into residential and agricultural plots of land for administrative areas, community forest lands, community forest lands and streams, ponds for roads and canals. For building community infrastructure, etc.
At the same time, the project will also develop infrastructure, including roads, schools, health posts, community buildings, community markets, teachers' accommodation, wells, ponds, irrigation systems, etc. And provide farming techniques, animal husbandry, and processing of agricultural products.
In addition, the project will provide working capital of about $ 280 per family to expand farming and animal husbandry, and overall the Royal Government plans to spend about $ 4 million for the development of people on land concessions. This social work.
(Koh Kong): Thousands of families living in Koh Kong town and part of Mondul Seima district have been short of water as of January 31, 2019, since January 27, which Make the people there very difficult and have to save water stored in jars or basins in the past.
