It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia in the new mandate has established the Supreme Advisory Council, which is composed of 18 political parties participating in the 6th National Assembly election.
The Supreme Advisory Council is a mechanism for consulting and advising political parties to the Royal Government outside the parliamentary framework in order to improve work efficiency for the benefit of the people and the potential development of the society. The Supreme Advisory Council has the same mandate as the mandate of the Royal Government of the 6th legislature of the National Assembly.
(Phnom Penh): At the 32nd Meeting of the UPR Working Group of the UN Human Rights Council on the Third Round of the UPR Periodic Review Mechanism for Cambodia in Geneva, Switzerland on 30 January In 2019, the Cambodian Human Rights Delegation briefed the UN Human Rights Council on the progress and improvement of the human rights situation in Cambodia in all areas, especially the implementation of rights and freedoms in the past.
The Cambodian human rights delegation that attended the meeting was led by Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, including inter-ministerial delegations such as the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, the Ministry of Interior, and the Ministry of Justice. Ministry of Information, Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
At the Third Periodic Review Meeting, Cambodia also received a total of 202 recommendations from 73 UN member states, most of which focused on Commendation and welcome to the Government's efforts to improve the human rights situation in Cambodia in the past.
Taking the opportunity before the meeting, Mr. Keo Remy, Head of the Delegation, also allowed the UN Special Rapporteur on Human Rights in Cambodia, Ms. Rhona Smith, to pay a courtesy call on human rights work and visits. Her coming to Cambodia in the near future.
