Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: Right-hand drive vehicle registration is no longer allowed (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has confirmed that right-hand drive vehicle registration is no longer allowed. According to the Minister, closing the registration of this right-hand drive vehicle to reduce traffic accidents to a high level.
The confirmation of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol was made at the monthly meeting on the progress of the Ministry in January 2019 on January 30, 2019.
During the meeting, the Minister emphasized that "with the new administrative mechanism and technology, the registration of right-hand drive vehicles must be stopped completely from now on, unconditionally, in order to reduce traffic accidents to a minimum, in line with the high-level statement of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia today, tomorrow, to avoid traffic accidents.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on January 5, 2016, decided to allow people to use all right-hand drive vehicles to make license plates and pay taxes as required and allow them not to change. Steering wheel. At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also banned the import of right-hand drive vehicles.
After the permit was issued, many right-hand drive car owners brought their vehicles to register. Although it has been about 3 years now, it is still observed that right-hand drive vehicles have been registered, leading to suspicions that criminals continue to bring right-hand drive vehicles into Cambodia. .
