He said that the main stages of the election are as follows:
Voter registration for the election: According to the NEC calendar, from March 7 to 27, 2018. Voters for this council election are commune councilors in positions with a total of 11,572 members nationwide. Registration shall be carried out by listing the names in the communes and sending them by hierarchy to the NEC.
* Registration of political parties and lists of candidates: is only 5 days starting from March 7 to 11, 2019. Political parties that are legally registered as political parties at the Ministry of Interior have the right to register political parties and lists of candidates for this council election.
* Election Campaign Phase: From 17 to 24 May 2019, the duration of the election campaign was reduced from 8 days to 15 days in the first and second mandates.
Voting, vote counting and summary of election results.
Dissemination of election results.
