Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly gives eight important recommendations to the leadership of the Ministry of Rural Development for further implementation.
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly, Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on January 30, 2019, made eight important recommendations to the leadership of the Ministry of Rural Development. To take further action.
The recommendation of Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly was made on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the 2018 Annual Review Meeting and 2019 Work Orientation of the Ministry of Rural Development on the afternoon of January 30, 2019. At Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
The eight key recommendations of Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly include:
First, the Ministry of Rural Development must continue to work to promote capacity building and institutional development to further improve the provision of public services to be more efficient and effective in rural development work and to participate more deeply in the revised program. The various forms of the Royal Government in accordance with the priority direction of the Royal Government are people, water, roads and electricity.
Second, the Ministry of Rural Development must continue its efforts to build rural roads and improve rural roads into two-story paved roads and concrete roads that are resistant to climate change to promote economic, social and cultural development in rural areas. Improved.
Fourth, the Ministry of Rural Development must pay double attention to continue to change the living habits and understanding of the people in rural areas to be a country where people have a high awareness of health issues and clean living, especially Encourage villages, communes, districts and provinces to have better sanitation conditions and become villages, communes, districts, and provinces that stop more open defecation (ODF).
Seventh, the Ministry of Rural Development must continue to strengthen and maintain the role and operation of the Cambodia-Korea Rural Development Center in Chbar Morn City, Kampong Speu Province as a center to link the theory and practice of the people to improve their lives through professional agricultural work. Other occupations and small and medium enterprises.
