Nicolas Maduro was sworn in as president for a second term on January 10, 2019. But Guaido, the opposition parliamentary speaker, immediately announced his appointment as acting president, promising to seek true democracy and freedom for the Venezuelan people.
Below is a map and the names of the countries that support the two as the big countries are mobilizing more friendly countries to follow their respective political turns:
The countries that support Maduro include Russia, China, Turkey, Iran, Syria, Cuba, Bolivia and North Korea, while Mexico and Uruguay call for dialogue.
Guaido's supporters are the United States, Canada, Britain, Guatemala, Honduras, Costa Rica, Panama, Ecuador, Colombia, Peru, Chile, Argentina, Paraguay, Brazil, Australia, Kosovo and Albania.
European countries such as France, Spain, Germany, Portugal and the Netherlands have given Maduro eight days to hold re-elections or they will recognize Guaido as Venezuela's legitimate president.
Despite this, neither side seems to be in a position to surrender, with opposition leader Guaido preparing for a rally on Wednesday ahead of a travel ban and a Supreme Court freeze on bank accounts. Venezuela.
Maduro, meanwhile, gave an interview on Tuesday this week attacking the United States and its allies, and he agreed to sit down with the opposition leader, with international arbitration, but the re-election is the president. This picture does not agree.
(CHINA) - Since China introduced a new law on personal income tax in early January, it has made tax collection more fair and reasonable, a tax official in China has said.
China's central government began implementing the new law on Jan. 1, after the state raised the personal income tax rate from $ 519 to $ 741 a month, or $ 8,900. In one year. The tariff increase is expected to help tens of millions of people in China be taxed on their income.
The new law also introduces a number of specific tax cuts for the first time in China, offering six tax breaks: tuition fees, personal education fees, and serious medical expenses. Interest, mortgage, rent and care for the elderly.
The special tax cut is expected to reduce more than $ 45 billion by 2019 as a whole.
The company also sees an overall shift in taxed employees.
(China): Consumption in China is booming as the Chinese New Year approaches.
A variety of exhibitions for the Chinese New Year will be held throughout China, and it will attract many shoppers who are preparing to celebrate the 15-day festival, which will start from February 5 onwards.
With a history of about 300 years, an exhibition in Portli, eastern Shandong Province, attracts more than 100,000 daily visitors. "These holiday decorations reflect the progress of the Chinese people's way of life," said Chou Sanfen, a paper seller who brings glory.
