Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Tells All Local Officials to Collect Specific Rice Data from Farmers to Help Solve Falling Rice Prices
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, said that the problem of falling rice prices is a major issue while the provincial authorities and district governors are already working on this, but at the same time, the commune chief, local officials have to go down. Connect with farmers to collect accurate data on rice yields, easy to find private companies to help buy rice yields to solve problems for people in a timely manner.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said this on the morning of January 30, 2019, when he announced the inauguration of Ms. Pang Dany as Deputy Governor of Kampong Cham at the Kampong Cham Provincial Hall under the chairmanship of Mr. Leng Vy, Secretary of State of the Ministry. Interior.
The governor of Kampong Cham province said that he had recently contacted a private company to help buy rice from farmers in Prey Chhor district after farmers complained that rice production was low and it was difficult to find a market. That is the problem when we find a partner to buy rice and there is no specific data to provide information to the company.
"This is where we get in the habit of collecting specific data and easily providing information to partners who have to buy rice from our farmers," he added. The provincial governor hopes that all district and municipal governors will take the data to verify and participate in monitoring exactly where you harvest and there are no buyers.
