(Phnom Penh): In the whole period of 2018, the Ministry of Rural Development has built more than 50,000 toilets for people to use throughout the country. This is according to the report summarizing the work results in 2018 and the work direction in 2019 of the Ministry of Rural Development.
This report was presented at the meeting to review the results of 2018 and work direction 2019 under the chairmanship of Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, this morning, January 30, 2019, which was held at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
According to the report, in 2018, the Ministry decided to build 1,626 pump wells of all kinds, repair 2,768 pump wells, build and rehabilitate 374 community ponds, build 1,052 rainwater catchment tanks. Constructed 43 piped water distribution systems.
The Ministry of Rural Development added that in 2018, the Ministry, together with development partners, in cooperation with the Ministry, built new rural roads paved with red gravel, a total length of 390.46 km, double-paved roads, a total of 1.65.6 km and concrete roads. 6.74 km long, 31 concrete bridges with a length of 1,516 meters, a total of 707 artistic structures (box and round drains).
"After the disaster of the Mekong River flood and rain, the Ministry has immediately rehabilitated 267.95 km of roads, 26 round canals, 1 box drainage and 1 bridge," the report said. .
Collect data on 302 rural roads, equivalent to 703 kilometers, and update 316 roads with a length of 2,400.35 kilometers. The ministry has also planted 33,850 trees on the roads to increase resilience to climate change.
In addition to the construction of rural roads, the Ministry of Rural Development has also built other infrastructure to help improve the livelihoods of rural people, such as: construction of water wells, ponds, water filters, reservoirs, construction of water distribution systems, toilets, washrooms. Clean hands, etc.
