(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kouch Mengly said that due to the political stability, the higher economic growth of Cambodia and to meet the market demand, as well as many requests from parents, guardians and students from all walks of life about quality, discipline and service. Strive to expand and establish more private schools to participate in national development with the Royal Government.
He said that all these factors have made his private education sector, which was established in 2005, more and more famous both domestically and abroad, initially with only four students until now. The number of students has increased to more than 1,100.
Mr. Kouch Mengly, Founder, Chairman and CEO of Mengly J. Kouch Education Co., Ltd., stated this at a press conference on the expansion of the new branch of the AII Language Center and the American Intercontinental School in Choam Chao this morning. January 30, 2019.
"Due to the high demand from parents and the perception that our country is now stable, the economy in various areas is growing, there is development, both in terms of population and national economy," he said. "Chom Chao is a place that is no different from other places, it is an area full of potential and a strategic area that I have thought of and seen."
"We have a clear vision and mission to expand the branch," he said. Chom Chao is one of our strategic locations besides Mao Tse Tung Branch, Toul Kork Branch and Chak Angre Branch. "In that area and around Chom Chao, there is a lot of development, which makes the population grow and many big buildings are booming."
According to Kouch Mengly, the AII Language Center and the American Intercontinental School currently have three locations: head office along Mao Tse Toung Boulevard, Tuol Kork Branch on Street 289, and Chak Angre Branch on National Road 2. He also plans to expand new branches in Phsar Thmey, Toul Sangke, Sen Sok, Chbar Ampov, Chroy Changva, Teuk Thla, Phnom Penh Thmey, Tep Phorn, Prek Phnov.
Please be informed that the AII Language Center and the American Intercontinental School have received a number of international awards and accolades, including the International Recognition Award for Quality, Excellence, Social Participation (CSR), and National Leadership. Many countries such as Singapore, France, the United Arab Emirates, Switzerland, the United States, the United Kingdom, Brazil, Hong Kong and Brunei.
Kampot will have beautiful beaches in the coming months, planned to spend nearly 2 billion dollars
(Kampot): A new sand beach, an artificial beach located on the seashore in Kep Thmey village, Boeung Touk commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province, was started to be built according to the project of the Royal Government of Cambodia, while Kampot province, which previously had only a beach But no beach like other coastal provinces. This is the proud confirmation of more senior officials of Kampot Provincial Hall on January 30, 2019.
Kampot Provincial Administration Under the mandate of Governor Chiao Tai has initiated a beach in Kampot province to have a beach to attract more national and international tourists to visit for the national economic growth. In particular, the provincial administration will host the Sea Festival, which will take place in December 2019, through the decision of the provincial level as well as the relevant ministries in mid-2018.
During the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of Kampot International Tourism Port on August 8, 2018, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, urged the Kampot Provincial Administration to build a new artificial beach in Boeung Touk commune. Ready before the Sea Festival in December 2019 to host the reception.
Ms. Mu Sokhom, Boeung Touk Commune Chief, a representative of the people, said this morning, January 30, 2019, that her people, together with the community fishermen and fishermen support organizations, fully supported and expressed their happiness when See the development of this beach area, which has been developing for the past two months and is continuing to follow the plan of the Kampot Provincial Administration as well as the Royal Government.
The commune chief said that the people and fishermen living in Boeung Touk commune, Teuk Chhou district were very happy to see that the beach was opened for tourists to visit before the day of Kampot. Host the Sea Festival at the end of 2019.
They understand that this beach is important not only to attract tourists but also to support their livelihood and daily business better, especially to provide employment opportunities for the villagers.
Kong Samnang, Coastal Development Project Manager, said that Kampot is a seaside tourist province in southwestern Cambodia that is popular due to its natural beauty. The province has 17 major tourist attractions that can attract up to two million visitors in 2018.
However, this coastal province does not yet have a beach for bathing. Only in early 2019, with the policy from the Royal Government and the Kampot Provincial Administration, with the support of the Ministry of Tourism, he was assigned to prepare the land. And sand to develop a recreational beach area of about 200 hectares, with a budget of nearly $ 2 billion.
As a matter of principle, this coastal provincial administration will have to update before the Sea Festival, although it is not yet 100% complete, it will have to make a beach for tourists to visit. According to the plan, the coastal area will have high-rise buildings, a five-star hotel, a hospital, a school, a port, and a seafood market for the villagers.
