Phnom Penh Military Police said that on the morning of January 30, 2019, they arrested two veteran thieves, At Ratha and Sok Vanna, and filed a case to be sent to court, where the two thieves were charged. Theft is aggravated and unrelenting.
Phnom Penh Military confirmed that on January 26, 2019 at 07:30 pm, there was a case of burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary, burglary. Point # 28, Street D01, Bayap Village, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
After receiving the victims' complaints, the Sen Sok District Gendarmerie, together with the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie Criminal Office, the Chamkar Mon District Gendarmerie and the Meanchey District Gendarmerie, conducted a series of investigations until the target was identified and arrested. Two suspects, At Ratha and Poun Sokkun, also confiscated a Rav4 car, but the suspects refused to confess and cooperate with the military police.
Phnom Penh Military Police said that due to professional measures, at 2:35 AM on January 28, 2019, Phnom Penh Military Police searched until it reached the target and found another Luxis 570 car that the suspect took Hidden in a house with no number on Street 48BT, Kbal Tumnup 1 Village, Sangkat Stung Meanchey 2, Khan Meanchey, returned to the victim.
In early 2019, Art Ratha was arrested by the Phnom Penh Military Police and sent to prison for the third time. Four months ago, he has now escaped. Each time the military police arrested him, At Ratha used different names, including At Ratha or Kong Mean or Rom Ratha, also known as Mean or Poy.
