Chhim Pov Sokandy becomes the first female Director General of the General Department of Radio National of Cambodia in 40 years
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Chhim Pov Sokandy has become the first female Director General of the General Department of Radio National of Cambodia in 40 years. Ms. Chhim Pov Sokandy has been appointed by the Royal Government as the new Director General of the General Department of Radio National of Cambodia after Mr. Tun Sarath was appointed as the new Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information.
On the morning of January 30, 2019, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, officially announced the appointment of Ms. Chhim Pov Sokandy as the Director General of the General Department of Radio National of Cambodia of the Ministry of Information, following His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni. Of Cambodia issued a Royal Decree on August 24, 2018.
During the inauguration ceremony, Mr. Khieu Kanharith congratulated Ms. Chhim Pov Sukandy on her appointment as the Director General of the National Radio of Cambodia.
He stated that in the past, Ms. Chhim Pov Sokandy has played an active role in serving the National Radio of Cambodia to achieve many great achievements for the motherland, especially to serve the needs of the listeners of the National Radio of Cambodia, such as news programs and Entertainment.
"Today I feel happy because we have replenished the two-fifths rate, which we always set in the leadership is to have women, and we have five CEOs, always have women, and at the same time is an effort to raise," he said. "The role of women in society as a whole and in our media is unique."
Ms. Chhim Pov Sokandy, who has been appointed Director General of the General Department of Radio National of Cambodia, is committed to fulfilling her role under the leadership of Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information and the Royal Government of Cambodia.
She will urge the officers and leaders of the General Department of the National Radio of Cambodia in all departments to have good internal cooperation and solidarity to jointly develop the General Department of the National Radio of Cambodia to grow and compete with the rich modern media. Is happening with private radio.
"I clearly understand that getting a new role as the leader of an institution is a great honor, but leading the organization to success is even more important," she said.
It should be noted that Ms. Chhim Pov Sokandy first joined the People's Newspaper and transferred to the General Department of Radio National of Cambodia in the early 1990s. For almost 30 years, she has been actively working in the General Department of Radio National of Cambodia and has been given a series of roles by the management to become the Director General of the General Department of Radio National of Cambodia.
