Minister of Rural Development confirms nine major achievements of the Ministry in 2018 (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, presided over this morning, January 30, 2019. The opening ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work results in 2018 and work direction in 2019 of the Ministry of Rural Development, held at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Dr. Ouk Rabun stated that in the context of the rapid economic growth valve, the Royal Government has decided to carry out deeper reforms to provide more sacred benefits to the people of Cambodia throughout the country. The Ministry of Rural Development, on behalf of the Royal Government, has played an important role in achieving many major achievements, including:
1: Pay attention to expand rural water supply and sanitation activities to achieve the vision of rural water supply and sanitation by 2025. All rural people must have adequate water supply and sanitation and live in a clean environment. Sustainable.
2. Improving all types of rural road network to connect rural areas into a convenient, stable, safe, efficient and low-cost transportation system, especially in contributing to the family economy. Improvement.
3: Delegate functions to 20 district administrations in 4 target provinces to manage, manage and pilot for two years the three main activities of the Ministry of Rural Development, including: Regular maintenance of rural roads, repair and maintenance. Rural water supply system and improvement of rural sanitation services.
4: Increase family food security by mobilizing and training women on family food production, food storage and preservation, food processing to be nutritious and planting mixed crops for families.
5. Strengthen and expand micro-credit to rural people to be able to create small-scale family businesses to increase additional income to improve the family economy and reduce migration.
6. Promote gender equality at the national and sub-national levels through the dissemination and mainstreaming of women's rights to leaders and civil servants at all levels of the Ministry of Rural Development, and mainstreaming women's rights to rural communities through Promote the implementation of rural development programs, training and the creation of additional income opportunities for families through the creation of small businesses and hygiene education for health, etc.
7. Training of civil servants at the Ministry and Rural Development Departments of the Capital and Provinces on leadership, management and skills to be more capable.
8. Support the organization and capacity building of the Village Development Committee (CDC) as a local development structure to help guide and coordinate sustainable rural development programs.
9. Strengthen and expand good cooperation with relevant institutions at all levels with development partners, NGOs and the private sector to increase the efficiency of the implementation of rural development programs and poverty reduction to be more accurate and smooth.
The Minister further stated that in order to contribute to the successful implementation of the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 for the 6th Legislature of the National Assembly, the Ministry of Rural Development has been achieving its strategic direction, especially for the 2019 work direction. Focused on a number of priority strategies, including:
1. Institutional strengthening, capacity building and human resource development. 2: Building, building and renovating physical infrastructure, transportation and public services. 3. Promoting health, education and living conditions. Entrepreneurship and economic activity. Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Inaugurates School Building and Achievements at the National Police Academy of Cambodia
(Kandal): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, this morning, January 30, 2019, inaugurated the 5-storey Kampuchea school building and achievements at the National Police Academy of Cambodia.
Speaking on this occasion, General Dr. Seng Phally, President of the National Police Academy of Cambodia, spoke about the major achievements achieved on its 13 hectares of land, which are now inaugurated, including:
First: A dormitory for students, trainees and students with a height of 5 floors equal to 50 rooms.
Second: The accommodation building for a National Police teacher has 3 floors, equal to 30 rooms.
Third, the live ammunition training ground is a necessary place for the Armed Forces Training Unit to conduct live ammunition training for long arms and short arms to be proficient and shoot directly at the target during the operation to suppress crimes.
Fourth, the training course to overcome obstacles is another necessary place for training forces to be patient, able to withstand difficult situations and overcome all obstacles to achieve the goal of successful operation.
Fifth, the swimming pool was built for the purpose of training the swimming force to be proficient and in accordance with the technical standards to ensure the efficiency of work such as waterway operations, liberation when the boat sinks. Rescue drowning people, flood victims, search for victims in the water and so on.
Sixth: Martial Arts Building is another important training place for the forces that need to know martial arts for self-defense, arrest of criminals and fight with criminals in accordance with the technical specifications, as well as help strengthen the fitness Health and increase agility to the forces as well.
Seventh, for the executive study field was built, the practice of walking, the implementation of exercises, how to meet the queue, the organization of the stage, the suppression of crime and rescue. The gardens, streets, lights and plants also help to enhance the aesthetics of the academy.
(Phnom Penh): This morning, January 30, 2019, the Ministry of Rural Development held a meeting to review the work results of 2018 and work direction in 2019 under the chairmanship of Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, held at Sokha Hotel. Phnom Penh.
According to the report summarizing the work results of 2018 and the work direction of 2019 of the Ministry of Rural Development, the Ministry has set out a long-term strategic framework for the next 5 years 2019-2023 to improve the quality and value of people's lives. Rural areas through four priority mechanisms, including:
First, institutional strengthening, capacity building and human resource development are important foundations for strengthening good governance and sustainable development.
The Ministry has set out policies on human resource development aimed at increasing the capacity of civil servants at both the national and provincial levels to contribute to the implementation of public administration reform programs, public financial management reforms, decentralization and deconcentration reforms. Others to be more efficient.
Second, increase the construction, construction and renovation of physical infrastructure, transportation and public services in all areas of rural areas, especially areas with high economic potential.
Third, the promotion of health, education and living conditions, clean drinking, clean villages, communes, clean living environment, safe villages and communes are part of helping to promote modern living conditions in rural areas.
Fourth, job creation, entrepreneurship and economic activities to participate in solving daily life problems, which are the most important factors that can not be lacking.
The Ministry will establish mobile basic vocational training centers everywhere in villages, communes, districts, and provinces by inspiring and inspiring rural people to actively participate in the movement, as well as providing incentives for low-interest loans as capital. New businesses and movements for people to support local products to encourage Cambodian products.
