(Phnom Penh): Addressing the Minister of Culture and Tourism of the People's Republic of China, Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong confirmed that the Cambodia-China Culture and Tourism Year 2019 will further enhance Cambodia-China cultural and tourism relations and cooperation. "And deepen in the future from now on."
The former Cambodian diplomat said: "The Cambodia-China Culture-Tourism Year 2019 will further deepen and deepen Cambodia-China cultural-tourism relations and cooperation in the future from now on." "
Cambodia hopes to receive about 3 million Chinese tourists by 2020 and to 5 million by 2025 and about 8 million by 2030. The increase in Chinese tourists visiting Cambodia from year to year is also due to the direct flights from China to Cambodia by 12 Chinese airlines, with 207 flights per week to Cambodia, a total of 1504 per year. There are also recent direct flights from Beijing to Phnom Penh.
This is according to the press release of the General Department of Taxation on the meeting to summarize the results of tax collection for December 2018 and the achievements of 5 years and the direction for implementation for 2019 of the General Department of Taxation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. Fresh News received on January 29, 2019.
For 2019, in order to ensure the effective implementation of tax revenue collection and to achieve the maximum plan, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, supported the General Department of Taxation to continue its mission. It will make recommendations on measures and directions to be implemented, including:
1: Continue to modernize the tax administration by studying and preparing strategic information technology strategies to establish the Big Data Center of the General Department of Taxation.
2. Prepare, update and study additional tax regulations to support the management of tax revenue collection.
3: Cooperate with the General Department of Policy of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and relevant institutions to continue to develop a revenue collection strategy for 2019-2023.
4: Strengthen the implementation of the mechanism of repayment and use of VAT credit online for the management of VAT of the General Department of Taxation.
5: Continue to strive to improve the management of tax debt collection. 6: Strengthen attention to organize audit procedures.
7. Continue to reform human resources by strengthening the evaluation management in the human resource management system. 8. Continue to update all property information in Phnom Penh and in areas that are subject to property taxes.
The accident happened when a Highlander traveling in the same direction on Route 592 oversteered and collided with a Lancer parked on the road after trying to dodge a motorcycle. After the incident, the owner of a Highlander with a Royal Cambodian license plate agreed to pay compensation to the Lancer to end the problem.
Although the two sides agreed to end extrajudicial killings, questions arose as to whether the Highlander, which was traveling in the opposite direction, collided with a Lancer parked on the road and reversed. In the other direction, which side is wrong and which side is right?
In the Road Traffic Law, as amended in 2015, Article 23 on stopping and parking on the road stipulates that all vehicles that stop or park must not cause any disturbance to other vehicles in traffic. .
This article also stipulates that in the city, all vehicles must stop or park in the direction in which they are traveling. Drivers must park or stop at the right lane in the middle of a two-lane road. For one-way lanes, drivers must park or stop right or left in the direction of traffic.
According to the provisions of this law, the parking of a Lancer is in violation of the law in two cases, the first case disrupts the traffic of other vehicles and the second case is reversing. According to the Sub-Decree on Transitional Penalties for Violations of the Law on Road Traffic, Article 6, the driver of a Land Cruiser shall be fined 25,000 Riels.
The traffic police official said that in the case of the above accident, the owner of the Highlander was not at fault and had to pay compensation to the Land Cruiser, not the Land Cruiser.
The traffic police officer added that in this incident, because the Highlander car with the Royal Cambodian license plate did not know the traffic law, the money had to be paid to the Land Cruiser party, which was illegal.
