(Phnom Penh): The Foreign Trade Bank of Cambodia (FTB) celebrated its 39th and 40th Anniversary Celebration on January 28, 2019 at Sofitel Phnom Penh Phokitra Hotel in Phnom Penh under the chairmanship of Mr. Chea Chanto. The Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia will be joined by shareholders, the Board of Directors, the management, the staff of the Bank, relevant institutions, business partners and customers who are national and international guests.
This 40th Anniversary Celebration was organized and held in the sense and purpose to commemorate and express gratitude to the founders, staff, bank officials, relevant institutions, business partners and all national and international customers who have always supported And believe in the Foreign Trade Bank of Cambodia (FTB) in the past.
As the first and leading commercial bank in Cambodia since 1979, the Foreign Trade Bank of Cambodia (FTB) has played an important role in promoting and developing the economic and social market by promoting and Help provide basic financial services to local customers, traders and merchants.
Based on a strong business foundation, many achievements, experience in the process of contributing to the development of the national market and economy for the past 39 years, and with the total assets of the bank, which has increased to more than 1 billion dollars. Of Cambodia (FTB) has set a clear long-term business direction under the vision to make the Foreign Trade Bank of Cambodia (FTB) become the most preferred commercial bank in Cambodia.
In line with the development direction of the Banking and Finance Sector of the National Bank of Cambodia and to achieve the long-term goals set, the Foreign Trade Bank of Cambodia (FTB) will continue to expand its operations and raise the standard of provisioning. New product services that are the right financial solution for customers and the market.
At the same time, the Foreign Trade Bank of Cambodia (FTB) will continue to actively participate in promoting the use of the riel and continue to play its important role in contributing to the development and promotion of the national economic market and supporting its partners. All districts to further develop in accordance with the trajectory and direction of the national economic development of the Royal Government.
