He also urged the commitment and connection with local people and the relationship between subordinates to increase friendliness and experimentation to find solutions to farmers' problems such as seeds, crops and fertilizers.
Separately, the Minister in charge of management in the unit, the Minister instructed the Director of the Department of Agriculture, who has just taken this position to work together better and to know how to look at the work behavior of their officials, on the other hand, if officials He did a good job, the director of the department has to help him, train him, encourage him, encourage him to become a leader in turn, that is better.
Dr. Ly Chheng led the management team, staff, professors, teachers and nearly 25,000 BELTEI students to visit the Victory Monument.
(Phnom Penh): For one month, Dr. Ly Chheng, General Director of BELTEI Group, led the management team, staff, professors, teachers and nearly 25,000 BELTEI students to visit the Victory Monument.
The leadership of BELTEI students by Dr. Ly Chheng was made for the students to learn more about the true history of Cambodia in the process of ending the civil war in Cambodia and the difficult search for peace through the introduction of Samdech Techo's win-win policy. Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
On the morning of January 29, 2019, Dr. Ly Chheng led the management team, staff, professors, teachers and nearly 1,500 BELTEI students to visit the Victory Political Monument, a historical monument of national unity, territorial unity and Complete peace in Cambodia.
According to Mr. Ly Chheng, on behalf of the management, staff, professors, teachers and students of BELTEI Group, and he himself expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense. Opportunity and allow the management and students of BELTEI International School and University to visit the Win-Win Political Monument according to the daily visit schedule for one month.
Please be informed that the construction of Win-Win Monument started in February 2016 on an area of 8 hectares in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh. The Win-Win Political Monument was officially inaugurated on December 29, 2018 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
This win-win monument represents the heroism of Samdech Hun Sen, who dared to risk his life to travel to Vietnam to ask for Vietnamese forces to help overthrow the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and use all means to end the flames of war in Cambodia. On the other hand, the construction of this win-win monument is to commemorate the merits of Khmer ancestors of all eras who sacrificed their lives in the cause of the motherland.
Although the "Win-Win Politics" memorial has been inaugurated for a long time, so far, Cambodians and foreigners continue to visit this historic monument. Mr. Nuon Pharath asked teachers to be honest to ensure a better education
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nuon Pharath, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, asked teachers in both public and private schools to be honest about the various challenges to find solutions and promote education to get better results. This was stated at the opening ceremony of the meeting to evaluate the evaluation of education, youth and sports for the academic year 2017-2018 and the work direction for 2018-2019 at the Department of Education, Youth and Sports in Phnom Penh on January 29, 2019.
The Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh stated that the meeting was very important for each unit, especially the officials or members to exchange opinions, not like in the past that the organization of the meeting was just a picture and did not get any results. Therefore, he encouraged teachers to dare to raise the challenges encountered in the past year to discuss in the conference to find appropriate solutions and improve the quality of education.
Mr. Nuon Pharath said, "In fact, the conference is very important for the leadership of each unit is an opportunity to gather collective wisdom to improve, evaluate and set appropriate directions for implementation." So our conference, if we organize it in a picture without any direct discussion, it will not get good results. Therefore, I would like to ask all teachers to attend the conference to have a straightforward discussion to get good results and a common idea to implement together.
It should be noted that the meeting to review the evaluation of education, youth and sports for the academic year 2017-2018 and the work direction for 2018-2019 of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Phnom Penh will end on the evening of January 30, with more than 500 participants. People. But in the opening ceremony this morning, there were also many great achievements from Mr. Hem Sinareth, Director of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Phnom Penh.
(Phnom Penh): A widow who is currently raising four children has asked the Supreme Court to give her justice in the case of property distribution with her ex-husband because of this case, Mr. Ouk Savuth, Attorney General of the Court of Appeal issued an order. Allegedly charged with ex-husband in case of forgery of residence book documents.
However, the couple later disagreed with each other, filed for divorce and divided property into two equal parts at the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, during which the Phnom Penh Municipal Court ruled. The verdict divides the joint property of the two ex-spouses into two equal parts. But then Nget Samnang refused and appealed the verdict of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
It was then that Nget Samnang went to create another new residence book in the name of a family member, taking the name of a ghost named Meas Srey Vin as his wife instead of Iv Sre, but in reality so far there is no real identity of the person. Name Meas Srey Vin Whether dead or alive, everyone must have a very clear history of living, such as birth certificate and identity card, and if this person dies, they must also have a death certificate.
Starting from this issue, Iv Sreu filed a complaint with the Department of Criminal Investigation of the Ministry of Interior to open a search operation for Meas Srey Vin, who Nget Samnang registered as a family member in the residence book and submitted As evidence in the Court of Appeal's case, Iv Sre's lawyer copied it and told his client to sue the authorities for justice.
Based on the above story, the police force of the Criminal Department conducted an investigation and assumed that the residence book documents used by Nget Samnang as the reason for the name of Meas Srey Vin as his wife were a clue in the forgery of real documents, because there was no The presence of Meas Srey Vin came to clarify and appear to the authorities, and the authorities have built a case to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
Because Iv Sreu felt that the acquittal of Nget Samnang had been dropped by the judge, Iv Sreu relied on his lawyer to appeal Judge Than Leng's order, but the Court of Appeal upheld the court's acquittal order. The Phnom Penh Municipal Court is still valid. At that time, a woman named Iv Sreu also appealed the decision of the Court of Appeal to the Supreme Court.
The case was heard by the Supreme Court on January 23, 2019 and is scheduled to be made public on January 31, 2019. What Iv Sre's hope is is that she believes that the President of the Supreme Court, Dith Monty, will help bring him to justice as a widow with four sons and daughters, all of whom are members of the Youth Federation. Cambodia, chaired by Hun Many.
Iv Sree also thanked the Minister of Justice for giving him justice in this case through his letter to the Minister.
Ms. Iv Sreu hopes that the Supreme Court, the Supreme Court of Cambodia, will give her justice by referring the above case to the Court of Appeal for a retrial in accordance with the procedure.
