(Kampong Speu): To continue to promote the reading culture of students and promote human resources in Cambodia, a brand new green library building, built and equipped with library facilities, funded by PRASAC MFI in primary schools and Hun Sen Chamkar Dong Secondary School in Trapeang Andong Village, Chan Sen Commune, Oudong District, Kampong Speu Province has been officially inaugurated.
The inauguration ceremony was also attended by representatives of various departments in Kampong Speu, local authorities, teachers, students, youth, scouts, Red Cross youth, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and hundreds of people.
On that occasion, Mr. Sim Senacheat, CEO of PRASAC MFI, stated that PRASAC, a private institution, has initiated the construction of library buildings for students in many schools across the country.
He stated that PRASAC not only provides the library building, but also supports the equipment of resources, materials, documents and training of librarians to make the library run smoothly under the cooperation of the project from the Department of Curriculum Development of the Ministry of Education and Youth. And sports. He also thanked the Ministry and the Department of Education, Youth and Sports and local authorities for helping make this project a reality.
The Governor of Kampong Speu Province also said that due to the shadow of peace and social security, the students are very lucky to have a proper education, with a school, a library and a lot of books to work. Study, research and acquire knowledge. Therefore, you have to work hard to learn and develop yourself well through this library to become a bamboo successor.
In addition, he also advised students to build themselves with quality, morality, virtue, compassion, trust, know how to help each other, do not associate with sinful friends or negative people who interfere with their capacity building. And when you are successful, please share your success to the society as PRASAC does now.
Finally, he also thanked the teachers who worked hard to train all students to be the pillars of the country and future leaders.
General Ke Kim Yan Presides Over a Workshop on Drug Control in the Northeast and Implementation of a Drug-Free Village, Commune and Sangkat Plan
(Stung Treng): On January 29, 2019, General Ke Kim Yan, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, led a workshop on drug control in the northeast and the implementation of the "S" commune-free village plan.
The meeting was attended by representatives of ministries, institutions, deputy chairmen, members of the National Anti-Drug Authority, drug control committee, border provinces, districts, communes, sangkats, implementing the "white" drug-free village / commune / sangkat plan, and representatives of the parties. A total of 250 Thai, Vietnamese and Lao friends participated.
Mr. Mom Saroeun, Governor and Chairman of Stung Treng Provincial Drug Control Committee, said that this workshop was very important, showing the results of drug control work, especially the implementation of the village-commune / Sangkat "S" plan. No drugs to continue to strengthen and be more active in implementing anti-drug measures for the northeastern provinces of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, said that in Stung Treng and Preah Vihear provinces, where drug criminals often bring into Cambodia drugs, methamphetamine (Ice-Wy), ketamine, heroin and dried marijuana, which Cambodia operates. Cracked down in many cases.
On that occasion, General Ke Kim Yan thanked all the people and stakeholders of the Northeastern Provinces for their significant contribution in curbing the influx of illegal drugs from the border areas into the country. Helps solve many significant problems in the fight against drugs.
"Cambodia is not a country that produces drugs, but a country where drugs are trafficked from other countries in the region into Cambodia and continue to be exported to third countries," said General Ke Kim Yan.
