2018 APSARA Authority allows more than 2,000 Angkor families to renovate their houses and build small structures
(Siem Reap): According to the report in 2018, the working group of 5 secretariats of the APSARA Authority has continued to inspect, allow the renovation and improvement of 2,159 families in the World Heritage Site. Angkor.
Types of renovations, housing improvements and small-scale constructions that are permitted include roofing or wall replacement, pillar replacement, stair tread replacement, basement, brick flooring, construction of toilets, chicken coops, landfills, cowsheds, pig pens, etc. and other requirements. Others that are necessary in daily life.
Among the 2,159 families who received permits, Prasat Bakong district received 377 permits, Angkor Thom district received 288 permits, Puok district received 427 permits, and Siem Reap received permits. 906 families and Banteay Srei district received 161 families.
This permission was made after the community team inspected the back of the house and some other relevant documents to provide a technical basis for assessing whether they are the real people living in the Angkor area for a long time. Clear from local authorities, villages, communes and sangkats and there is a real need to improve living conditions.
It should be noted that APSARA Authority has established this community working group to facilitate the living of the people in the Angkor area, which covers an area of 401 square kilometers in 5 cities, 21 communes and 112 villages. On renovating old houses and constructing small structures, solving challenges, rescuing people in distress, and promoting heritage awareness to all people.
