The Reminder of the Head of the Cambodian Diplomatic Mission was made this morning, January 29, 2019, during the first consultation meeting with foreign NGOs operating in Cambodia. The consultation meeting was held to strengthen the cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and foreign non-governmental organizations and to ensure that all organizations fulfill their obligations in accordance with Cambodian law.
In his opening remarks, Minister Prak Sokhon outlined the objectives that led the Royal Government of Cambodia to draft a law on associations and non-governmental organizations in 2015.
The head of the Cambodian diplomatic corps said that some development partners and civil society organizations may have concerns about their right to freedom of expression at the grassroots level after the new law on civil society organizations was introduced in 2015.
While explaining the reasons and objectives of the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations, Mr. Prak Sokhon reminded that all non-governmental organizations operating in Cambodia must properly comply with Cambodian law. As well as avoiding some illegal acts.
However, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon also called on relevant ministries and institutions that are partners of foreign NGOs to continue to coordinate and facilitate the MoU with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs in its activities. They.
