During his visit to Cambodia, the Chinese Minister of Culture and Tourism visited some temples in the Angkor resort
(Siem Reap): The Minister of Culture and Tourism of the People's Republic of China, Mr. Lu Xukang, paid an official visit to Siem Reap Province from January 27-28, 2019.
On the morning of January 28, 2019, accompanied by Mr. Sum Mab, Director General of APSARA Authority and other relevant officials, the Minister and all the delegates visited some temples in the resort. Angkor, especially to the temples, which are part of a joint project between the APSARA Authority and the Academy for Chinese Cultural Heritage (CSA).
A delegation led by Mr. Lu Xukang visited Chao Say Tevta Temple, Takeo Temple, both of which were restored under the auspices of the Apsara Authority and the Chinese Academy for Cultural Heritage.
In addition to exploring the renovations of the above two temples, Mr. Losukang and his delegation also visited Bayon Temple, Ta Prohm Temple, Banteay Srei Temple and Phnom Bakheng Temple, which were the end of the visit in Siem Reap.
During the visit, Mr. Lashukang was very interested in the construction of Khmer ancient temples with fancy carvings, perfect design, suitable as a World Heritage Site.
Regarding the preservation and restoration of temples, he praised the cooperation between the two countries' professional institutions and said that China has a great honor to contribute to the restoration and preservation of temples at Angkor.
