Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: 366 km of National Road No. 5 will be renovated with a budget of $ 500 million (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that the project to upgrade the section The 366-kilometer National Road 5 from Prek Kdam to Poipet will be rehabilitated at a cost of approximately US $ 500 million.
He claimed that the cost of compensation to the people is the responsibility of the Ministry of Finance in some other budget, and the government also pays for taxes and the settlement of unexploded ordnance.
This was stated by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol on the afternoon of January 28, 2019, when he presided over the signing ceremony of the Agreement on the Rehabilitation of National Road No. 5 Central (Thla Mam - Battambang and Serey Sophorn). Poipet), a concessional loan project from the Government of Japan through the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia at the 5th floor of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
The project to upgrade the central section of National Road No. 5, which is currently signed for loan, has a total length of 146.04 km, from Thla Mam - Battambang with a length of 110.90 km and includes the last section of Serei Sophorn - Poipet has a length of 35.14 km.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that the 366-kilometer National Road 5 was planned to cost about $ 500 million, of which 62 kilometers were new roads between the cities, including the station. 6 places for weighing cars traveling on National Road 5 as well.
He added that at this time, three packages to be signed and other packages have already been completed from Battambang to Serei Sophoan has been opened by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, about 30 percent from Prek Kdam. Thla Mam has already opened the construction site, only 25 percent, which can take three to four years to complete, the Ministry of Public Works will complete in four years.
The Minister stressed that this road is very important as it is a major road for ASEAN, which connects China to Burma, passes through Thailand, enters Cambodia and continues to Vietnam, so goods passing through Cambodia must cross the national road. Number 5, it is very important to widen this road, it can help reduce traffic accidents, facilitate transportation, and it has brought many benefits to Cambodia.
