Acting Governor of Koh Kong Province Urges Provincial Agriculture Officials to Work Harder
(Koh Kong): Mr. Phay Thun Pham Keson, Acting Governor of Koh Kong Province, urged the Provincial Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Officers to train and disseminate agricultural techniques effectively in training and disseminating new agricultural techniques and disseminating relevant documents. Better agriculture.
Mr. Phay Thun Phkamkeson said this on January 28, 2019 in the program to summarize the results of the implementation of agriculture, forestry and fisheries.
Mr. Phay Thun Plam Keson said that all agricultural officials must be trained and disseminated agricultural techniques, and this work must be highly effective in training and disseminating new agricultural techniques.
At the same time, regulations related to the management of the agricultural sector must be disseminated, which will enable local farmers engaged in agriculture to gain knowledge of new techniques such as cultivation, care and animal husbandry. In particular, raising farmers' living standards through agricultural diversification and commercialization.
He added that the relevant departments should have the policy to establish agricultural communities, fishing communities and forestry communities, fisheries communities and the cooperation of relevant units and development partners to support all communities to run successfully and farmers have better knowledge to improve. Family life and agriculture are improving from year to year.
Announcing the appointment of the Director of Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Agriculture, Mr. Sim Tha Virak to replace Mr. Kim Savoeun who moved to work in Phnom Penh
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Sim Tha Virak has been announced as the new Director of the Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, replacing Mr. Kim Savoeun, who has been transferred to his new job in Phnom Penh.
The announcement ceremony was presided over by Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, and was attended by Mr. Khlot Phorn, Chairman of Kampong Cham Provincial Council and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham Province on the morning of January 28, 2019.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said that the agricultural sector absorbed about 60% of the local labor force and contributed more than 31% of domestic production, of which Kampong Cham is also considered as a province with agricultural potential. And contributed to the national economy, including: agriculture, agro-industry, modern industrial animal husbandry and animal products, etc.
According to the provincial governor, in the past, Kampong Cham province has gradually developed in all areas, in general and in particular, through the attention of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Kampong Cham province has strengthened its capacity and provided experience. Good for local farmers throughout the province and have done training and presentations that are admirable, especially in 2018.
On that occasion, Mr. Veng Sakhon also instructed Mr. Sim Tha Virak, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Cham Province, who has just taken office, to make more efforts related to the work of the agricultural sector, that is, to strive to help people. People on cultivation will have to work hard to find a market for them as well.
