The problem of falling rice prices! Minister of Agriculture orders professional officers to hold an emergency meeting with rice companies and traders to discuss solutions for farmers (Video Inside) (Kampong Cham): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on 28 January 2019. Order the officials of agriculture, forestry and fisheries to hold an urgent meeting by inviting the relevant departments, companies or traders to collect rice to study the price of rice.
This decision was made on the occasion of Mr. Veng Sakhon presiding over the inauguration ceremony of the Director of Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, which was held at Kampong Cham Provincial Hall this morning, January 28, 2019. .
On January 25, 2019, the Ministry of Agriculture issued a directive setting out measures to improve rice production and business after the European Commission decided to impose a tax on Cambodian rice.
According to the Ministry of Agriculture, in order to promote the rice business, especially the intervention to prevent the situation of falling rice prices, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries decided to set out some necessary guidelines for immediate implementation as follows:
1: The specialized unit under the Ministry must continue to research and release luxury fragrant rice varieties and pure fragrant rice seed production through community-level production and seed production groups to ensure sufficient seeds and reasonable prices to expand. Aromatic rice production. At the same time, the private sector is requested to invest in the production of high quality fragrant rice seeds in accordance with market standards and requirements.
3. Rice collectors must continue to liaise with the Rural Development Bank to obtain loans to collect rice from agricultural community farmers and must not justify EU market protection measures to lower the price of rice purchased from farmers. Rice exporters must check and ensure the quality of fragrant rice is pure, not mixed with other types of rice, which leads customers to lose faith in the quality of Cambodian fragrant rice.
