Third US city alliance with Phnom Penh aims to boost cultural ties, education, economic sector and friendship between the people of the two cities
This is the third city in the United States to form an alliance with Phnom Penh after Lowell and Cleveland have already signed up. January 30, 2019.
During a courtesy call and discussion with the Long Beach delegation, Phnom Penh Governor Mr. Khuong Sreng said that the two cities have now signed a Memorandum of Understanding on sisterhood between Long Beach, California. Of the United States and Phnom Penh of the Kingdom of Cambodia in order to enhance cultural and educational ties, as well as economic and friendship relations between the people of the two cities.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that Cambodia and the United States have established bilateral diplomatic relations since 1950.
He also wants to turn Long Beach into a cultural city, especially Khmer culture, which can tell the world about Khmer cultural traditions. Mr. Khuong Sreng and Dr. Robert Garcia signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on the six sister cities (Phnom Penh and Long Beach) on six issues related to closer cooperation between the two cities.
