Good news! Five deaf people from birth who underwent surgery at Preah Ang Duong Hospital can hear and speak well
(Phnom Penh): After a collaboration between Ang Duong Hospital and a team of doctors from Korea, 5 deaf patients using Austrian state-of-the-art machines were operated with 100% success last month. October 2018 As of January 27, 2019, these children can hear and speak quickly before the deadline.
Dr. Thong Meng Long, Deputy Director of Preah Ang Duong Hospital, said that Preah Ang Duong Hospital has the first machine and deaf surgery in Cambodia and we have already operated on five of our Cambodian children. "Since October 2018, we have been 100% successful, now they can listen and talk a lot."
He added that children with deafness can learn to speak faster than adults because children are easier to imitate, while adults with deafness take a little longer to practice their tongues.
She added that she would like to express her sincere condolences to the doctors and nurses of Ang Duong Hospital and their Korean partners who treated her son so that he could hear and speak like normal children.
At the same time, she also called on the people who have relatives with deafness to come to Ang Duong Hospital for surgery to hear and speak like a normal person in a short time and be 100% successful. Opportunity of hope for family and personal patients.
