Battambang Provincial Court issues arrest warrant for man involved in defrauding his uncle of $ 240,000
(Battambang): The specialized office of the Battambang Provincial Police in cooperation with the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police arrested a man involved in defrauding his uncle of $ 240,000 and some other jewelry in 2017.
The arrest was made on the orders of Battambang Provincial Court Investigating Judge Ly Sokha in response to a complaint filed by the victim in a $ 240,000 fraud case, along with some jewelry in July 2017. Into Battambang province.
Battambang provincial police officer told Fresh News on January 28, 2019 that the victim was Chang Kimny, an elderly and chronically ill person living in Kordathan village, Sangkat O'Ambel, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province, while the suspect was named Mich. The idea of living in Banteay Meanchey together is to be the nephew of the victim.
The victim's family also said that during July 2017, the accused and another partner planned to use fraudulent means to take money from the victim in stages.
* For the first time, for $ 150,000, in order to follow the superstition, to make a gold statue in Phnom Kulen and buy the soul of life from India to get rid of the plague quickly from many chronic diseases for many years. .
The second time, the victim was tempted by the victim with $ 90,000 and some other jewelry to be placed on the seat under the image to work as soon as possible. Finally, the suspect took the money and accessories. All the jewelry disappears at once.
After this happened, the victim filed a complaint to the court to arrest the scammer. After the arrest, the suspect was sent to the Battambang Provincial Court for legal action.
Royal Government of Cambodia meets for the first time with foreign NGOs to strengthen cooperation
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia will hold its first consultation with foreign NGOs working in Cambodia to sincerely exchange views and strengthen cooperation between the Royal Government and foreign NGOs.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia on January 28, 2019, the first consultation meeting between the Royal Government and foreign non-governmental organizations will be held on January 29, 2019 at Office of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, will preside over the opening ceremony. The Minister will make an opening speech focusing entirely on the presence and contribution of local foreign NGOs in the socio-economic development of Cambodia, as well as their rights and obligations under the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations.
According to the announcement, a total of 300 representatives of relevant ministries and institutions of Cambodia and representatives of foreign NGOs will participate in this first consultation forum.
