International Analysis: Why will Thailand be the beneficiary of the Sino-Japanese cooperation?
(Bangkok): Thailand will benefit greatly from building good relations between China and Japan in joint development to resolve the crisis caused by the stronger US trade policy. China and Japan have been under pressure to reduce their overwhelming trade ties with the United States, prompting the two countries to step up efforts to find common ground.
Notably, several agreements have focused on Thailand, including projects to promote smart city development in Chonburi province involving Japanese and Chinese companies' JFE engineering. Chonburi, along with Chaiyangsao and Rayong provinces, is a key area for Thailand's $ 45 billion Eastern Economic Corridor project for east coast development.
The project includes a high-speed rail network to connect Bangkok's two main airports, Don Mueang Airport and Suvarnabhumi Airport, with Pattaya Airport's Utapao Airport as part of a plan to develop the area into a commercial and investment hub.
Thailand has also passed a law that shows its willingness to attract more investment, providing tax breaks for investors in the economic corridor and allowing them to lease land for up to 99 years. Also.
Observers say the decisions of Beijing and Tokyo to invest in Thailand may reflect both countries' dissatisfaction with US President Donald Trump's uncertainty.
In particular, Yasuhiro Matsuda, a professor at the Institute of Advanced Studies in Asia at the University of Tokyo, said that cooperation in third countries could help the two countries build better relations and help Japan reduce risks. Which angered the big brother of the United States for increasing relations with China.
But even though Japan is actively cooperating with China for the time being, the idea of a natural race between the two countries has not changed. But more importantly, the third party is that Thailand will benefit greatly from building relations between the two countries in the meantime. Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Appointed Mr. Chum Bayon Vibol as Chairman of Russey Keo District Council to replace Mr. Van Saly who passed away
