(Kampong Thom): After leaving Siem Reap, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on the afternoon of January 27, 2019, continued his trip to Kampong Thom to inspect the dry rice harvesting activities of farmers in Koh Kram village. Bai, Kampong Kor Commune, Kampong Svay District, Kampong Thom Province.
According to the report of the Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Agriculture, there are more than 60,000 hectares of dryland rice in Kampong Thom province, and so far more than 4,000 hectares have been harvested, with an average yield of about 4 to 4 hectares. .5 tons per hectare. For today, feed rice costs 690 riel per kilogram, while fragrant rice farmers who have signed a contract with AMRU RICE buy at 1,150 riel per kilogram.
According to the farmers, in this area, farmers generally use IR51 and IR 54 varieties and fragrant rice varieties (Phkar Romduol and Sen Pidor). At the same time, they can grow dry rice twice a season due to the system The canal, built by the Cambodian Agricultural Value Chain Project, a grant from the Australian Government and the canal system of a private water supply company at $ 105 per hectare, is from sowing to harvest time.
