(Siem Reap): Mr. Lu Xukang, Minister of Culture and Tourism of the People's Republic of China, arrived in Siem Reap-Angkor this afternoon, January 27, 2019, during his five-day official visit to Cambodia from January 27-31, 2019.
Arrival at Siem Reap International Airport was welcomed by Mr. Hor Moniroth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, Siem Reap Provincial Authority, and other relevant leaders.
During his official visit, he will join the celebration of the first China-Cambodia Tourism and Culture Year on January 30, 2019. According to the plan for his visit to Siem Reap, he will visit Angkor Wat, Bayon Temple, Ta Prohm Temple, Takeo Temple, Chao Say Tevta Temple, Banteay Srei Temple and some other temples of Angkor resort area, then continue to visit the National Museum and plan to meet Siem Reap provincial leadership.
In the morning of January 29, the Minister will travel to Phnom Penh and in the afternoon he will meet with Minister of Tourism Thong Khon. On the morning of the 30th, he will meet with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the Peace Palace. He will then meet with the Minister of Culture and Fine Arts.
