Koki commune health center in Svay Rieng province, where the US dropped a lot of chemical bombs, was officially inaugurated, people can go for free treatment
(Svay Rieng): People all over Svay Rieng Province expressed their great joy and thanks to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for providing a brand new health center that is very beneficial for them to achieve their goals. In particular, this area was the victim of US chemical bombs during the war.
The inauguration ceremony was held on the morning of January 27, 2019 under the chairmanship of Mrs. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection in Koki Commune, Romeas Hek District, Svay Rieng Province. More than 1,000 people.
Mrs. Men Sam An sent greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit and sincerely commended Theranu Thera and all of you, ladies and gentlemen, local authorities at all levels and brothers and sisters. All the people who have always contributed their energy to the local development in the past until the village-commune has achieved many new achievements.
In fact, the building of Koki Thmey Sralang Health Center, which is a precious gift from both Samdech, has contributed significantly to the provision of free care and treatment services to the people, especially women and children. Not only to provide care and treatment in Koki commune, but also to provide medical services to the people in the communes around Romeas Hek district, which will contribute to better health care services in Svay Rieng. .
She said that the health center building, which has been jointly inaugurated now, is an initiative of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, although the number of people in Koki commune is not yet in proportion to the establishment of health centers. .
However, considering the well-being, especially the health problems of the victims of the chemical bombs dropped by the United States between 1970-1975, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit decided to donate the new Koki Health Center to Respond to practical needs.
Ms. Men Sam An added that this chemical has caused some unusual symptoms such as: big head, paralysis, paralysis, skin reactions and itching.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed the Ministry of Health to include the people in Koki commune, Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province, who suffered from US chemicals into the equity program, that is, receive free examination and treatment at public hospitals. Fees.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, in the sixth legislature of the National Assembly, remains committed to reducing poverty to the maximum and ensuring key indicators in the social sector, especially health, and to continue to implement policies to increase efficiency. And better public health services, gaining the trust of the people through more in-depth, strong and effective reforms.
