Washington: US President Donald Trump remains adamant that the border wall with Mexico will still be built, even if the US government closure ends without a drop in funding for his project. This was released by the BBC on Sunday, January 27, 2019.
"The agreement to reopen the government temporarily does not mean abandoning the border wall project ... but it is a matter of concern," Donald Trump said on Twitter. Put to millions of people who are affected by the government shutdown. National security is important, and what has happened in the border area in the past makes it clear that the border wall must be built. So we will build a border wall! ”
Donald Trump on Friday agreed to open the interim government for 21 days, while the $ 5.7 billion package to build a border wall with Mexico was not approved by the Democrat-controlled Congress. He also warned that a government shutdown or a security emergency would be declared if his request was still rejected.
