Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who is highly regarded by the Cambodian people and world leaders as a Cambodian ancestor and the mother of Cambodian humanitarianism, has been active in the humanitarian cause and the supreme symbol of Rescue of all victims in Cambodia.
Not only Cambodians, even people in countries around the world who suffer from natural disasters such as hurricanes, floods or earthquakes, etc., Samdech Kittipritthbandit has always contributed to save the nation to the victims. Those accidents, too.
The Cambodian Mother of Humanity has made every effort to manage and deal effectively with the humanitarian cause, mobilizing humanitarian aid to rescue the elderly, the homeless, the orphans, the widows, the HIV victims. By various disasters everywhere.
In fact, at the beginning of 2019, which is on January 23-24, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen and the accompanying delegation visited and distributed humanitarian gifts to the elderly, widows, orphans, the disabled and A total of 5,077 HIV-positive families, including 73 Cambodian-Muslim families in Pailin province.
On the morning of January 23, 2019, this humanitarian mission was held in O'Kantheangva village, Stung Trang commune, Sala Krao district for 1,251 vulnerable families. Stung Karch, Sala Krao district, reached 1,152 vulnerable families and on January 24, 2019, it was held in Otavao village, Pailin commune, Pailin city, where 2,674 vulnerable families.
On the occasion of visiting and providing humanitarian donations to 5,077 vulnerable families, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen expressed his deepest condolences and brought a royal message to visit and remember. Compassion from the Queen Mother of the Khmer Nation, the Honorary President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always cares about the well-being of his people at all times.
At the same time, Samdech Kittipritthbandit also gave some instructions to the people, including:
Parents and siblings should take good care of their health by drinking clean water and boiled water to avoid various diseases to reduce the rate of illness and death, including loss of family economy.
Participate in respecting traffic laws to reduce deaths and disabilities due to traffic accidents,
* Stay away from drugs, which are the cause of theft, domestic violence, murder, sometimes killing even one's own parents, which makes society hate and destroy their future and family.
* Please, all children and youth of the Cambodian Red Cross strive to learn to be good role models in school to help educate friends who commit mischief, such as drug abuse, to know how to help each other, especially to friends. Who studied well and lived in poverty
* Urge citizens not to engage in gambling that could seriously affect the family economy and create domestic violence
For people living with HIV, do not pass it on to others and their families, and for people living with HIV, go for regular check-ups and take antiretroviral drugs as prescribed by your doctor.
* For pregnant women, in order to avoid any danger to the mother and the unborn child, all pregnant women must know how to take care of their health and the baby by going to the hospital or health center for a pregnancy test. Regularly follow the instructions of your doctor
* Encourage people to work hard to grow other crops to help improve family life.
In addition, call on people to be very careful about fires this summer.
At the same time, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen also thanked all the compatriots who know how to love and help each other without prejudice and discrimination on the basis of race, color, caste, high and low. Live in unity under the roof of our Cambodian peace.
On that occasion, Samdech Kittipritthbandit also expressed his deep gratitude to the local and foreign philanthropists who donated food, materials and funds to the Cambodian Red Cross, especially on the occasion of May 8 and other opportunities to contribute. Relieve the plight of the most vulnerable and vulnerable Cambodians.
Uncle Chea Kosal, who is paralyzed in both legs, is one of the above vulnerable people, and he is very happy, especially the longing to see and meet his humanitarian mother for many years, our people It's really exciting here.
He continued, "I would like to express my deep gratitude to Samdech Kittipritthbandit and Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who is a wise leader for allowing my children to live in the cool shade, even though I am disabled, he does not discriminate and does not leave We left too.
