Understand the law: juvenile delinquency
(Phnom Penh): Every year, a worrying number of babies are abandoned by their parents or guardians at health centers, public places, or in some cases at landfills. Abandoned infants and children may be in danger of death, harm to health or may not have a good future, because after the abandonment of their parents or guardians, they will experience many things. Unexpected.
According to the Constitution, the supreme law of the Kingdom of Cambodia, parents have an obligation to take care of and educate their children to be good citizens. Therefore, abandoning a minor child under his or her guardianship is against the law.
Therefore, the actions of parents or guardians who abandon a minor under the age of 15, causing harm to the health or security of the minor, the parent or guardian is responsible before the law.
At the same time, a question was raised: "Is it considered a crime to adopt a minor child to another person?" Adoption of a minor child to another person is not a crime if the adoption of a minor is in accordance with the legal provisions of the 2007 Civil Code relating to the adoption provisions and does not affect the interests of the minor. Minors are defined in the above provisions of the 2009 Penal Code.
In short, the abandonment of minors is illegal and increases the society of homeless children who do not have a clear identity and can make their lives unstable and uneducated, so some criminals take the opportunity. Exploit the labor force and beat the minors.
