Japanese investors invest hundreds of millions of dollars in real estate in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): With confidence in the ongoing peace and political stability in Cambodia, a group of foreign investors, especially investors from Japan, have invested hundreds of millions of US dollars to invest in real estate. Japanese quality housing for Cambodians in Phnom Penh.
The Director General confirmed that today, Borey Arata Garden Residences handed over houses to customers with a total of 233 houses, including shops, hybrid villas and twin villas. Arata Garden Residence has completed about 100 projects in Asia, including Japan, Cambodia, Vietnam, Indonesia, Laos, Bangladesh, Myanmar and Malaysia, with a total value of $ 1.6 billion.
