Phnom Penh Municipal Court will continue questioning a man tomorrow regarding the theft of land for sale in Kampong Speu
(Phnom Penh): After much questioning, Mr. Plang Sophal, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on the evening of January 26, 2019, decided to send a suspect to the authorities to continue the proceedings tomorrow morning.
According to the authorities, the suspect named Poun Thean, 63 years old, resides in Thnal Bapek village, Svay Kravan commune, Chbar Morn city, Kampong Speu province.
The suspect was arrested by the Intervention Force of the Criminal Police Department of the Ministry of Interior on January 23, 2019 in connection with a case of stealing and selling land. According to the complaints of the victims, Leung Jing Chhay, a 56-year-old man, and Chhay Muy Fong, a 52-year-old woman, live in Phnom Penh.
After researching, they found out that Poun Thean had forged documents to sell their land to others, so they prepared a complaint to arrest the authorities.
