Minister of Agriculture recommends 6 important points to Siem Reap Provincial Department of Agriculture for further implementation
(Siem Reap): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, January 26, 2019, presided over the closing ceremony of the 2018 Annual Meeting and the 2019 implementation direction of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Fishing in Siem Reap.
On that occasion, the Minister welcomed the presence of members who attended the ceremony and thanked the local authorities, relevant departments around the province, the Armed Forces at all levels, which always support and provide good cooperation. With the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in the past to achieve great achievements.
Mr. Veng Sakhon said that, of course, this achievement has helped to improve the lives of local people, especially the joint production of food for tourism in the glorious province of Angkor and contribute to the implementation of the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4. Of the Royal Government of the 6th Legislature of the National Assembly "For the growth of employment, equity and efficiency in Cambodia."
The Minister stressed that the implementation of the past work is still lacking, smooth and slow on some tasks that require all of us to deal with in a timely and effective manner and need to learn from each other to gain experience. Both good and bad from the past and improve the orientation for implementation and get positive results both now and in the future.
In order to continue to implement the plan and implementation direction successfully, Minister Veng Sakhon has set out some basic points for the department to implement, including:
First, to continue to increase the productivity of agricultural production, diversification and trade in the agricultural sector by diverting from "prosperous" development to "intensive" development to increase yields and ensure quality. Food security and increase income to meet demand.
Third, to encourage and encourage the implementation of "contract agricultural production" system to improve the quality of competitive agricultural products, ensure public welfare, implement good agriculture intelligently and increase the provision of agricultural market information services more widely and timely. .
Fourth, to cooperate with the relevant departments, authorities at all levels to take measures to prevent and suppress the timely import of animals and meat of defective quality, forest crime, fisheries and illegal agricultural equipment.
Fifth, strengthen internal unity, pay attention to perform duties in a responsible manner, ensure high efficiency in accordance with the code of ethics as stated in Chapter 5 from Article 33-38 in the Law on the General Statute of Civil Servants. Must manage and maintain the state property to be good.
Sixth, monitor the daily situation, especially the opinions of the people and attacks from civil society or from various sources and other challenges to monitor the situation or situation, both political, social, economic and technical, and there should be a network to receive Information and suggestions of the community, civil society and all partners to review and resolve in a timely, comprehensive and effective.
On that occasion, the Minister also presented job medals to civil servants and gave souvenirs to 123 retirees to encourage and express gratitude, especially to show the culture of respect, love and care. For the merits of civil servants who have worked hard to sacrifice everything that has served the nation and the people.
