World Tourism Organization Selects Cambodia to Host International Conference on World Civilization and Historical Tour at the End of 2021
The UNWTO Secretary-General made the remarks during a working meeting with Tourism Minister Thong Khon on January 25, 2019 at the UNWTO Permanent Office in Madrid, Spain, after the Ministerial Meeting. World Tourism.
During the meeting, the Minister conveyed the greetings of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to the Secretary-General and confirmed to the UNWTO the support and agreement of the Royal Government of Cambodia in allowing the Ministry of Tourism to cooperate with UNWTO on plans to hold a major international conference on world civilization and a historical tour of Cambodia.
On that occasion, the Minister also informed about the development in Cambodia, especially the development of tourism and thanked UNWTO, which always supports Cambodia in the development of tourism, especially cooperation with other countries in the world.
The Secretary-General also thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for its cooperation in organizing the First World Conference on Tourism and Culture in 2015 in Siem Reap, Angkor, which has been becoming a global event that continues to be hosted. Held for the second time in 2017 in Oman, the third time in 2018 in Turkey, the fourth time in 2019 in Japan and so on.
Leaked information: US Vice President called Venezuelan opposition leader and later announced himself as acting president ...
The WSJ quoted a senior US government official as saying that Pence had promised that the White House would support Guaido if the opposition leader agreed to seize power from President Nicolas Maduro. Period of application of articles in the Venezuelan Constitution.
The source claimed that Pence's late-night phone call on Tuesday was part of a secret plan that Washington had devised weeks ago in an attempt to oust Maduro and recognize Guaido. Acting President of Venezuela.
An unnamed U.S. official said Trump had made Venezuela one of his three main foreign policy priorities, including Iran and North Korea. The White House plot to oust Maduro has been pushed by key members of the US National Security Council, as well as those opposed to Maduro in the US Congress.
According to the source, on January 10, US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo met with Guaido and pledged US support for a democratic future for Venezuela. The US State Department later issued a statement regarding Venezuela: "It is time to start a smooth transition to a new government."
