DaraPay Partners with Cambodia Post Bank and Funan Microfinance Institution to provide loan repayment services
(Phnom Penh): DaraPay, one of Cambodia's leading fast-growing mobile wallet and cash payment solutions provider, has signed a partnership agreement to provide loan repayment services. From customers with Cambodia Post Bank and Funan Microfinance Institution.
This partnership agreement demonstrates the strong trust that Post Bank of Cambodia and Funan Microfinance Institution have in place of DaraPay as an additional financial transaction network for customers to repay their loans to the Bank.
Through this partnership, all customers will be able to repay their bank loans in KHR or USD easily and securely through more than 2,700 DaraPay agents throughout Cambodia without having to spend time traveling to Branch of Cambodia Post Bank or Funan Microfinance Institution.
Toch Chao Chek, CEO of Post Bank of Cambodia, said, “Through this partnership, our clients can easily repay their loans back to Post Bank of Cambodia through DaraPay agents nationwide. Cambodia.
He added that in addition, the new service will help customers who need to repay the loan during the holidays or weekends. Not only that, customers can also repay the loan through Dara The App, which gives customers another level of convenience and security.
Alternatively, customers can transfer money from their savings or current account in Cambodia Post Bank to DaraPay e-wallet through Cambodia Post Bank Mobile Banking app or transfer money from DaraPay Mobile e-wallet to their savings or current account. Cambodia Post through Dara Pay App for free anytime and anywhere.
