Intervention Brigade 1 tells Sam Rainsy that the army is always listening to the orders and ready to take action to destroy the nation
(Phnom Penh): The Army of the 1st Intervention Brigade has announced its readiness to take legal action and court orders against those who attempt to destroy the peace and well-being of the people. In particular, follow the orders of Samdech Techo General Phkay Meas 5 Hun Sen, who ordered the army to take action against those who attempted to destroy the revolution without waiting for orders.
The announcement of the army of the 1st Intervention Brigade came after the prisoner Sam Rainsy, a cowardly politician who was hiding abroad for fear of Cambodia's prisons, called on the armed forces not to obey the orders of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. .
Responding to the call of Sam Rainsy prisoner, Lt. Gen. Prohm Pheng, Deputy Commander of the Army and Commander of the 1st Intervention Brigade, told Fresh News this Saturday, January 26, 2019 that the army is always loyal to Nation, religion, King will always be ready to protect the peace, protect the well-being of the people. But without protection, the people try to destroy the peace and well-being of the people.
"I would like to tell the prisoners who run away from the law that the army always listens and obeys the orders of Samdech Techo General Phkay Meas 5 Hun Sen, the army's top commander. "We are always ready to enforce the law, to comply with court orders against those who attempt to revolutionize, to destroy the peace and well-being of the people, like Sam Rainsy." Lt. Gen. Prohm Pheng confirmed.
The commander of the 1st Intervention Brigade continued, "We, the troops in the 1st Intervention Brigade, would like to invite Sam Rainsy prisoners to enter the country, not just shout." "Come on, we, the army, are waiting for you to come back all the time, waiting for you to strictly enforce the law against him."
