(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has announced the second cold snap in Cambodia, stating that due to the effects of the high pressure valley, the weather in Cambodia will be cold again from today to 28 January. 2019.
The Ministry of Water Resources has confirmed that the minimum temperature will drop to 17 degrees Celsius in mountainous areas and highlands, especially in the Dangrek mountain range in Preah Vihear, Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri provinces. In other capitals and provinces, the minimum temperature will drop to around 20-22 degrees Celsius, except in the coastal provinces where the temperature does not drop.
At the same time, the Ministry called on the people, especially the army heroes, who are stationed in the Dangrek mountain range and in the northeastern plateau to be careful of the cold weather.
