Senior Minister Ieng Moly instructs health officials to study the source of the disease to end AIDS by 2025
(Siem Reap): At Sot Nikum District Referral Hospital and Samrong Health Center, on January 25, 2019, Senior Minister Ieng Moly, President of the National AIDS Authority, met with representatives of Siem Reap Provincial Health Department, Director of Referral Hospital, Director of Health Center. And Samrong Commune Chief to study and understand the integration of HIV / AIDS programs into the joint disease program and the integration of HIV / AIDS into the safe village-commune policy.
After listening to the presentation of Dr. Deputy Director of the Referral Hospital on the implementation of the fight against HIV and AIDS, it is clear that integrating patients is a good way to reduce discrimination. But new figures show an increase in the rate of HIV infection. The senior minister and accompanying officials inquired to find out more.
At the same time, the senior minister also instructed the hospital to study the source of the infection. Is the problem due to the high number of elderly patients or young people in the villages? The senior minister also praised the joint efforts to fight HIV / AIDS and urged hospitals as well as those involved in HIV / AIDS to find innovative ways to eradicate HIV / AIDS by 2025.
At Samrong Health Center, the Senior Minister inquired about the work process as well as the fight against HIV / AIDS. At the same time, the Senior Minister also asked the commune chief to integrate the fight against HIV / AIDS into the policy of safe villages and communes. Past practice in Samrong commune When there is a meeting, there is always talk about HIV / AIDS. But the priority in the commune is the infrastructure with access to clean water and toilets.
In the afternoon of the same day, the Senior Minister went to Siem Reap Referral Hospital to discuss, understand the work process and find ways to continue to succeed in the fight against HIV / AIDS. The Deputy Director of the Hospital and the Director of the Provincial AIDS Secretariat made a brief report, in which Siem Reap Province has achieved the second and third goals of 90-90-90.
After questioning and debating to find good ways to implement the meeting, it was seen that the Commune / Sangkat Council must play an important role in achieving the end of AIDS by 2025. Local authorities are well aware of the well-being of their people, especially migrant workers, who remain difficult targets to find and provide services. Before leaving the hospital, the senior minister and his team also visited the blood test center and dialysis center.
The senior minister praised the health officials for their hard work, especially the fight against HIV / AIDS, which we have worked together successfully. Break the law! Two new constructions on the Twin Canal, a prohibited area in Russey Keo district, were blocked by the authorities
