Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces the withdrawal of Camcontrol at the border checkpoint, the revenue that the Royal Government used to receive more than 30 million US dollars is lost, but the private sector claims that it will get back 40 million dollars because of the official payment of about 30 million dollars And unofficial payments of about $ 10 million.
On January 15, 2019, Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, stated that after the removal of Camcontrol from the border gate, the function of Camcontrol will be given to the customs institution to take responsibility instead.
He added that today only Cambodia has Camcontrol officers at the border unlike other countries, and if Camcontrol is removed from the border gate and left to the customs, it can help reduce royal costs. Government to supply for other expenses.
If we look at the background of Mr. Sam Rainsy's deportation, we can see that from 1997 until now, there have been many deportations and repatriations, including:
June 1, 1997: Deported after leading a series of demonstrations and returned to the district in November of the same year after the situation returned to normal after the events of Day 5. July 6, 1997
2: In February 2005, he was deported after being convicted of defaming the head of the Royal Government. In this case, Mr. Sam Rainsy was pardoned and repatriated in February 2006.
3. At the end of 2009, he was deported after leading his group to remove the Cambodian-Vietnamese border in Svay Rieng province. In the spirit of national unity, Mr. Sam Rainsy was pardoned by the King at the request of the head of the Royal Government and returned to the country in 2013.
4: In November 2015, Mr. Sam Rainsy fled abroad on his own again until now, after the National Assembly decided to revoke his immunity to allow the court to continue the proceedings related to the defamation suit of HE Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong. .
Based on the above background, we can understand that the repeated fabrication of excuses under the pretext that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng forbade him to return to the country in 2015 is a distorted statement with malicious intent. To cover up his cowardice, who did not dare to return to the country to be punished.
Thus, it is clear that fabrication as an excuse through Mr. Sam Rainsy's repeated statements is just a slanderous statement to cover up his cowardice and shame.
We will wait and see how Sam Rainsy can come up with new excuses to hide his cowardice and escape the law.
National Bank of Cambodia: More than 6 million depositors, while 2.85 million borrowers in 2018
(Phnom Penh): According to the report of the National Bank of Cambodia, in 2018, the rate of depositors in banking and financial institutions was more than 6 million, an increase of 13% compared to the same period in 2017. For borrowers, there was an increase of only 2.85 million, an increase of only 3% compared to 2017.
With this steady growth, the banking sector has also expanded its branches and network of operations, including 2,164 locations. The number of ATMs increased to 1,804 throughout Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has made efforts to improve the banking sector, with the National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) promoting the financial and hedging risks to the banking sector in order to continue to support sustainable and inclusive growth. Reduce poverty in Cambodia.
He said these results were particularly evident through the growth of deposits, loans and payments in the banking system. At the same time, the National Bank of Cambodia has continued transparency, fair competition, consumer protection, financial literacy and the draft National Strategy on the Cambodian Financial Environment, which aims to contribute to the sustainability of the banking sector.
He said financial institutions were allowed to incorporate the use of financial technology into their operations to enhance the efficiency and reliability of financial services.
