Ministry of Agriculture launches measures to boost rice production and business after Europe announces rice import tax from Cambodia (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on January 25, 2019 The guidelines set out measures to boost rice production and business after the European Commission decided to impose a tax on Cambodian rice.
The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries (MoFA) has decided to put in place a plan to promote the rice business, especially the intervention to prevent the situation of falling rice prices, according to the instruction of the Ministry of Agriculture, which was received by Fresh News on January 25. Issue some necessary guidelines for immediate implementation as follows:
The European Union (EU) has decided to impose market protection measures by imposing tariffs on Cambodian and Myanmar rice exports to the EU for three years from 2019 to 2021. Cambodia's rice import tax will be levied from January 18, 2019, with the first year paying 175 euros per tonne, the second year paying 150 euros per tonne and the third year paying 125 euros. Euro per ton.
