The following is a sub-decree from the Royal Government of Cambodia: Human Rights Activists: The US military base being built in Japan will adversely affect the Asia-Pacific peace efforts.
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The establishment of a new military base on the Japanese island of Okinawa will have a negative impact on Washington's efforts to negotiate a trade deal with China and eliminate nuclear weapons from Korea, an analyst has said. North. This is according to a quote from the Russian newspaper Sputnik on Friday afternoon, January 25, 2019.
"No country wants rival military bases near their borders," he said. On the other hand, these bases can do nothing but push China and North Korea to spend billions of dollars on strengthening military defense. "Besides, if a conflict erupts, the US military base in Japan could be easily destroyed by China or North Korea in just a few minutes."
The southern Japanese island of Okinawa, which accounts for 0.6 percent of Japan's total territory, is home to more than 30 US military bases with an estimated 25,000 troops. According to the Japanese government, a US military presence is necessary to ensure the security of the East Asian country. But in recent years, there have also been large-scale demonstrations on Okinawa against the US military presence there.
