The Cambodian Naval Agency, known as Kamsap, is currently under the control of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. This unit is responsible for overseeing the activities of international ship business, arranging for legal permission for ships to enter Cambodia and providing information to all relevant parties to form the ship entry-exit and for the owner or customer to prepare documents to receive the goods. As well as some other roles.
During this morning's ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: The Kamsap unit knows that the uncle has decided to cancel the Kamsap unit. And transfer individuals to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to fill.
According to Samdech Techo Prime Minister, before reaching the decision to eliminate such weapons, Samdech also has other options, including leaving the weapon intact, but lowering some fees and some unnecessary services and put in place. Compete between multiple agencies. But the prince thinks that the only option is to eliminate the knife, which is a good option to reduce the complexity of doing business.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that the abolition of the Kamsap institution caused Cambodia to lose only $ 500,000 in revenue per year, but this abolition was for the survival and competitiveness of the national economy, to facilitate trade and business in Cambodia. Nowadays, with more advanced technology, foreign ships can communicate directly with the port.
Cambodia's Kampot Loeung Banana, co-invested by Cambodian-Chinese investors worth $ 32 million, has been exported to the Chinese market for the first time.
According to the tycoon, the first export in the pilot phase started at the beginning of the first week of January, 20 to 40 tons every day and will double when Cambodia can export directly to the market. China.
The tycoon told Fresh News that for 2019, the company plans to export between 20,000 and 25,000 tonnes of fresh bananas to international markets. The main goal of the company is to export more than domestic supply, with the first planned export market being China, followed by other markets.
The banana farm investment project will employ more than 1,000 people to grow, care for, harvest and process bananas for export in 2019, and the number will increase next year.
On the morning of January 25, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on the occasion of meeting with about 10,000 workers in Kampot province, expressed his appreciation and congratulations to Long Met Banana Farm for helping to create jobs for workers. The minimum wage is $ 182 for factory workers. In addition, the farm provides workers with the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) for free medical check-ups, a leading agricultural company.
Please be informed that in early August, Cambodia and China signed a protocol on phytosanitary requirements for Cambodian banana exports to China between Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia. Mr. Shungbor represents the Ministry of Customs of the People's Republic of China under the chairmanship of Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong. This protocol to pave the way for Cambodia to export bananas directly to the Chinese market.
(Phnom Penh): The first 100 million Riel of Carabao energy drink fell into the hands of a young man named Kim Sreng, 19 years old, now a factory driver and living in Trapeang Leap village, Chumpou Prek commune, Udong district, province. Kampong Speu.
In front of the team representing the company to hand over 100 million Riels to the house located in the above geographical location, Mr. Kim Sreng described that today in terms of family living standards are difficult. He was very poor because his father was sick and paralyzed from falling from a palm tree and had no job other than driving a factory truck.
He added that especially for winning the big prize from Carabao energy drink company now is also the most coincidental, because from the beginning, he never thought he would be lucky to win the prize from No carabao, even though there have been frequent winners on television.
He said, but suddenly, on January 23, after taking a break from work, he went to buy a can of Carabao energy drink and ate it. Immediately tell the seller and call the company immediately.
Young Kim Sreng confirmed that after receiving the big prize of 100 million riels, some will be used to treat his father's feet and build a suitable house, and some will be left to set up a business to support the family's livelihood in the future.
Please note: For real prizes, only on the cans with Khmer letters as a mark.
