On Wednesday, after the United States announced the recognition of opposition leader Juan Guaido as Venezuela's acting president, President Maduro announced the severance of diplomatic ties with Washington and allowed 72 hours for US diplomats to leave the country. . In addition, Maduro has decided to close all Venezuelan embassies and consulates in the United States.
At the same time, US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo rejected the dismissal of Maduro US officials, claiming that the Venezuelan president had no decision-making power and that US diplomats had left Maduro. 72 hours to leave the country does not need to follow his instructions.
But it was not until Thursday this week that the State Department immediately announced that its unemployed Venezuelan diplomat should leave the country and even advised all Americans to do the same. .
