According to the announcement of the National Social Security Fund for Civil Servants, obtained by Fresh News on January 25, 2019, "Social Security Policy Funds and Social Security Supplements for Retirees and People "Loss of professional fitness for January 2019 for two weeks, the second will be open from January 29, 2019 onwards."
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Microfinance Association (CMA) has partnered with Khemarak University to provide financial training to university students, as well as to expand their knowledge in this field in Cambodia.
The signing ceremony between CMA and Khemarak University took place on January 24, 2019 with the participation of Dr. Ros Ravuth, Vice Rector of Khemarak University, Mr. Kea Boran, President of CMA and many participants. Crowds.
Dr. Ros Ravuth said that the cooperation between the university and the CMA came after seeing that the understanding of microfinance to students as well as citizens is still limited. In fact, a few years ago, the Royal Government of Cambodia advertised microfinance over the phone to the general public.
He added that this cooperation has provided three benefits to both partners, including: 1. Microfinance staff have a lot of understanding without additional training before entering the job. Second, they already have the skills to work, and third, the unemployment crisis is reduced because when they have the skills, they will apply for these jobs as a contribution to the economy. And society.
Kea Boran said that this is the first collaboration between CMA and Khemarak University, after the success of training, the association also plans to find other educational institutions to cooperate in the training of financial skills more widely.
He added that after the training, he hopes that there will be more people who understand the financial sector than before. In the past, many banks and microfinance institutions have been looking for employees to fill the positions in their institutions, but that search has encountered many difficulties and took a long time to recruit.
He said that this collaboration will help train and produce a lot of human resources in the financial sector, and even if the human resources are produced, but they do not work in the financial sector is not a problem because Financial skills are important skills in managing personal finances in the family and so on.
In addition, the two partners have encouraged the training of financial literacy skills to educational institutions to jointly expand this skill. Please increase caution while driving! One killed, 14 injured in road accidents nationwide
