Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign January 24: 953 Illegal Vehicles Found and 664 Fineed
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for January 24, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 4,961 vehicles and found 953 vehicles violating the law (82% motorcycles), 289 education vehicles and 664 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 3,070 helmets and goggles were inspected on January 24, 209 education helmets and 573 fines were inspected.
In a meeting with a US business delegation led by Norman Arikawa, Assistant Director of Business Development for the Port of Los Angeles, held at the Department of Commerce this afternoon, January 24, 2019, Mr. Pan Sosak explained. The potential of agriculture and manufacturing, where foreign investors can extract high profits from the processing of raw materials into consumer goods and export to third countries.
