The congratulations and presentation of the position of UNDP representatives were made at the Board Meeting of the Working Group on Mine Action for the Third Phase on the morning of January 23, 2019, chaired by Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Authority and attended. Representatives from donors include Australia, Switzerland, Canada, UNDP and the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Mine Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch promised to use the most appropriate aid funds for the real benefit of the people. He also called on donor countries to continue to support the mine action sector so that Cambodia can achieve its goal of a mine-free Cambodia by 2025.
The third phase of mine clearance project for the duration of 4 years 2016-2019. For 2018, the project has continued to address three key points: first: the preparation of the National Strategic Plan for Mine Action 2018-2025, second: the establishment of a control system, and third: the clearance of land with mines and explosive remnants. War, including land reduction projects through non-technical research and the drawing of new minefield polygons.
For 2018, about $ 2,460,877 from the aid of Australia, Switzerland, Canada and UNDP to clear 17.21 square kilometers, focusing on provinces with high levels of landmines and unexploded ordnance. Battambang, Pailin and Banteay Meanchey provinces.
This project is supported by donor countries (Australia, Switzerland, UNDP, Canada and the Royal Government of Cambodia). On that occasion, all donor countries appreciated the rapid economic growth and development in Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and committed to continue to support the Royal Government of Cambodia in the field of mine action. Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will visit Kampot province to meet with more than 10,000 workers.
