A Chinese-funded hospital building was officially inaugurated in Laos on Saturday. The construction of this building is intended to help improve the provision of health services to local people and soldiers as well.
Equipped with nearly 300 beds and six operating rooms, the building operates at the 103rd Lao Military Hospital in Vientiane. Started in 2016, the 24,000-square-meter building is the largest hospital building in Laos compared to other military hospitals. The building can provide medical services to about 3,000 patients a day.
"This is the first time that a large hospital has been set up with the systematic assistance of our troops," said Hor Wei, head of the Chinese medical team in Laos. In the past, when we helped set up a hospital, we used to have different departments, providing free consultation or treatment in a separate way.
