Egypt will begin construction of the country's first electric line after signing a $ 1.2 billion loan agreement with China. The 67-kilometer light rail line will pass through five cities east of Cairo to Egypt's new administrative capital.
"This electric train will open the door to the construction of more light railways in other parts of Egypt, using the same means as with China," he said. "So we can borrow money from China to expand the railway to more areas."
According to the Egyptian government, the electric train should be completed within the next two and a half years. The train will provide transportation services to people living in the new capital, starting in 2020.
Egypt is working on a multibillion-dollar project aimed at developing infrastructure, including the construction of new highways and transport links to connect 13 new cities under construction across the country. Egypt.
