Cambodian Rice Federation issues statement on response to European tariffs on rice imported from Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Rice Federation on January 23, 2019 issued a statement outlining some strategies to respond to and address the EU's taxation on four types of rice imported from Cambodia.
The statement came after leaders of the Cambodian Rice Federation and board members met recently to discuss the impact of tariffs on rice imported from Cambodia to the European market. .
The Cambodian Rice Federation considers that the decision to impose the tax is too early, as the Cambodian rice sector needs a few more years to become strong enough to compete without tax incentives. This tariff will affect competition and make it difficult to import rice from Cambodia to the EU because we are not fully prepared.
The Rice Federation of Cambodia also stated that the decision to impose the tariff was a step backwards between the EU and Cambodia, which had been built in the past, hoping to take many more steps forward in this cooperation.
Taking this opportunity, the Cambodian Rice Federation also called on all Cambodians to support by purchasing Cambodian rice to expand the local market and support our farmers as well as the Cambodian rice sector as a whole.
