(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia National Rescue Party (CNRP) was dissolved by the Supreme Court in accordance with Judgment No. 340C, dated 16 November 2017, blocking the way for protests, and in that verdict it banned the political activities of former leaders of the former CNRP. There are also 118 nationalities, but so far, former senior officials of the party continue to use the same name, logo and structure at all levels without fear of the law.
