Mr. Lim Chea Vutha: Hello Mr. Prak Sam Oeun, can you confirm that the continued use, control and leadership of the former CNRP ("LOGO" and structures at all levels) by the former senior officials of Does this former party show illegal acts? Because the name of this former party was dissolved by the Supreme Court through the power of Judgment No. 340 on November 16, 2017, already blocking the way to protest?
Beijing to spend more than $ 4 billion on 5G development plan by 2022
BEIJING: Beijing telecom operators will jointly spend more than 30 billion yuan (4.4 billion US dollars) to build a 5G network in the Chinese capital by 2022. This is according to the 5G development plan of Beijing, quoted by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Wednesday evening, January 23, 2019.
The 5G network will cover the core areas of the city, including areas within the Second Ring Road, as well as centers in Tongzhou, as well as locations and streets that serve key functions. The 5G technology will also be applied to major infrastructure systems such as the new airport and during the 2022 Winter Olympics.
The President also reaffirmed to Samdech Techo Hun Sen that the One Belt One Road Initiative will continue to strengthen and expand cooperation with countries within the One Belt One Road framework, in which both sides will continue to focus on expanding Regional and international cooperation.
The Chinese president also said that the relationship between China and Cambodia is very special compared to other countries, that is, the relationship between the two countries is very important. He affirmed that China and Cambodia will continue to work together as a community to plan cooperation in all fields, including politics, security, economy and people-to-people contacts.
At the end of the meeting, Chinese President Xi Jinping announced 4 billion yuan (nearly 600 million US dollars) in development assistance to Cambodia from 2019 to 2021. He announced that he would continue to import Cambodian rice to China. 400,000 tons in 2019, an increase of 100,000 tons compared to last year to contribute to improving the lives of Cambodian farmers.
During his visit to China on January 21, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen had two separate meetings with Ms. Gu Xiulian, President of the China-Cambodia Friendship Association, and Mr. Song Tao. Minister of International Relations of the CPC Central Committee
The Chinese Prime Minister said that China will continue to import agricultural products from Cambodia and hoped that Cambodia would continue to export other agricultural products to China and other countries. The Chinese Prime Minister also called on Cambodia and China to continue to use existing mechanisms, including bilateral and regional mechanisms.
After meeting and discussing some important work, on the evening of January 22, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Mr. Li Keqiang, Prime Minister of China, presided over the signing of the document and agreement. Eight important Memoranda of Understanding. The documents of the eight main agreements and Memoranda of Understanding include:
First, an exchange of letters on the second phase of the Rural Road Improvement Project was signed between Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and Mr. Wang Xiaothao, Chairman of the Chinese Agency for International Development Cooperation.
Second: Exchange of Letters on Rural Water Supply Project, Phase 2, signed by Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and Mr. Wang Xiaotao, Chairman of the Chinese Agency for International Development Cooperation.
Third: Exchange of Letters on Engineering Project for Supporting Phnom Penh Expressway Project, Sihanoukville Province, signed by Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and Mr. Wang Xiaothao, Chairman of the Chinese Agency for International Development Cooperation.
Fourth: Certificate of handover on the bodyguard building project of the Office of the Council of Ministers signed between Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Mr. Chung San, Minister of Commerce.
Fifth, a letter of acceptance on the project to upgrade National Road No. 7, which was damaged by floods, signed between Mr. Sun Chanthol, Senior Minister and Minister of Public Works and Transport, and Mr. Chung San, Minister of Commerce.
Sixth: Certificate of handover on Takeo temple restoration project signed between Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Chung San, Minister of Commerce.
Seventh: Concessional Loan Agreement for Preah Vihear Reservoir Development Project signed between Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Mr. Hu Xiaolan, President of the Export-Import Bank of China.
8th: Agreement on the Promotion of Investment Cooperation under the Rectangular Strategy and the Belt and Road Initiative signed between Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, with Mr. Yi Huayman, President of the Industrial Bank and Chinese trade.
After concluding a successful visit to the Great Land of China for the past three days, Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to return to Cambodia on the afternoon of January 23. This 2019.
CL Japanese Language Training Center criticized for defrauding tens of thousands of students by promising to send them to work in Japan
(Phnom Penh): Students from many provinces have lost tens of thousands of dollars because the Director General of the Japanese Language Training Center (CL) did not keep their promises and used fraudulent tricks to defraud them of thousands of dollars in Everyone did not go to Japan as promised.
