Chheang Chhum later used dishonest tactics and told his students, who were studying at the CL Japanese Language Training Center, that they had been forced to work in Japan, requiring all victims to pay to prepare. Visa to work in Japan
At that time, Chheang Chhum paid the victims $ 1,700 each, and some of them spent almost $ 5,000, but the results were useless, waiting for a day. It took months to realize that they had cheated the director of the CL Japanese Language Training Center.
According to the source, Chheang Chhum played the role of director general and chairman of the board, and when the Ministry of Labor never invited him to appear, he appeared.
Other sources make it clear that it was not just the nearly 20 victims who cheated on Chheang Chhum. The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training kindly inspected the location of the Japanese Language Training Center (CL) above so that the people as well as their nephews would not suffer the same loss of time and money and did not go abroad.
