This expression of satisfaction with the development of the Parliament in the South China Sea was confirmed in the joint statement between Cambodia and the People's Republic of China released on the afternoon of January 23, 2019, as a result of Samdech Techo's official visit. Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to China from January 20 to 23, 2019.
"The Cambodian side highly appreciates and supports the request of the Chinese side to conclude the COC consultations within three years and to cooperate with the relevant parties to maintain the positive development of the consultations," the joint statement said. "We strive to complete the consultations as soon as possible on the basis of mutual consensus and to build the South China Sea into a sea of peace, friendship and cooperation."
