(Phnom Penh): Many well-known online electronic news organizations in Cambodia have called on the media and website owners to stop plagiarizing their writings or news articles immediately.
In a joint statement issued on January 23, 2019, the owners of these well-known online news organizations stated that all forms of plagiarism were in violation of the intellectual property law of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Stealing works or stealing intellectual property is an act of betrayal of ideals and professional conscience.
The statement also called on legitimate and professional companies to consider carefully when choosing to advertise their products on any news website and not to cooperate with news websites that do not respect the news profession and are prone to plagiarism. Do not copy the work and wisdom of others.
The owners of these well-known online news organizations also called on the public to join in the fight against piracy by rejecting and stopping any websites that plagiarize articles from others.
(Banteay Meanchey): On January 23, 2019, Mr. Teng Samay, Deputy Prosecutor of the Provincial Court, led Mr. Chap Sopharith, Deputy Provincial Commissioner in charge of crime prevention, Mr. San Vichea Saravuth, Branch Manager of Camcontrol and professional officers. Many others cracked down on illegal palm sugar production and processing in Chankiri village, Phsar Kandal commune, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province.
Mr. Chap Sopharith said that the above forces searched the site for several days until the crackdown, confiscating a large number of exhibits.
According to the Deputy Commissioner, the owner of the location, Phay Samnang, a 26-year-old man living in the above handicraft shop, confiscated the following exhibits: 900 kilograms of sugar, 2 pots of brown rice for cooking, 30 bags of unprocessed palm sugar, and a motorized frying pan. Beat 1 palm sugar, 600 grams of sausage, 50 kg of processed palm sugar and some other ingredients.
The owner of the palm sugar factory, Phay Samnang, a 26-year-old man, confessed to the police that he had been making palm sugar from his father's ghost for eight years without knowing the health effects of the buyers. Also.
The owner of the location said that this processed palm sugar is mixed into 4 types, including: 14 kg of water, 50 kg of sugar, 10 kg of pure palm sugar and 10 g of sour meat, which can be processed into 60 palm sugar. -70 kg.
Currently, the competent authorities have temporarily detained the owner of the above handicraft site for further interrogation, while the processing equipment and location have been closed pending further investigation. The Minister of Cults instructed the Acharya to follow the ancient rules that our ancestors left behind to avoid contradictory practices.
(Phnom Penh): In the closing ceremony of the training course on the role, duties and ethics of the 31st generation of Khmer priests on January 23, 2019, Mr. HIM Chhem, Senior Minister, Minister of Cult and Religion, stated that Cambodia is a country with culture and tradition. It has rich traditions and is one of the oldest ethnic groups in the region.
During the ceremony, Senior Minister Him Chhem stated, "Through the study of history from one era to another, we can conclude that Cambodia is a country with a rich culture and traditions and a nation with Older people in the area.
"That is why we observe that all activities in the tradition are always in many forms and embedded with deep meaning," he said. For each ritual, there are many philosophical educational arts. Therefore, all Buddhist ceremonies, traditional customs need to be educated and properly practiced with a unified principle.
At the same time, Mr. Him Chhem said that the Achar as the leader must know how to explain and guide others to know the right and wrong path, and must have a high and clear knowledge of both Buddhism and the empire in order to lead the work in other rituals. In the traditional Khmer way.
He said that as the leader of various ceremonies, the acha must do the right thing according to the ancient rules left by our ancestors, and that the practice must be consistent from one area to another to avoid the opposite practice. Each caused by the application of different rules of the ancient rules and the copying of different practices.
At the same time, in order to enhance the strengthening of the implementation of Khmer traditions in line with the influx of globalization and development in all fields, the Minister of Cult gave some recommendations, including:
* First, all abbots must be united, cooperate and have good relations with the pagoda committee, pagoda chaplain, as well as the chief of the sub-department of cult and religion, the capital, provinces, municipalities, districts, local authorities and Buddhists are not partisan and social class discrimination.
* Second: We must strive to preserve and preserve the cultural heritage of Buddhism and Khmer traditions to be stable, to work together to promote the field of Buddhism to be prosperous.
* Third: All abbots must respect and implement effectively all existing documents.
* Fourth: In order to be worthy as an elder with experience and knowledge in the village, district, all abbots must adhere to the seven charities consistently.
* Fifth: Acha must continue to strengthen his knowledge, try to research the scriptures, rules, rules, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals, rituals. All left for the benefit of the future.
* Sixth: As the Acharya acts as the elder of his district, the Acharya must be an example in obeying Buddhism, the rules of morality, ethics, preventing domestic violence and taking the lead in contributing to social development to set a good example. Our younger generation.
* Seventh: In order for the people to respect the position of elders, all abbots must respect the roles, duties and ethics of abbots in accordance with the rules and regulations to lead the ceremonies, weddings and other ceremonies on the basis of law, custom and certainty.
