During his three-day visit to China, Hun Sen met with Chinese President Xi Jinping, Chinese Premier Li Keqiang and Wang Yang, chairman of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference. Mr. Li Chanshu, Chairman of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress, and Mr. Song Tao, Minister of International Relations, Central Committee of the Communist Party of China.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also authorized the management of three major Chinese companies, including the Chinese Engineering and Steel Company, the China Bridge and Road Corporation and the Huong Neng Group. The Prime Minister also allowed the President of the Bank of China to pay a courtesy call and discuss some investment matters.
In addition to the above meeting, the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia also allowed the President of the China-Cambodia Friendship Association to pay a courtesy call. Taking time to meet Cambodian people and students living and studying in Cambodia is a job that Samdech Techo Hun Sen never misses.
During his current visit to China, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also met with nearly 500 Cambodian students studying in China.
It is noteworthy that during his visit to mark the 60th anniversary of Cambodia-China relations, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was especially welcomed by the Chinese leadership. Strengthening relations and cooperation in the fields of economy, trade, investment and strengthening the relationship between the people of the two countries were discussed, especially between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Chinese leadership.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's sixth official visit to China is fruitful for further strengthening ties and cooperation between the two countries. Both Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Chinese leadership are committed to enhancing relations and cooperation with each other without any external forces.
In addition to its commitment to boosting investment and strengthening economic, trade and investment cooperation, Chinese President Xi Jinping has announced a $ 600 million grant from the Cambodian head of government. Developed in Cambodia for 3 years from 2019 to 2021 and announced to buy 400,000 tons of rice from Cambodia in 2019.
The Chinese president also announced an increase in purchases of Cambodian products and agricultural products. The announcement of aid, as well as the purchase of rice and other agricultural products, is seen as a sign of China's firm stance on promoting and strengthening relations with Cambodia.
During Samdech Techo Hun Sen's current visit, China and Cambodia also signed eight documents and a memorandum of understanding. Documents of the eight main agreements and memoranda of understanding, including:
First. Exchange of Letters on Rural Road Improvement Project, Phase 2, signed between Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and Mr. Wang Xiaothao, Chairman of the China Agency for International Development Cooperation.
Second. Exchange of Letters on the Second Phase of Rural Water Supply Project signed between Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Mr. Wang Xiaotao, Chairman of the Chinese Agency for International Development Cooperation.
Third. Exchange of Letters on Engineering Project in Support of Phnom Penh Expressway Project, Sihanoukville Province, signed by Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and Mr. Wang Xiaothao, President of the China Agency for International Development Cooperation.
Fourth. Letter of Acceptance on the Bodyguard Building Project of the Office of the Council of Ministers signed between Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Mr. Chung San, Minister of Commerce.
Fifth. Letter of acceptance on the project to upgrade National Road No. 7, which was damaged by floods, signed between Mr. Sun Chanthol, Senior Minister and Minister of Public Works and Transport, and Mr. Chung San, Minister of Commerce.
Sixth. Certificate of handover on Takeo temple renovation project signed between Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Chung San, Minister of Commerce.
7th. Concessional Loan Agreement for Preah Vihear Reservoir Development Project signed between Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Mr. Hu Xiaolian, President of the Export-Import Bank of China.
8th. Agreement on the Promotion of Investment Cooperation under the Rectangular Strategy and the Belt and Road Initiative signed between Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, and Mr. Yi Huiman, President of the Bank for Industry and Commerce of China .
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid his first visit to China in February 1999. Starting from this first relationship, the Chinese government has worked closely with Samdech Techo Hun Sen to expand and strengthen the relationship to the present.
In addition to these six official visits, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has visited China six more times to attend meetings and forums held in China.
