(Mondulkiri): The National League of Local Councils, which is an organization representing all municipal, district, Khan, commune and sangkat councils in Cambodia, on January 23, 2019, held its National Council meeting for the purpose of reviewing the achievements of 2018. And raise the work direction for 2019 in Mondulkiri province.
The National League of Local Councils was established with the aim of enhancing the status and capacity of municipal, district, Khan, commune and sangkat councils throughout Cambodia. There are currently 197 municipal, district and khan councils in Cambodia, and 1,646 commune councilors are members of the National League.
The meeting, which was attended by a total of 130 people, including the National Council of 88 National Coalition, will also disseminate the five-year strategic plan (2018-2022). In addition, the meeting focused on gender analysis in local economic development and lessons on general perspectives on local economic development.
BEIJING, Jan. 22 (Xinhua) - The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, presented the progress of the national trade sector to the Cambodia-China Trade and Investment Promotion Forum 2019, which was held on Tuesday morning, January 22, 2019. The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, together with a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of China, a total of more than 800 people.
On that occasion, Minister Pan Sosak informed Samdech Techo and the whole forum about the progress of the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and China, which in 2017 reached 5 billion USD as planned and plans to increase. $ 6 billion by 2020 and $ 10 billion by 2023.
He also mentioned the establishment of Cambodian business centers in major cities in China, such as Guangzhou, Hainan, Xi'an and Hong Kong, which are currently playing an important role in boosting the country's trade, economy, tourism and culture. In the future, the Ministry of Commerce also plans to set up more centers in Beijing, Kunming, and other cities.
Please be informed that the Cambodia-China Trade and Investment Promotion Forum is the best meeting for the private sector to get recommendations from the two heads of government and also an opportunity for Chinese investors to learn about Cambodia's key policies and potential sectors. To trade and invest in line with the Belt and Road Initiative of Chinese President Xi Jinping.
