Cambodian Minister of Justice attends World Conference on Judgment Implementation in China
Speaking at the conference, Mr. Ang Vong Vathana noted that the implementation of the verdict is important and complex when it comes to implementation, and each country has its own set of legal systems and court procedures for the mechanism to implement the verdict.
In fact, for Cambodia, there are important laws related to the execution of judgments, such as the Code of Civil Procedure, the Law on Complaints related to Individual Status, the Law on Non-Civil Procedures, etc. The execution of the verdict is done by the court and the implementation of the foreign verdict according to Article 352 of the Cambodian Code of Civil Procedure requires the prior recognition of the Cambodian court.
The Minister also said that in order to implement the verdict effectively, it requires training and capacity building as well as ethics of law enforcement officers, focusing on close cooperation with other countries in the field of information technology to modernize the judiciary. Smart court.
He said that in accordance with the Rectangular Strategy, the Ministry of Justice has set a clear vision, developing a strategic plan and a sustainable action plan to implement the verdict effectively to ensure justice for all Cambodians.
The World Conference on Judgment Enforcement was chaired by Zhou Qiang, President of the Supreme Court of China, with the participation of Justice Ministers, Supreme Court leaders from 29 countries and two international organizations. As a result, the conference adopted the Shanghai Declaration of the World Conference on the Implementation of the Judgment.
At the official welcoming ceremony, Samdech Techo PM and his Chinese counterpart paid homage to the flags of the two countries, the Kingdom of Cambodia and the People's Republic of China.
Afterwards, the two heads of government of Cambodia and China convened a bilateral meeting in a very cordial atmosphere. Chinese Premier Li Keqiang warmly welcomed Samdech Techo's official visit as well as the Chinese delegation.
The Prime Minister of China considers the first official visit to China since the formation of the 6th term of the Royal Government of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as an important visit for Cambodia-China bilateral relations. He also said that he paid a visit to Cambodia in January 2018, which was not only an official visit but also attended the Lancang-Mekong Cooperation Summit.
In response, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that his current visit to China is to strengthen bilateral relations as well as cooperation and friendship between the two countries. The Prime Minister said that Mr. Li Keqiang's visit in 2018 contributed to the strengthening of friendly relations and cooperation between the two countries.
During the meeting, the Prime Minister asked the Prime Minister whether any leaders of the country will visit China in 2019? Answering this question, Mr. Li Keqiang said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the first Prime Minister of a friendly country of China to visit China in 2019.
The Chinese Prime Minister stressed that he has seen a lot of progress and development in Cambodia-China relations and thanked the Prime Minister for his significant contribution to the bilateral relationship. Prime Minister Li Keqiang also raised issues related to the July 2018 Cambodian elections. He congratulated Samdech Techo Hun Sen on his election as Prime Minister in the new term.
Li Keqiang said that the cooperation between China and Cambodia is based on mutual respect and mutual benefit. He considered the Prime Minister an old friend of the Chinese people.
The Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo, congratulated the 40th anniversary of the introduction of China's economic reform policy to become the world's second largest economy. The Prime Minister also congratulated China on the 70th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China and its great achievements.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also briefed the Chinese Prime Minister on the political and social situation in Cambodia. Samdech Techo said that the political situation and social problems in Cambodia have improved, especially economic growth in 2018, maintaining growth of about 7 percent with many reforms. The Prime Minister said that now Cambodia has been continuing to implement what was promised to the people before the election. In particular, the provision of social protection.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked China for its support for development in Cambodia in the past. He also thanked the Chinese government for supporting the Royal Government of Cambodia's measures to maintain peace, stability and security in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo also highlighted that what was important in the meeting between Samdech and President Xi Jinping yesterday was to provide a quota of 300,000 to 400,000 tons of Cambodian rice to China. Samdech Techo said that increasing the quota is an important political response for the people of Cambodia and other countries as well.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that he would like to see a free trade agreement between the two countries in the near future. Samdech Techo said that he was very happy to see the traditional relationship between Cambodia and China, which has become a strategic partner in all aspects.
Samdech Techo continued that in 2018, he visited Cambodia and both sides celebrated the 60th anniversary of the two countries' relations. Samdech Techo said that the substantial assistance from China to Cambodia is an important contribution to Cambodia's economic development. Samdech Techo said that this assistance has helped strengthen Cambodia's independence. Samdech Techo thanked China for providing assistance for the 2018 election.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia said that the two countries still have a lot of potential for promoting trade, investment and tourism. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that a number of projects are part of the Royal Government of Cambodia's fourth phase of the Belt and Road and Rectangular Policy Initiative, which the Bank of China can support in terms of financing. Samdech Techo said that supporting the project is beneficial for both countries.
Samdech Techo expects the two countries to have more projects within the framework of the Royal Government of Cambodia's fourth phase of the Belt and Road Initiative and Rectangular Policy.
Yesterday, President Xi Jinping announced a 4 billion yuan grant for three years from 2019 to 2021. Samdech Techo Hun Sen presented six major projects related to road, bridge and electricity infrastructure. Samdech Techo asked China to support these six important projects.
Regarding free trade, Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked both parties to examine and study this issue. During the meeting, the Prime Minister also asked China to continue to import more Cambodian agricultural products and agricultural products beyond what China currently has as a large market in the world.
Regarding culture, tourism and education, as well as other fields, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Chinese friends who have helped Cambodia in the past and asked China to continue to help in this area. Samdech Techo asked China to help restore ancient temples in Cambodia and thanked China for providing scholarships to Cambodian students, who currently have nearly 2,000 Cambodian students studying in China.
Samdech Techo also highlighted the need for human resources for Cambodia today. In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also raised security issues.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also welcomed the docking of Chinese ships docked in Sihanoukville three times in 2018. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked Mr. Li Keqiang for providing 840 million yuan in aid for the military in the past. Samdech Techo expressed his desire to see the Government of the People's Republic of China continue to assist other sectors, including the police, in managing security.
Finally, Samdech Techo Hun Sen cordially invited Mr. Ly Ker Chheang to visit Cambodia at an appropriate time.
The Chinese Prime Minister said that China will continue to import agricultural products from Cambodia as well, and hoped that Cambodia would continue to export other agricultural products to China and other countries. He also called on Cambodia and China to continue to use existing mechanisms, including bilateral and regional mechanisms.
The Chinese Prime Minister also said that he would find a suitable time to visit Cambodia.
After meeting and discussing some important work, on the evening of January 22, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Mr. Li Keqiang, Prime Minister of China, presided over the signing of the document and agreement. Eight important memoranda of understanding.
