Qingdao, China strengthens economic, trade and tourism cooperation with Sihanoukville
(Preah Sihanouk): A delegation from Qingdao City led by Mr. Luoy Jianjun, Deputy Governor of Qingdao City of the People's Republic of China paid a courtesy call on Mr. Yun Min, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province on the morning of January 22, 2019 at Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hall. To strengthen cooperation between Qingdao and Sihanoukville in the fields of economy, trade, science, education and tourism, and the development of the Blue Port economy and tourism.
On that occasion, Mr. Yun Min welcomed the delegation from Qingdao City and informed about the potential of Sihanoukville International Port, which has a wide scope for connecting national and international sea freight services. It accounts for nearly 73% of the country's total exports and imports.
He added that Sihanoukville has an international airport that plays an important role in transporting national and international passengers to visit and invest in Sihanoukville. Currently, the airport is operated by 11 airlines, including domestic flights. 83 feet per week and 61 feet per week abroad. There are 16 direct destinations from Chinese provinces and cities to Sihanoukville.
According to Yun Min, Sihanoukville has four special economic zones in operation, with a total of 160 small and large factories and 1,037 handicrafts, employing a total of 68,354 people. The average number of tourists increased by 10 to 15 percent per year, especially Chinese tourists ranked first with 202,947, an increase of 68.79 percent.
