Nearly 60 militants and seven Egyptian soldiers killed in fighting in Sinai
Cairo: At least 59 militants have been killed in fighting in recent days on the Sinai Peninsula in Egypt. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday evening, January 22, 2019.
An Egyptian military spokesman said that during a recent counter-terrorism operation in the Sinai Peninsula, national security forces killed about 59 terrorists armed with explosives and other weapons. This left seven soldiers dead. In addition, 56 vehicles, two weapons depots and 242 explosives belonging to the militants were also destroyed.
Egypt has been battling terrorism since former President Mohamed Morsi stepped down in 2013 over large-scale protests against his leadership. The Sinai Peninsula is a stronghold of terrorists in Egypt, as more than 800 militants and more than 30 Egyptian soldiers have been killed since the anti-terrorism campaign in Sinai began in February 2018.
