In a statement, the Royal Government spokesman stated that Sam Rainsy's repatriation was a purely personal will because Sam Rainsy's departure was also a personal choice and his personal character.
The statement added that the use of Sam Rainsy's repatriation, through any group or organization, to create a political image related to the activities of the former party, which was dissolved by the Supreme Court's ruling yesterday. November 16, 2017 is considered an act against the actual judicial power that is defined and prohibited by law.
Mr. Phay Siphan stated: "The Royal Government would like to emphasize that it still maintains and respects the democratic principle of separation of powers between the executive and the judiciary, as well as the legislature. In this context, if there is any request from the court, the Royal Government as well as the relevant authorities will take action in accordance with the legal authority.
The Cambodian government's warning comes after supporters of Sam Rainsy and his party, who claim to be members of the former CNRP Standing Committee, held a meeting in Lowell, USA, and former Vice President Eng Chai Eang Of the former CNRP announced that the outcome of this meeting was decided to organize the return of Mr. Sam Rainsy to Cambodia in the near future.
Mr. Sam Rainsy has repeatedly stated that he intends to return to Cambodia since he was deported in 2016, but apparently he did not return to Cambodia as promised.
Mr. Sam Rainsy is currently on trial in a number of court cases, including a series of criminal cases, including a five-year prison sentence for forgery of Cambodian-Vietnamese border documents and sentencing. Imprisoned for 1 year and 8 months for defamation and incitement without charge based on Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the person behind the murder of Dr. Kem Ley.
In Beijing, the prices of both new and resold homes will fall in 2018 in general. House prices in Guangzhou, on the other hand, have fluctuated significantly as new homes have risen steadily. In December 2018, Guangdong ranked first among 70 cities with new home prices up 3% from November.
Level 2, 3 and 4 cities have a similar situation. In the first six months of 2018, new housing prices in cities such as Sanya and Haikou in southern China continued to rise, forcing local governments to introduce a series of measures to control house prices. A big one last May.
Ms. Ren believes that these policies have helped slow down the rise in property prices in some cities where housing prices have risen. And today these policies have some adjustments to each city.
These adjustments are based on recent developments in the real estate sector and the realities of supply and demand in the market.
New Year is the most important festival for the Chinese people and has been celebrated for more than 4,000 years. This is also an opportunity to return home, reunite family, celebrate the New Year and wish good luck for the coming year.
