All this is even more important for the traditional dining gathering that will take place on February 5, 2019. This dinner is the most important dinner of the year for the Chinese people and is a time for all family members to come together and celebrate the New Year.
For restaurants across the country, New Year is the busiest time of the year and many places are reportedly fully booked.
As a sign of the growing popularity of online shopping in China, semi-finished and cooked dinners for the New Year are also selling well online. All of these meals allow those who are very busy or those who do not know how to cook to organize a delicious meal for their family.
