The body of Professor Kong Nary will be cremated tomorrow night at Srah Chak pagoda
Professor Kong Nary passed away at 12:30 on January 20, 2019, after falling seriously ill and being hospitalized for nearly two months at Preah Kosamak Hospital, also known as Lok Sang Hospital. At present, the body of Professor Kong Nary is being kept for the traditional ceremony at Wat Srah Chak.
From this important forum, Samdech Techo Hun Sen tried to highlight the economic reforms and some features that are all favorable for investors and business people.
In front of senior Chinese officials, a total of 800 Cambodian-Chinese investors and businessmen, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Cambodia has undergone profound internal reforms to increase competitiveness and ensure economic independence. A fully sovereign country.
The Prime Minister emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been implementing five approaches, including mirrors, dehydration, treatment and surgery under two mottos: internal reform and increasing external friendships in the spirit of independence.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he has decided to deepen the reform of the internal economic system by introducing and implementing a new measure, keeping only the customs agents to inspect goods at the international gates. International border gates, bilateral border gates, border area gates and seaports, special economic zones, temporary customs warehouses and other import and export control points.
"Such a decision is the implementation of a surgical approach, one of Cambodia's major reforms to reduce the complexity and cost of trade, aimed at improving the business environment and investment. And enhancing Cambodia's competitiveness. ” Samdech Techo Hun Sen further confirmed.
The Prime Minister pointed out to Chinese investors and businessmen that in addition to the above reforms, Cambodia has five other features that are sacred opportunities for investment in Cambodia.
Fifth, Cambodia and China have many agreements that promote and provide rich benefits to Chinese businesses and investors, both incentives and investment guarantees.
Investment volume has grown to about $ 6.8 billion, an increase of about 7% compared to 2017, with China remaining the largest investor in Cambodia in 2018. The total investment capital is about 3.6 billion US dollars, accounting for 53% of the total investment volume, an increase of about 54% compared to 2017.
