Cambodia and 17 other international countries meet in Phnom Penh to learn about globalization and new technologies to change the competitive market environment
(Phnom Penh): Under the auspices of the Cambodian Federation of Employers and Business Associations (CAMFEBA) and the Association for Overseas Technical Cooperation and Sustainable Partnership (AOTS), the Royal Government of Cambodia, together with 17 regional countries Other countries are meeting to learn about globalization and new technologies to change the competitive environment in the market.
The meeting was held on the evening of January 22, 2019 at the Phnom Penh Hotel under the chairmanship of Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, and the presence of delegates representing federations and employers' associations from 17 countries in the region, including China, India, Indonesia, Korea, Laos, Malaysia, Mexico, Mongolia, Myanmar, Nepal, Bangladesh, Pakistan, Sri Lanka, Philippines, Singapore, Thailand and Vietnam.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng highly appreciated the organization of this important forum to study, understand, compare and share the working conditions of each country so that the participants can have knowledge about professional relations, human resource management, tripartite management system. .
The Minister said that this forum has really contributed to the Royal Government in creating opportunities to attract international investors as well as strengthen the friendship and good cooperation between local employers 'associations, employers' federations and the Cambodian Business Association. Hosted this international networking event.
The forum will also provide opportunities for Cambodian business owners to build networks and find future investment partners from these participating countries.
