Small hydropower at Roleang Chrey Dam will become a new tourist attraction in Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, together with many professional officials, on January 22, 2019, inspected the construction of a small hydropower plant at the Leang Chrey sluice gate in Tang Krouch commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province. It is believed that the Reang Chrey Dam will become another new tourist attraction.
The small dam has the power to generate 3.4 megawatts of power to supply and distribute more to the people in the area for additional use.
Mr. Vy Samnang said that the construction of this dam has made Kampong Speu not only have a high level of electricity, but also can be developed into a tourist area.
The governor said that the provincial administration intends to turn the area into a tourist attraction by boat, fishing and hydropower to increase people's daily lives.
Please note that Kampong Speu has some tourist attractions, including:
* Phnom Preah Reach Trop: The Khmer capital of the Udong period, located in Udong district.
Chreav Waterfall: Located in Omlaing Commune, Thpong District, a newly discovered natural waterfall resort with great potential.
Noor Borey Museum: Located on National Road 4 at Chambok village, Vallis commune, Samrong Tong district. This museum was built as a family for the purpose of owning property and contributing to the preservation of national cultural heritage. Nor Borei Museum has artifacts from prehistoric times to the present, and most of them are statues made of wood, stone and pottery, totaling thousands of artifacts.
Ampe Phnom: Ampe Phnom is a cultural and natural resort located in Taing Tonle village and Ampe Phnom village, Sopor Tep commune and Svay Kravan commune, Chbar Morn city, about 48 km from Phnom Penh, turn left 2 km and reach this resort.
* Preah Suramarit Kosamak National Park or Kirirom: Kirirom is a natural resort. This area has special features for tourists such as dense pine forest, shady paradise and fresh air, which makes it feel very fresh. In Damrey Phong village, Kirirom commune, Phnom Sruoch district, 117 km from Phnom Penh on National Road 4 on the top of the mountain, 700 m high.
* Kirirom Resort (Lower): This resort is located near the foot of Kirirom Mountain, most of it has been revitalized to attract tourists. There are hotels, playgrounds, dinosaur parks, playgrounds and baths.
* Chambok: Chambok is a beautiful natural resort and is popular with national and foreign tourists. The road is cool, very interesting. Chambok is more than 1 km north of Kirirom in Chambok commune, Phnom Sruoch district.
Anlong Roth Waterfall: Anlong Roth Waterfall is located about 4 km north of Kirirom National Park and about 3 km from Chambok Waterfall Resort, located in Chambok Commune, Phnom Sruoch District. The Anlong Roth Waterfall Resort was established in late 2008 under the tutelage of Mlup Baitong and Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Tourism under the auspices of the Dutch VCN.
Old Phnom Cave Cave Resort: Old Phnom Cave Cave Resort is located in Oral District. 'Resort is a recently discovered historical resort. There are many large caves, especially visitors will see the dance and get to know the traditions of a minority there, the Sui.
Phnom Preah Natural Cultural Resort: Phnom Preah is a place where people from near and far gather to worship and pray according to their faith, because there are so many miracles in the faith. Phnom Chas Cultural and Tourist Resort covers an area of 100 hectares in Oral district on the way to Lyong Phat sugar plantation, more than 50 kilometers from Kampong Speu provincial town.
* K'aek Pong Temple: This temple is a solitary temple, 15 km away from Kampong Speu province, located in Taing Yeak commune, Phnom Sruoch district. K'aek Pong Temple was built on a hill about 300 meters high with four corners. The top of the temple collapsed and the temple cracked almost completely.
Mr. Khuong Sreng stated that Phnom Penh Capital Hall does not have the right to order a factory owner to dismantle his factory, enterprise or warehouse from Phnom Penh. However, he encouraged the construction of factories, enterprises or warehouses along the Third Ring Road, because after this road is completed, container trucks and trucks will no longer be allowed to enter Phnom Penh.
"We have no right to order them," he said. But the future is like this, so I encourage him to consider finding a place to build a factory, enterprise or warehouse along the third ring road. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Khuong Sreng.
The Third Ring Road is an important strategic route to connect the provinces to Phnom Penh and avoid traffic in Phnom Penh. The construction of the third ring road was opened on January 14, 2019, recently under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The Third Ring Road (National Road No. 4-National Road No. 1) is located in Phnom Penh and Kandal Province, with a total length of nearly 53 km, including more than 15 km through Phnom Penh and almost 38 km through Kandal Province. Kilometers with a starting point from km 14 + 105 of National Road No. 4 and an end point at km 24 + 840 of National Road No. 1.
This road is up to 27 meters wide for downtown and 25 meters wide for out of town. The road will have street lights for city streets and ornamental trees for suburban roads.
The third ring road will have four flyovers (crossing National Roads 4, 3, 2 and 21) with a total length of 1,000 meters. Construction of 2 bridges across the Bassac River at Anlong Chen Island with a total length of 996 meters (including the 630-meter-long East Bassac Bridge and the 366-meter-long West Bassac Bridge). Construction of 6 medium and short bridges and 113 sewers of all kinds.
The road project will cost a total of 273 million US dollars, a concessional financing from the Chinese government, and the Royal Government of Cambodia contributes to the impact of demining and unexploded ordnance, taxes and royalties. The road, a major economic artery, will take 42 months to complete and is scheduled for completion in December 2021.
