Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Distributes Donations to 3 Families Affected by Riverbank Collapse
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, this morning, January 22, 2019, distributed the donation from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to 3 families who were affected and displaced by the collapse. The river bank is located in Prek Sdey village, Preah Andong commune, Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province.
After receiving greetings from the people of Samdech Bun Rany Hun Sen, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said that the river bank collapse is a natural disaster that always happens every year, especially during the flood season. This landslide depends on the area where the river flows, only once it collapses at this point and then grows at that point according to its nature.
He added that this has been the case for many years in the Mekong Delta. Meanwhile, the river bank collapse during the dry season also occurs, but not as severe as during the actual flood season, now three families have been affected by the impact of the river bank collapse, making them decide to demolish their houses. Switch to building on a new location.
The provincial governor said that in the case of the river bank collapse, he also set up a committee to study and research data to conclude the level of impact on the people in the coming year in order for the commission. We have measures in place to better rescue the people.
According to the provincial governor, the gift of Samdech Kittipritthbandit, which was distributed to 3 families at this time, 1 family received 50 kg of rice, 2 sticks of canned fish, 2 sticks of soy sauce, fish sauce. 2 sticks, 2 noodles and a budget of 200,000 riels.
It should be noted that after distributing gifts to the people, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun continued to visit the people and inspect the bank of the river that collapsed at the back of the house of Prime Minister Hun Sen in his hometown in Peam Krao village. Peam Koh Sna, Stung Trang district as well.
CamControl officers inspected some petrol depots in Russey Keo district and found 4 locations selling incorrect fuel
(Phnom Penh): The fuel inspection team of the General Department of CamControl of the Ministry of Commerce through the mobile fuel laboratory vehicle led by Mr. Mean Chamnap, Deputy Director of the Department on January 22, 2019 in cooperation with the professional officers of the laboratory. Inspected the quantity and quality of fuel at some stations and depots located in Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
He said the operation was aimed at protecting the economic interests of consumers, protecting the machinery of all types of vehicles and protecting the environment arising from improper fuel consumption, and especially to prevent fraud.
The deputy director of the department added that the quality and quantity control is based on on-site monitoring equipment, such as a caliper tank with a specific size for measuring the amount of oil fired from the counter in different sizes, with a capacity of 5 liters 10 Liters and 20 liters. The octane and cetan indexes are used in mobile laboratory vehicles.
Inspection officials have asked the station and depot owners to make a contract to adjust the vending machine according to the correct prediction through the competent authority.
He added that all vehicle users must consider in advance to choose a gas station / depot, a company that trusts the use of new equipment, sells regular gasoline or soup and good quality diesel, and all liters check the counter number from zero. Always check the operation of the counter number to start with the fuel injector up to the last liter requested to monitor the Ministry of Commerce's fuel price notice.
At the same time, be careful of fire safety by turning off the vehicle engine when refueling in the station and please provide information to the CamControl officer in the capital or province or to the General Department of CamControl in case of any event.
