Chen Siqing, chairman of the Board of Directors of the Bank of China, said his bank had been operating in Cambodia for many years. The bank representative said that in China, Samdech Techo Hun Sen is considered an old friend of China, and in the past, the Chinese side has always considered the Prime Minister's relationship with President Xi Jinping to be close and close.
The Chinese representative said that he was grateful for the past support of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as well as the Royal Government. He will work to ensure that the Royal Government of Cambodia's One Belt, One Road and Rectangular Strategic Political Initiative is coherent and interconnected.
The Chinese representative said that after listening to Samdech's speech, he appreciated the vision of Samdech's leadership, saying that Samdech has a clear vision to lead Cambodia to develop into a high middle-income country by 2030. And high-income countries by 2050.
In response, Samdech Techo Hun Sen mentioned the need for more capital, and today China has more capital and more branches in the world, so the Bank of China can help meet this need. Samdech Techo Hun Sen has invited the President of the Bank of China to visit Cambodia to review investment projects supported by the Bank of China.
Samdech Techo also said that he would like to see the signing of agreements on projects under the Belt and Road Political Project. In particular, Samdech assigned the Ministry of Economy and Finance, a state institution, to work with the Bank of China.
Samdech Techo also said that he was interested in President Xi Jinping's announcement to establish the 21st Century Silk Road, which is an important point for the development of member countries.
For Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that all of Cambodia's priorities, both public and private, are focused on four major areas: human resource development, water, roads and electricity, which are key areas for the Royal Government. For the development of human resources, Samdech Techo wants China to provide grants to participate in training human resources for infrastructure such as roads, bridges, airports and ports, etc. need a lot of capital from Chinese friends.
Samdech Techo requested the Bank of China to provide capital for companies that invest in training, infrastructure, as well as in the agricultural sector to promote the processing of Cambodia's agricultural products. Samdech Techo also emphasized that electricity is also important for Cambodia. In this regard, Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested the Bank of China to continue to support the construction of this power distribution network.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen accepted the invitation of the President of the Bank of China and found an appropriate time to visit the Bank's headquarters.
The President of the Bank of China thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for his suggestions. He also invited the Prime Minister to visit the Bank's headquarters when he attends the Belt and Road Initiative Summit in April to preside over the loan signing ceremony for projects under Belt and road politics, as well as the rectangular policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
This year, China will hold a one-way belt summit in April, and the Bank of China will sign a number of agreements to provide credit to companies involved in the Belt and Road policy project.
The Chinese side also thanked Samdech Techo for allowing him to meet in 2015, as he provided many recommendations for investment in Cambodia, and his bank also participated in many trainings for Cambodian officials. The Chinese representative hoped that he would pay a visit to Cambodia and pay a courtesy call on Samdech again.
