BEIJING (Reuters) - Chinese President Xi Jinping has announced about 4 billion yuan ($ 600 million) in development aid to Cambodia from 2019 to 2021. The President also announced to continue to import 400,000 tons of Cambodian rice to China in 2019 to help improve the lives of Cambodian farmers.
