On the afternoon of January 21, 2019, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with Chinese President Xi Jinping.
The President of China welcomed the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his delegation warmly and warmly. Many issues related to strengthening relations and cooperation between the two countries were discussed in depth.
After the discussion, in the evening of the same day, Mr. Xi Jinping will organize a food washing ceremony for Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the delegation.
It should be noted that Cambodia and China formally established diplomatic relations on July 19, 1958. On December 13, 2010, Cambodia-China bilateral cooperation was upgraded to a comprehensive strategic partnership. Cambodia and China have agreed to organize activities to celebrate the 60th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations in 2018.
In the new era of comprehensive cooperation, strategic partnership, the leaders of the two countries, Cambodia and China, exchanged visits, including the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom. Sihamoni paid 11 royal visits to the People's Republic of China from August 2005 to September and October 2018.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid 12 official visits and other working visits from 1999 to 2017, including 6 official visits and 6 working visits.
Separately, Chinese leaders have paid several official and official visits to Cambodia. Chinese President Xi Jinping paid an official visit to Cambodia from October 13 to 14, 2016, and Chinese Premier Li Keqiang paid an official visit to Cambodia on January 11, 2018.
During the official visit, the heads of government of Cambodia and China issued a joint statement and signed 19 documents on economic and technical cooperation, infrastructure, agriculture, energy and health.
On the trade volume between Cambodia and China, the leaders of the two countries aim to increase bilateral trade to 10 billion US dollars by 2023, while the current trade volume between the two countries is more than 5,577. Million US dollars. By 2020, the two sides aim to increase bilateral trade to 6 billion US dollars.
In terms of investment in 2018, Chinese investment in Cambodia amounted to 2.822 billion US dollars, ranking first among foreign investment. These include the textile, garment, hydropower, rice mills, agro-industrial, cotton and fertilizer industries, construction and coal plants.
In terms of tourism, more than 1.9 million Chinese tourists visit Cambodia. Chinese tourists to Cambodia could reach 3 million by 2020 There are currently 15 airlines, of which three Cambodian companies operate 155 direct flights from China to Cambodia per week.
Cambodia-China Belt and Road Cooperation Agreement Signing Point of the Bilateral Cooperation Plan for the Joint Establishment of the 21st Century Silk Road and Maritime Silk Road Cooperation May 2017. The Prime Minister attended the Belt and Road Forum for International Cooperation on May 14-15, 2017 in Beijing, China.
In terms of infrastructure construction, China has financed cooperation and grants from China to build 24 roads with a total length of 2,483 km at a cost of 1.437 million US dollars.
Seven major bridges have been completed, with a total length of 6,824 meters, with a budget of approximately US $ 216 million, and one bridge under construction, the 1,131-meter-long bridge across the Mekong River, Stung Trang-Kroch Chhna, with a budget of $ 57 million. .
A total of 3,295 km of projects funded by cooperation and grants of the Chinese friends have been completed and are under construction with a total value of 2.581 million US dollars.
On human resource development, the Chinese side has provided scholarships to Cambodian students, including 121 in 2016, 181 in 2017, 338 places in 2018. In particular, during the state visit of Chinese President Xi Jinping to Cambodia in 2016, he promised to provide scholarships to 500 Cambodian students in addition to the existing scholarships.
Currently, 1,644 Cambodian students are studying in China, of which 213 are studying in Beijing.
