After years of economic growth, the world's second-largest economy seems to be in decline. According to official data from the National Bureau of Statistics of China, economic growth in 2018 was China's slowest pace since 1990, down from 6.8 percent in 2017.
Chinese policymakers are expected to boost support for the national economy this year to avoid a further slowdown, but analysts say economic activity may not be stable forever. Until the summer, as this will put pressure on Beijing to try to find an agreement as soon as possible with Washington to end the trade war.
