Foreign direct investment (FDI) in the 56 countries participating in the One Belt One Road project will reach 15.6 billion US dollars in 2018, according to the Ministry of Commerce. 8.9 percent compared to the same period last year.
Revenue from investment in all projects contracted with foreign countries was 169 billion US dollars in 2018, up 0.3 percent from the same period last year. Of that, $ 89 billion came from investments in 63 countries participating in the One Belt One Road project, accounting for 52 percent of total investment turnover.
Han Yong, deputy director of the Ministry of Commerce's Department of Overseas Investment and Economic Cooperation, said most of the contracted projects were for transportation, general construction and power generation projects, which accounted for 66.5 percent of the total. All.
"These projects have greatly improved the infrastructure of the country that participates with us, as well as created 842,000 jobs for the people of that country, leading to better living conditions for the people," he said. "Better in those countries."
China has also made progress in building overseas economic cooperation zones. By the end of 2018, there were 933 companies eligible to do business in those areas, with a total investment of nearly 21 billion US dollars.
The companies paid a total of $ 2.3 billion in taxes and fees to the government of the country in which they operate, as well as employing 147,000 people. . (China's CCTV)
Letter to readers: "Politics is a dangerous culture that must be eradicated together"
(Phnom Penh): Today, I would like to draw the attention of Cambodians in general to see the most dangerous and worst culture of the opposition politicians in Cambodia led by Sam Rainsy, which has been actively and successfully implemented. That is the politics of opposition, to oppose, to destroy and to oppose in all directions, whether it is good or bad, whether it is for the benefit of the nation or the people, they only know how to oppose and always oppose.
For decades, the extremist opposition party led by Sam Rainsy has resorted to stagnant politics to the point of creating a well-defined political culture. Unlike the opposition parties in other countries, which compete for power by setting policies or promises to do better and more than the ruling party, Cambodia's opposition leaders never take the time to brainstorm policies. National level to compete with the ruling party.
Third, at home, opposition politicians try to mobilize more development aid to show that they can do better than the ruling party. At least they are willing to remain silent rather than talk because it is in their national interest. But strangely, in Cambodia, the main task of the opposition is to block development aid from entering the country. Opposition groups in Cambodia have even been shamelessly proud if any foreigner cuts off Cambodian aid.
Fourth, local opposition politicians often call on the people to remain calm when a crisis arises because they do not want to see the country fall into chaos and violence. Strangely, in Cambodia, opposition politicians led by Sam Rainsy continue to use politics to provoke anger and call on the people to rise up and protest until the violence erupts to make the country fall into chaos and seize control to seize the opportunity. Power.
That is why they do not leave the nation and its people at peace. Such opposition political views are considered by the world to be the most dangerous thing that politicians must absolutely avoid. But the most hated and hard-to-avoid politics has been used by the Cambodian opposition as its "Road Map" and has been very active and popular.
This is a great danger for our nation. Therefore, it is time for us to work together to eradicate this corrupt political culture from society by cracking down on opposition politicians led by Sam Rainsy.
