The founder of the watch brand "I run a lot of business, fail like eating, but I do not give up and give up the dream"!
(Phnom Penh): Usually, doing business always encounters obstacles, some businesses fail and so on. Apparently, like a young Cambodian, Mr. Set Pito, the founder of Mak Pu watch, a watch made by Cambodian children that is being sold on the international market, shared his experience of struggling in business, self-motivation and hard work.
"Many businesses that I used to run have collapsed, and despite the many failures, I am not discouraged, because every business that collapsed was my own hand, and this collapse is "Providing opportunities to learn about the causes of business failure."
The 29-year-old continued, "When I started my uncle's watch business. I always ask myself, what if I fail in this business again, what should I do? However, I still have the courage to try to start this new business. In particular, for each business, I do it myself, without relying on the family.
He stated that when starting a business, he never knew the feeling of success, because during that time, only business failed, this failure is like eating.
He added, "Looking at the opening of the watch business, I spent a lot of money and the production was very good because this watch has received a lot of support from international customers."
He said that with the opening of this new business, there is also the support and encouragement from the younger brother.
Currently, the brand's watch made by Cambodian children is gaining support from foreign customers in four countries, including the United Arab Emirates (Dubai), Korea, the United States and Japan, and plans to go to Brazil.
