Speaking to the media after the meeting on the confiscation of irregular Cambodian administrative documents held by foreigners and the application for immigration this morning, January 21, 2019, General Sok Phal confirmed that. "This work must be determined by Samdech Techo, that is, on June 30, 2019, the documents will be confiscated."
In fact, according to General Sok Phal, this meeting was held to remind the provincial administration, the provincial police commissioner, especially the immigration plan, to better understand in terms of efforts to implement this work more effectively according to what the Royal The government has set.
General Sok Phal claimed that he also faced some challenges because some foreigners did not understand clearly and some seemed to avoid cooperating with the authorities. However, the Ministry of Interior For example, the General Department of Immigration has instructed the relevant authorities to clearly explain to foreigners who hold these documents in the sense of respecting all Cambodian laws.
General Kiet Chantharith, Director General of the General Department of Immigration, Ministry of Interior, also revealed that so far (early 2019), the authorities and stakeholders have confiscated about 90% of the irregular Cambodian documents held by foreigners. There are more than 30,000 of them with 10 nationalities, of which 90% are Vietnamese.
General Kiet Chantharith stated, "So far, we have confiscated almost 90% of the documents, which are more than 30,000 copies, including family books, residence books, ID cards, birth certificates, passports and so on." "There are 10 ethnic groups, but most of them are about 90 percent Vietnamese."
In particular, for the deportation of foreigners who come to live or work without a permit, General Kirt Chantharith also stated that since 2014 until now, Cambodia has expelled all foreigners in 15,000 In 2018, there were more than 3,000 people, mostly from China and Vietnam.
Please be informed that the Royal Government of Cambodia in August 2017 issued a sub-decree on the cancellation and confiscation of irregular Cambodian administrative documents that foreigners are occupying. After receiving this sub-decree, it is observed that all relevant authorities have done this work diligently according to their respective skills.
Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Instructs District Governors to Pay Attention to Water Shortage
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, instructed four district governors to pay attention to reviewing the problem of water shortage because some districts have already experienced drought in the past, which makes people People lack water to use.
This was stated by the Provincial Governor on January 21, 2019 at the 2018 Annual Meeting within the framework of the Tonle Sap Poverty Alleviation and Small-Scale Agriculture Development Project Phase 2 at Kampong Cham Provincial Hall.
The provincial governor said that in the past, water shortages were encountered in four districts, including Kang Meas, Batheay, Chamkar Leu and Cheung Prey districts. Therefore, the district governor must review how many wells people can still use and how many wells have been damaged so that the provincial authorities can find measures to help them have enough water.
"The problem of water shortage that people have faced in the past, so far the district authorities must look into the reality, if they see that they are facing this water shortage, we must work together to find "The solution for the people before they face the drought, then we bring water to distribute to him is not good."
At the same time, Kouch Chamroeun urged the Kampong Cham Provincial Water Supply Authority to cooperate with its service providers to prepare the water supply system as soon as possible in rural areas where people are in need of clean water supply to use because of work. This is necessary to meet the needs of the people.
