(Beijing, China): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has urged Chinese bridge and road construction companies to speed up the construction of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, which has already studied and addressed the impact. Samdech Techo Prime Minister also asked the company to study in detail the project of the expressway from Phnom Penh to Bavet.
China Bridge and Road Corporation has contributed to the construction of many roads and bridges in Cambodia. The company will also build an expressway from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville, which is scheduled to open soon. In addition, the company also plans to build an expressway from Phnom Penh to Bavet on the Cambodian-Vietnamese border and to build Road 15-51, which connects Koh Kong to Pursat and Battambang.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, instructed the Chinese Bridge and Road Corporation to open the construction site of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway as soon as possible, while the relevant issues have already been resolved. For the road system to be connected from Phnom Penh to the expressway, it is urgent to study to build the connection.
Separately, the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway, Samdech Techo asked the company to study and talk more with relevant institutions because many companies have already studied on this road project.
The Ministry of Environment issued six notices on measures to prevent and prevent wildfires in protected areas and biodiversity corridors (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment on January 21, 2019 issued a notice on Measures to prevent and prevent wildfires in protected areas and biodiversity corridors.
According to the announcement, in order to prevent and prevent wildfires, the Ministry of Environment would like to instruct the sub-national administrative units of the Department of Environment, the competent authorities, including local communities and all stakeholders to implement the following six measures:
1: Prevent and advise to be very careful about the use of fire as a means to harvest non-timber forest products, forest fires, abduction and burning of grasslands.
2. Prevent the clearing, encroachment, burning of forests and flooded forests for other purposes, which are illegal activities and cause forest fires, flooded forests and spread to the homes of people, offices, sub-offices and physical infrastructure in and Around protected areas.
3: Be very careful to use fire as a way to burn waste in and around nature.
4: The Capital-Provincial Department of Environment shall instruct the relevant parties to implement appropriate technical measures that can ensure the safety of wildfires by extinguishing the fire as necessary before leaving the fire place.
6. To cooperate with the relevant sub-national administrations in banning access to forest and flooded forest lands in order to allow plants to regenerate naturally or to replant.
