(Phnom Penh): On the morning of January 21, 2019, Mr. Hem Darith, District Governor and Honorary President of the Red Cross Sub-Branch of Po Sen Chey District, together with the sub-branch team and other Khan Military Police officers, paid a courtesy call on Lt. Gen. Ek Meas Vuthy, an assistant military police officer in Po Sen Chey district, who is suffering from chronic diabetes, severe dehydration, is being treated at Preah Keto Mealea Hospital.
According to Toch Saran, the wife of Lieutenant Colonel Meas Vuthy, her husband of 58 years, a former military police officer in Por Sen Chey district, has been suffering from diabetes for more than two years.
With this, his family and children tried to take him to the hospital for treatment, but in recent months, his condition worsened, so he decided to bring him to Preah Keto Mealea Hospital last Saturday because he was in Military framework.
According to the doctor, his condition has improved a bit, but it is not yet possible to set a date for him to return home, as doctors are still monitoring him.
Mr. Hem Darith, on behalf of the Board of Governors and the working group of the Red Cross Sub-Branch of Po Sen Chey District, expressed his sympathy to Mr. Meas Vuthy and encouraged him to continue to try to take care of his health, especially to follow the advice of doctors who hope that his disease. He will soon recover and return to normal service to the local people.
With this, on behalf of the Board of Governors, the Gendarmerie and the working group of the Red Cross Sub-Branch of Po Sen Chey District will always be close to him and will always support, encourage and never abandon any officer.
