(Phnom Penh): In a health seminar on "How to identify counterfeit drugs", Dr. Em Vuthy, Assistant Chairman of the Anti-Counterfeit Products Committee, said that in order to identify counterfeit drugs, we need to understand what drugs and counterfeit drugs are. What should we do about counterfeit medicine and what are the effects on our health?
He said that medicine refers to one or more substances with two sources: biochemicals, microbial products, plant compounds for use in the prevention or treatment of human diseases or medical research, medicine or diagnosis, modification or Supports the function of organs.
For counterfeit medicine refers to a type of drug that does not have the active ingredient or contains the wrong active ingredient according to the formula specified on the label or contains insufficiently active substance according to the label limit or has the packaging. Another drug that is a real drug or manufactured and packaged without a license from the Ministry of Health.
He stated that to identify counterfeit medicine, there are three methods: 1: Preliminary analysis or physical examination (see, smell, hear from consumers), 2: Manufacturing - Import - Export, 3: Analyze in the national laboratory. - International.
Speaking to about 500 participants in the hall of the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center (CJCC) on January 20, 2019, President of the Cambodia-Japan Business and Investment Association (CJBI), Mr. Ieng Sotheara, who was the speaker and organizer of this workshop. Emphasize that seeing the risks to citizens in the use of drugs, because no one can avoid treatment, today's workshop was organized.
Mr. Ieng Sotheara added, “The main purpose is to show participants what counterfeit medicine is and to be careful. "Moreover, I want to show all sellers, manufacturers and consumers of medicine understand the value of virtue, truth and morality for the happiness of themselves, families and society as a whole."
He hopes that all participants will be able to understand how to identify counterfeit drugs, as well as be able to share this knowledge with relatives, friends and relatives to participate in the protection and maintenance of health.
