According to Syrian state media, the Israeli military has launched airstrikes using Lebanese airspace and the Israeli-controlled Galilee region. But at the same time, the Syrian air force's missile defense system responded immediately by intercepting and destroying several of these missiles over Damascus airspace.
On Monday morning, the Israeli military acknowledged airstrikes on several Iranian bases near Damascus, with Syria warning to stop attacks on Israeli forces and territory.
This is the second airstrike on Damascus in the last 24 hours, since last Sunday when the Israeli military fired a large number of missiles at several locations in Syria. Syrian media claim that the attack was prevented by its missile system in time.
Israel launches massive airstrikes on Iranian bases in Syria
JERUSALEM (Reuters) - The Israeli military has said it has launched airstrikes on Iranian militant positions in Syria, warning the Damascus government to stop attacking Israeli forces and territory. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Monday, January 21, 2019.
"We have launched air strikes on Iranian Quds militants on Syrian territory ... and we have also warned Syrian government forces," the Israeli military said in a statement issued Monday morning. "To stop attacks against the Israeli military and territory." The Israeli military did not provide further details, but Syrian media reported that the attack took place near Damascus.
This is not the first time the Israeli military has launched an attack on an Iranian military base on Syrian soil, just days after Tel Aviv claimed an air defense missile system. It intercepted a missile fired from Syrian territory on Sunday.
