Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh Leads a Delegation to Celebrate the 70th Anniversary of the Lao People's Army in Vientiane
(Laos): At the invitation of the Minister of National Defense of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, on January 20, 2019, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, paid an official and friendly visit to Cambodia. The celebration of the 70th anniversary of the founding of the Lao People's Army was held in Vientiane.
Senior officials accompanying Prince Tea Banh included General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander and Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, General Nem Sovath, Director General of the General Department of Politics and Foreign Affairs, and General Tea Vinh, Chief of Staff. Deputy Commander and Commander of the Navy, General Soeng Samnang, Deputy Commander and Commander of the Air Force, as well as officers in the Ministry of National Defense.
The celebration of the 70th anniversary of the founding of the Lao People's Army was also attended by a delegation from the Ministry of Defense from Vietnam, Thailand, the Union of Myanmar, China and the military delegation from the Russian Federation and leaders at all levels. Class of the Lao People's Democratic Republic.
On that occasion, Mr. Bunyang Volak, Secretary General of the Central Committee of the Party of the President of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, stated that 70 years ago, on January 20, 1949, the Lao People's Liberation Army, now the Lao People's Army, was formed. In a standing area in Houaphanh province, President Kaison Phumvihan announced the establishment, directing and directing.
He stated that after the establishment of the Lao Army, Issarak was soon confronted with many enemies, such as the economy, the armed forces, the weapons, but due to the strong patriotic spirit and the continuation of the unyielding tradition of the ancestors and the Lao people. With the wholehearted support of the people of Laos, the people as well as the socialist country of Laos, the Lao army fought valiantly and won a series of victories.
On the occasion of the celebration of the 70th anniversary of the founding of the Lao People's Army on behalf of the ruling party of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, Mr. Bun Yang Vlakchit expressed his deepest gratitude to the veterans of the Lao People's Army. Families who sacrificed their lives for the independence, freedom and happiness of the Lao people.
