Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs Releases Official Results of the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting in Chiang Mai, Thailand
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on January 20, 2019 issued a press release on the official results of the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting in Chiang Mai, Thailand, chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon. Foreigners in Cambodia also participated in that work.
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting was held on 17-18 January 2019 in Chiang Mai to discuss key issues related to the follow-up to the outcome of the 33rd ASEAN Summit and related summits. In particular, the process of building the ASEAN Community, ASEAN relations with external partners and the exchange of views on regional and international issues.
During the meeting, the Thai Foreign Minister in charge of ASEAN chaired the meeting on Thailand's priorities as chair of ASEAN in 2019 under the theme "Promoting Partnership for Sustainability". Regarding the building of the ASEAN Community, the Ministers had a fruitful discussion on the implementation of the ASEAN Community Vision 2025, in particular the detailed plan for the ASEAN Security-Political Community, ASEAN Integration, ASEAN Development Gap and ASEAN Connectivity.
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers stressed the need to further strengthen the ASEAN Middle East and ASEAN's leading role in the emerging regional model and relations with the outside world. The ASEAN Foreign Ministers acknowledged the growing competition between major powers in the region and the potential impact on the ASEAN Middle East.
Regarding the strengthening of the complement between the ASEAN Vision 2025 and the UN Agenda 2030 for Sustainable Development, the Cambodian Head of Mission believes that the strength of building the ASEAN Community depends on the expansion of the efforts of member countries. All ASEAN in adapting national development policies in line with regional and global development agendas to benefit from each other's complementary development.
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers acknowledged the importance of developing a common ASEAN approach to the Indo-Pacific concept based on key principles, including environment, transparency and complementarity. The Ministers also decided for the ASEAN Senior Officials to further discuss this concept.
