Ministry of Public Works Educates and Disseminates Traffic Risk Factors to People Living Along Roads in Svay Vieng Province
(Svay Vieng): Seeing the challenges of traffic accidents, the Road Construction Unit of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, under a loan from the Asian Development Bank, organized education and dissemination on traffic risk factors to people living along the road. Of the road improvement project in Romeas Hek district, Romduol district, within a distance of 62 kilometers, passing through 10 communes and 35 villages of Svay Rieng province.
According to officials involved in the education, human resource development, people's well-being and transportation are central to Cambodia's development process. Following the guidance of the leadership of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, education and outreach play an important role in preventing and reducing traffic accidents, especially farmers and young people, students who are at risk of road accidents.
A farmer living in Prey Keav village, Kampong Chak commune, said that now that the road has been paved, she seems to be very worried about road accidents. Today, she participated in road safety education. It's a pleasure to know the causes of traffic accidents and to know some safe ways to travel on the road.
She added that the teacher talked about speed and speed, this is very true, because after the road was paved, the driver drove so fast that when he had to cross the road once, he almost did not dare to cross. She also urged drivers to respect the law on road traffic and not to drive fast and love their own lives and the lives of other road users.
