Senior CPP official visits Sangkum Thmei district, Preah Vihear province: For the past 40 years, Cambodia has changed from a pile of ashes to a proud one
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Chan Nonvitya, Deputy Chairman of the Central Working Group for Sangkum Thmey District, Preah Vihear Province, this morning, January 20, 2019, participated in the celebration of the 40th anniversary of the 7th of January Victory Day.
Also present were Mr. Samleang Try, Provincial Working Group Chairman, Working Group Deputy Chairman, Working Group Members, as well as government officials, local authorities, the Armed Forces, students and about 600 people.
After listening to the speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, Mr. Chan Nonvitya said that January 7 is the second birthday of the Cambodian people, which is a historical fact that no one or force. Can not be tampered with or destroyed.
He said that on January 7, 1979, things were as they are today, and that January 7 was born of the sacrifice of fresh flesh, blood and courage of the Cambodian military leaders, with the support of the Vietnamese army. Success on the genocidal regime, so may the spirit of January 7 remain immortal.
He added that the past 40 years have been 40 years of unity, heroism and victory, and the CPP's efforts over the past 40 years have transformed the motherland of Cambodia from a pile of ashes to a revival and a proud growth. The most strengthened foundation for us to achieve the lofty goal is an independent, peaceful, free, neutral, democratic and progressive Cambodia.
At the same time, he also called on all people to work together to maintain the peace that is most difficult to find today to be stable and sustainable for the long term.
