This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen pays a visit to China as China prepares to receive the 6th official visit
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Sunday, January 20, 2019, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will lead a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia. This is the sixth official visit to China after 34 years as Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In addition to the above meeting, Samdech Techo PM will receive separate courtesy calls by His Excellency Minister Song Tao, Director of the International Relations Department of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and Lok Chumteav Ku Xiaolian, President of the China-Cambodia Friendship Association and leaders. Four more businesses from the Bank of China, the China Road and Bridge Corporation, the China Engineering and Steel Corporation and the Huang Neng Group.
Senior Cambodian officials who will accompany Samdech Techo include Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and other senior government officials. And business leaders of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Winthean expressed hope that Hun Sen's current visit to China will further deepen political trust between the two countries and pragmatic cooperation between the two countries. Both countries will take it to a new level.
"We will strengthen cooperation in the field of culture and establish cooperation in law enforcement of the two countries to improve all-round strategic cooperation between China and Cambodia," he said. "
Mr. Wang Vin Thean also stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit will focus on four tasks, including:
First. Deepen political trust between the two countries. In particular, the two sides will increase connectivity to exchange experiences on governance in the interests of mutual benefit.
Second. Strengthen trade cooperation between the two countries and increase connectivity through the cooperation of the Belt and Road and the Rectangular Strategy of Cambodia to strengthen and expand practical cooperation in the fields of infrastructure, trade, investment, agriculture, etc. To provide greater benefits for both our countries and bring more happiness to the people of both countries.
Third. Expand cultural exchanges between the two countries, increase cooperation on youth issues, tourism, culture, etc. to increase mutual understanding between the people of the two countries to improve communication.
Fourth. Increase law enforcement cooperation between the two countries to combat transnational crime, as well as some illegal gambling, human trafficking, as well as telecommunications and drug trafficking. Etc. to ensure strong social development, as well as strengthen China-Cambodia bilateral relations, including politics, the belt and the road.
Please note that although Cambodia and China have a long history together and Samdech Techo Hun Sen has been the Prime Minister for 34 years, but so far Samdech Techo has just paid an official visit to the country. China only 6 times.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid his first visit in February 1999. Starting from this first relationship, the Chinese government has worked closely with Samdech Techo Hun Sen to expand and strengthen the relationship to the present.
In addition to these six official visits, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has also visited China several times to attend various meetings and forums held in China.
