6. The two sides also agreed to support each other in organizing cultural events to promote tourism cooperation.
Mr. Sok Sopheak made the remarks at a press conference on the Ministry of Commerce's response to the imposition of import duties on Cambodian rice, with the participation of several local journalists. Office of the Ministry of Commerce on the afternoon of January 18, 2019.
He said that according to the calculation of the amount of rice that Cambodia exported to Europe in 2018, Cambodia will lose about $ 50 million in tax revenue. But not all Cambodian rice is taxed.
"In terms of the impact, if they are involved, we have to pay that tax, about $ 50 million a year, based on the figures that we export to Europe of more than 260,000 tons," he said. "But not all Cambodian rice is taxed, only four codes."
He said that in addition to these four codes, other types of Cambodian rice, such as brown rice, can be exported with the same tariff preferences. He also expressed concern that if the situation remained the same, farmers' rice prices would fall as exporters had to lower their purchase prices to reduce costs.
Please be informed that Cambodia exported nearly 270,000 tons of rice to Europe, equivalent to 42.98 percent of the total exported 620,000 tons.
