(Siem Reap): Mr. Kong Vibol, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, chaired a meeting to discuss and inspect the work with the management and tax officials of the Siem Reap Provincial Tax Branch on Friday afternoon, January 18, 2019. At Siem Reap Tax Branch.
The meeting was also attended by Mr. Him Bunthoeun, Director of Finance and Personnel Department, Mr. Lim De Lux, Director of Information Technology Department, Mr. Chao Mao Mony, Branch Manager and Siem Reap Provincial Tax Branch Manager, as well as relevant tax officials.
The agenda of this meeting and discussion focused on the inspection and strengthening of the work of the Siem Reap Tax Branch, especially on 1: the issuance of administrative letters that require a bar code number from the data management system of the General Department. Proper taxation, 2: Proper tax audit in accordance with the procedure and 3: Reduce and eliminate congestion of application documents, especially documents for transfer of ownership or possession of real estate.
The Royal Government delegate, who chaired the meeting, also expressed his support and appreciation for the results of the efforts of the Siem Reap Provincial Tax Branch, which collected 128% of the tax revenue compared to the revenue plan for 2018, which is a contribution to the achievements of the General. The tax department achieved 114.27% of the tax revenue collection compared to the revenue plan for 2018.
He also highlighted the efforts of the tax administration to reform and modernize the tax administration from year to year in accordance with the policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the strengthening of good governance.
He also emphasized that the purpose of this meeting to discuss and review the work is to ensure the provision of services to taxpayers effectively, efficiently, transparently, as well as to provide convenience and reliability in providing services to taxpayers and Reminded tax officials to implement in accordance with the five work methods for daily practice, including "mirroring, bathing, scrubbing, treatment and surgery."
He thanked and instructed all the leaders and civil servants of Siem Reap to be present today to strengthen the work and solidarity between the leaders and officials in order to ensure transparency, efficiency, efficiency in tax collection and delivery. Services for taxpayers in Siem Reap.
