CamControl officers take mobile test vehicles to inspect food items at 5 markets in Chbar Ampov district and found some beans containing pesticide residues
(Phnom Penh): In addition to the regular inspection of goods in the market every day to strengthen the protection of people's welfare, on January 18, 2019, Camcontrol Phnom Penh International Port in cooperation with officials of the Department of Commerce brought a mobile test vehicle Inspected food products in 5 markets, including: Chbar Ampov Central Market, Chbar Ampov Vegetable Market, Prek Pra Market, Champouk Kaek Market and Prek Eang Market.
The team took 95 samples of food products and analyzed them. As a result, 5 kg of soybeans with pesticide residues were confiscated and destroyed by our officers, requiring the contractor to stop using the pesticides. Exterminate and store technically for a period of time before collecting for sale.
He said that the work of surveying and monitoring in the market is to continue and strengthen more active activities to increase trust and protect the well-being of people across the country, contribute to reducing people's poverty by helping to prevent To avoid diseases caused by eating contaminated food and toxic chemicals in it.
In this operation, CamControl officers explained and instructed the traders to display the products properly, maintain hygiene, avoid mixing banned chemicals in food, purchase goods for resale, and know the source and name clearly. Distribute production invoices and contact telephone numbers, as well as explain to citizens and traders how to check the date of manufacture and the date (expiration date).
President of the Cambodian Dental Association: The medical sector in Cambodia is currently evolving.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Kao Hok Sim, President of the Cambodian Dental Association, said that currently the medical sector in Cambodia is evolving to grow more and more day by day.
This statement was made by the President of the Dental Association during the 19th Dental Conference and Exhibition of the Dental Association of Cambodia on the morning of January 18, 2019, with the participation of Dr. Oeun Borarath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, including Many dentists.
According to the president of the association, today, the Cambodian Dental Association has organized the 9th Dental Exhibition, which is organized to train more dentists and dental students, both previous and later generations.
"Currently, the field of dentistry is growing rapidly from day to day, and in order to keep up with the field of dentistry in the world, the association always organizes this dental exhibition every year," she said.
She added that currently the evolution of the field of dentistry in Cambodia is also evolving more strongly compared to 10 years ago and now 10 years ago, the field is almost unnamed, but now the field of dentistry is very prominent. .
According to Dr. Oeun Borarath, the Dental Association of Cambodia has been implementing a good education and training to sustain dentists every year for dentists in Phnom Penh as well as from other provinces of Cambodia.
