(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Road Safety (NCRC), on January 18, 2019, issued eight guidelines. Key points to continue to promote the work of the National Road Safety Committee in 2019 to achieve even better.
The introduction of the above eight guidelines was made on the occasion that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng presided over the meeting to review the work of road traffic safety in 2018 and work direction in 2019, which was held at the office. Ministry of Interior on the afternoon of January 18, 2019.
Samdech Sar Kheng stated that in order to further promote the work of the National Road Safety Committee in 2019 to achieve better, please request the national and capital-provincial leadership mechanisms to continue to promote the implementation of the direction. Set forth in the report and strive to address challenges in a sustainable, transparent, efficient and accountable manner in a spirit of commitment and responsibility.
Samdech Krala Hom added that with this, please pay more attention to some important issues as follows:
* First, to strengthen the road safety control mechanism at all levels, continue to cooperate with all relevant ministries and institutions, and encourage the participation of all circles in maintaining road traffic safety by focusing on implementing measures. The five are legal education, law enforcement, road engineering, emergency and road safety promotion.
* Second, the Capital and Provincial Road Safety Sub-Committee must make more efforts to reform the leadership and work mechanism to be effective in accordance with the changing situation of the current road traffic situation and in the future, especially for local Increase in accidents and casualties from road accidents in 2018, such as Phnom Penh, Kandal, Sihanoukville and other provinces where the accident figures are still high.
