Russia: 23 foreign planes a week fly near the Russian border to spy ...
Russia has spotted 23 foreign reconnaissance planes flying near its border over the past week. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua in the morning of Friday, January 18, 2019.
According to an official statement from the Russian Defense Ministry, the Russian planes were immediately sent to intercept the foreign planes to prevent them from invading its airspace. Foreign reconnaissance planes have frequently flown near the Russian border, while Moscow has repeatedly accused the United States and NATO of spying.
Last November, the US Navy's EP-3E Aries was intercepted by Russian warplanes over the Black Sea. The United States claimed that its aircraft were flying over international airspace and considered the interception of Russian planes dangerous, but the Russian Foreign Ministry responded that US planes were flying near Russian airspace and Su-27 fighter jets. Flying to intercept at a safe distance.
