Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia: Sub-decree to encourage taxation on the securities sector of the Royal Government will attract more investors in this sector!
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, recently issued a sub-decree on tax incentives in the securities sector. With the issuance of the Royal Government's tax incentive sub-decree, Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, expressed optimism that it will attract more investors from other companies into the sector.
Mr. Sou Socheat made this remark when he was invited to participate in the listed company forum under the theme "Sustainable Business Management Strategy" held on January 17, 2018.
Mr. Sou Socheat said, "I am very optimistic about the Royal Government's incentive sub-decree because it is time to give investors the opportunity to invest in the Cambodian securities sector better than leaving cash in the bank."
He added that this is the best news from the Royal Government of Cambodia, which has approved the sub-decree on tax incentives, this sub-decree continues to encourage additional income tax by reducing this tax for 50 years for 50 years with companies registered in the market. Securities of Cambodia, starting from 2019 onwards, for the listing is not yet deadline, they do not receive this incentive.
He said that in order for companies not to miss out on entering the securities sector while they are receiving incentives over the next three years, the Securities and Exchange Commission will work hard to encourage companies to look into the potential to move in this area.
He said that in addition to encouraging tax breaks of 50 percent of income, the sub-decree also provides incentives to companies with certain tax issues.
