Mr. Wang Vinthean said this in a press conference with Cambodian and Chinese journalists who came to work in Cambodia on January 16, 2019.
"China and Cambodia have a good tradition of" we always support each other and help each other, "Wang said. China has always supported the socio-economic development of Cambodia and also improved the living standards of the Cambodian people as much as possible.
Answering the question asked by the media, "What has China done to help improve the lives of Cambodians?" And what is the main point of the next step? ” The Chinese ambassador replied, "We are still increasing investment in Cambodia to create more jobs for Cambodia."
He said that now China has become Cambodia's largest trading partner by 2018, Chinese companies have invested in Cambodia with a total capital of more than 20 billion US dollars, and 70 percent Chinese companies are manufacturers of clothing and footwear. These companies employ hundreds of thousands of Cambodians. Especially in Sihanoukville, the special economic zone employs about 22,000 people.
Wang added that China has expanded its investment in the electricity sector in Cambodia to address the shortage of electricity for Cambodians. Chinese companies have now installed more than 8,000 kilometers of power lines, and 80 percent of Cambodia's electricity generation is made by Chinese companies. This electricity has helped reduce the cost of the company's production and reduce the cost of electricity use of the people of Cambodia.
Mr. Wang Vin Thean emphasized, “When I accompanied Samdech Techo Hun Sen to attend the inauguration ceremony of the Lower Sesan 2 hydropower plant in Stung Treng province, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced that he would reduce the price of electricity for the people. This is to provide more benefits for the people of Cambodia.
He said the Chinese government and people have expanded aid to Cambodia to improve the lives of Cambodians, especially Chinese companies have provided grants as well as some concessional loans to build more than 3,000 kilometers of roads. Many bridges and irrigation projects are about 45.6 million hectares to provide irrigation to people's crops.
Now, the construction of the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital has started, and the hospital in Tbong Khmum province will start construction soon, and China has built many rural roads as well as dug wells to build schools. Original.
According to Wang Vinthean, Cambodia and China need to do more priority work to help people, such as:
* First, we need to better plan, especially to use the current cooperation mechanism to promote more trade and investment between China and Cambodia to make the Cambodian economy stronger and improve the livelihood of the country. Citizens.
* Second, we need to provide more development to rural areas, especially the construction of infrastructure in rural areas, such as the construction of hospitals, schools, which is a real benefit to the people.
* Third, we must urgently address all the problems of the Cambodian people to ensure that Chinese aid has helped the rural people. Meanchey District Governor Intervenes to Hand over Two Female Twins to Cambodian Children's Fund for Accommodation and Education
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pich Keo Mony, Governor of Meanchey District and Mr. Seng Sanh, Chief of Stung Meanchey I Commune, along with many other working groups, on January 17, 2019, intervened and handed over two female twins. Cambodian Children's Fund to get accommodation and study at Cambodian Children's Fund (Scotland).
According to the authorities, the twin girls who did not go to school were asked by the Cambodian Children's Fund (Scotland) to help them get an education. On the same day, the twin girls were handed over to the organization so that the two children could go to school together.
The reason the twins did not go to school was because their parents' parents divorced because their father was a drug addict and they were in a correctional center. The two children live with Um, but Um is unable to raise them, so they decided to ask the local authority in Sangkat Meanchey 1 to contact the organization to help the two twin brothers and sisters so that they can go to school like them.
At the same time, Mr. Pich Keo Mony also inspected the disputed land of two families living in Russey village, Sangkat Stung Meanchey I, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh. Kampong Preah temple is the oldest of the temples in Kampong Chhnang province
(Kampong Chhnang): To travel to Kampong Preah temple, we have to pass through Kampong Chhnang provincial town along National Road 5 and enter the dirt road for a distance of 44 kilometers, taking about 1 hour and 30 minutes. It is possible to travel by water, taking a ferry from Phsar Krom port for more than 2 hours.
Kampong Preah Temple is a temple located in Kampong Preah Village, Chhnuk Trou Commune, Boribo District, with a total distance of 44 kilometers from Kampong Chhnang Provincial Town. This temple is the oldest of the temples in Kampong Chhnang province.
According to Khmer history books, the temple of Kampong Preah was built in the 8th century during the reign of Queen Chey Tevy. This temple is in the style of Kampong Preah before the Angkorian era.
In the rainy season, when the floodwaters surround the hills of the temple, if we look at the distance in front of the entrance of the temple, we will see a quiet parliament, which indicates that these two temples are rarely visited and are regularly preserved. No. Around the temple as well as the hill of the temple is rich in forest.
If we enter through the gate of the pagoda about 30 meters to the north, we will see a view of an oil well in the northwest of the two temples, which are now being destroyed by debris, leaves, landslides and other debris that people take. To prevent the danger to their children, and on the other hand, due to natural factors, landslides near the well, we can not see exactly.
Near the well, we see a stone pillar made of stone with a knuckle according to the type of penis. This temple was built by our Khmer ancestors to dedicate to the deity in the Hindu way. The pedestal and the penis were built as offerings and as a symbol of victory in the 7th and 8th centuries.
From the oil well site, about 30 meters, we will reach the front of both temples, which are the most interesting. The two temples face north toward the Tonle Sap, just over a kilometer away. This temple is located in the area managed by Wat Kampong Preah, with an area of 10,000 square meters, a public property built of brick and sandstone.
Prasat Srey is 6 by 5 meters in size, 10 meters high, has 3 false doors for 3 corners and 1 door to enter the temple facing north. At every gate on the four pillars of diamonds, vivid carvings, both flower arrangements and ornaments, prove that the richness has a devotional effect on Brahmanism and belief in His work is dedicated to the ancestors of that era.
It can be concluded that at that time, civilization, tradition, and tradition of worship were matriarchal, hence we see that Prasat Srey is bigger and taller and more beautiful than Prasat Pros next door. As for Prasat Pros, which is about 3 meters away from Prasat Srey, we can see that there is a difference with Prasat Srey in terms of size and height, as well as other designs that are not interesting.
The temple is 4 by 4 meters in size and more than 5 meters high. The entrance is very dilapidated. At the top of the temple, there is a conical roof made of hibiscus wood as a temporary cover to prevent rainwater from damaging the temple.
Prasat Pros is not older than Prasat Srey, it was built at the same time as Prasat Srey, but Prasat Srey is still stronger. The construction of this temple is made of brick and sandstone like Prasat Srey. According to the actual examination of the two temples, the temple that will be most vulnerable is Prasat Pros, while it is currently in a very dilapidated state.
