Next week, Cambodian diplomat leads a delegation to the ASEAN-EU Foreign Ministers' Meeting in Belgium
(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, will lead a delegation to attend the ASEAN-EU Foreign Ministers' Meeting to be held in Brussels, Belgium on January 21, 2019. . This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
According to the statement, during the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting, the European Union and its counterparts will discuss a number of areas of cooperation of common interest to achieve a common goal of regional integration of peace, stability and prosperity.
During his stay in Brussels, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon is scheduled to hold bilateral meetings with His Excellency Didier Render, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and European Affairs of Belgium, Cecilia Malstrom, EU Trade Commissioner and other heads of delegations. .
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the European Union became an ASEAN dialogue partner in 1977, and since then relations between the two regions have reached a high level, covering a wide range of areas of cooperation, including politics, economy and trade. Social activities and connections. Based on these decades-long partnership, many agreements have been signed, laying a solid foundation for the future direction of the two regions.
The following is a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs: The Ministry of Commerce's press conference in response to the European case of imposing tariffs on Cambodian rice has been postponed
(Phnom Penh): The press conference organized by the Ministry of Commerce on the action of the Ministry of Commerce in response to the import tax on Cambodian rice to be held at 4 pm on January 17, 2019 has been postponed. On January 18, 2019, tomorrow.
Speaking to reporters waiting to cover the conference, Seang Thai, a spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, confirmed that the ministry had just received a file from the European Commission regarding the decision to impose tariffs on rice imports. Cambodia and Myanmar, so the Ministry has not yet fully understood this content.
Mr. Seang Thai added that therefore, the Ministry asked not to hold a press conference in response to the case of Europe imposing import duties on Cambodian rice today, but postponed to 2:30 pm on January 18, 2019 tomorrow. Back.
Please be informed that the conference of the Ministry of Commerce took place after the European Commission issued a statement stating that the community will start taxing rice imports from Cambodia and Myanmar, which are exported to EU member states. 28 countries for 3 years from 2019-2021.
