She stressed that the increasing demand for rice from people around the world requires the Institute to increase activities such as research, new technologies, development strategies and cooperation with all relevant partners to increase rice production productivity in line with the mechanism. Modernize agriculture to ensure food security and contribute to the family economy and poverty reduction.
On that occasion, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia and himself, the Minister thanked the Institute for its important role in the development of the rice sector in Cambodia, and he hopes and believes that the Institute will continue to help. The Royal Government is working to achieve its vision of transforming the country into a high middle-income country by 2030.
