He said that the achievements achieved through training on the roles, duties and ethics of Khmer priests, which shows that always pay attention to the implementation of all means to ensure the development and preservation of the beautiful cultural heritage of the nation. The work that has been done is to preserve and develop the traditions, customs, culture, civilization and long-term unity of the Khmer ancestors.
All these resources and heritage are necessary and invaluable social capital for building a Cambodian society with strong interconnected cells, people with a deep knowledge of the culture, traditions and customs of the nation. They live a dignified, peaceful, harmonious and sustainable and prosperous life.
He understands that the achievements that will come out of this training are not only proud and beneficial only for the trainees, but also the pride of the whole society, by gaining more knowledgeable archbishop resources. Comply with the ancient rules for contributing and promoting the process of social development by maintaining a beautiful culture and national identity.
