(Phnom Penh): The European Union (EU) has issued a statement stating that it will start taxing rice imports from Cambodia and Myanmar to 28 EU member states for three years. From 2019 to 2021.
The tariff on Cambodian rice comes as Europe finds that Cambodian and Myanmar rice imported into Europe has hurt their rice producers following complaints from Italy and Spain.
Despite this decision, Cambodian exporters claim that Cambodian rice can still be exported in various ways, although the possibility of exporting to Europe may not be as large as before.
Mr. Song Saran believes that European tariffs are too high, making it difficult for some Cambodian rice varieties to compete. Europe should divide this tax according to the type of rice, because Cambodia also has a lot of fragrant rice that is exported to Europe.
Recently, the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, announced the introduction of internal economic reforms by reducing formal and informal expenditures to enable businesses to better compete in the export market. Without preferential tariffs, Cambodia can still export. Without preferential tariffs, Cambodia will not die.
Please be informed that the European Union is an important market for Cambodian rice in 2018, Cambodia exported nearly 300,000 tons of rice to Europe, equivalent to 42.98 percent of the total exported 620,000 tons.
