Interview with Chinese Ambassador on Cambodia-China Relations and Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Visit to China This Weekend
(Phnom Penh) - Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Vinthean, who has just completed his mission, held a press conference with Cambodian and Chinese journalists working in Cambodia on January 16, 2019.
The press conference focused on the 60-year relationship between Cambodia and China, as well as the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to China from January 20 to 23, 2019.
Responding to questions from Cambodian and Chinese journalists, Wang Winthean outlined the Chinese government's clear position on promoting cooperation and relations with Cambodia, as well as improving the lives of Cambodians by encouraging investors. Cambodia continues to provide concessional assistance and financing for the construction of infrastructure, roads, bridges, schools, hospitals and human resource training.
For Samdech Techo Hun Sen's four-day visit to China, Wang Winthean affirmed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and four top Chinese leaders, including: Chinese President Xi Jinping, President Li Keqiang Chinese Minister, Speaker of the National People's Congress and Chairman of the Chinese Consultative Assembly
The Ambassador expressed strong belief that Samdech Techo's visit to China will take Cambodia-China relations to a new level, especially to bring many fruitful benefits for the people of both countries.
The following is the confirmation of the Chinese Ambassador through questions from Cambodian and Chinese journalists:
Q: How do you evaluate the relationship between Cambodia and China? What do you think are the special features of the current Cambodian-Chinese relationship?
Mr. Wang Winthean: 2018 is the 60th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Cambodia. Since the establishment of diplomatic ties 60 years ago, China and Cambodia have always helped each other and shared their condolences. Most.
We have provided mutual benefits in the field of trade, especially the achievements of practical cooperation in all fields have also been fruitful. China has now become the largest source of investment in Cambodia and the largest trading partner and also Cambodia's largest development partner.
China and Cambodia have excellent cooperation within the framework of East Asia Cooperation, as well as the Lancang-Mekong Cooperation and the United Nations. And we have maintained common interests between the two countries, as well as developing countries and ASEAN member countries.
Q: What is the meaning and strategy of building a community with the same destiny between China and Cambodia?
The other is useful for us to build a common destiny community between China and ASEAN. Because China-Cambodia bilateral relations are unique in China's diplomatic policy, the two countries have always adhered to the "5 B" principle of peaceful coexistence, and we have always respected each other. Mutual respect for each other, which can become a model for building new forms of international relations.
Building a community of one destiny is the initiative of His Excellency Xi Jinping and is an important part of China's unique socialism of the new era. His Excellency Xi Jinping said that to build a community of one destiny in Asia, we must first build a community of one destiny in neighboring countries, and we must build this community with friends like Cambodia and Laos.
Q: What are the new trends in business and trade cooperation between China and Cambodia and what are the challenges? As for future cooperation mechanisms and projects, in what areas will the Chinese side continue to promote trade? What will be the future of Chinese investment in Cambodia?
Mr. Wang Vinthean: We know that Cambodia now has a policy to strengthen and expand to attract foreign investment, and now Cambodia will become an important destination for Chinese investment. I know that the Royal Government of Cambodia has announced that it will promote national development in the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy and will continue to promote globalization as well as globalization, requiring more human resources and more infrastructure.
China encourages and supports more Chinese companies to invest in Cambodia. We look forward to continuing to work with Cambodia to further strengthen trade and development cooperation, especially in areas such as infrastructure, electricity, agriculture, tourism, special economic zones, telecommunications, China will continue to invest more to help. To the economic development of Cambodia.
Major projects now include the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, the new airport in Siem Reap, the new airport in Phnom Penh, as well as the special economic zone in Sihanoukville. These are all important projects under the political framework, the belt and the road, which both countries will continue to promote these projects for the better.
Q: What has China done to help improve the lives of Cambodians? And what is the main point of the next step?
We have expanded our assistance to Cambodia to improve the lives of Cambodians, especially Chinese companies, which have provided grants as well as some concessional loans to build more than 3,000 kilometers of roads and also built many bridges and irrigation projects. There is also a large area of about 45.6 thousand hectares to provide irrigation to people's crops.
Now, the construction of the Sino-Cambodian Friendship Hospital has started, and the hospital in Tbong Khmum province will start construction in the near future, and China has also built many rural roads, as well as digging wells and building schools. .
Q: What will China do to further strengthen the relationship between the people of the two countries as well as increase the Cambodian people's understanding of China?
China also supported the construction of the Confucius Institute. To date, the Confucius Institute in Cambodia has more than 40 classrooms. And there are some Chinese teachers who go to teach Chinese in government institutions and get full support.
We also have many artifacts experts from China helping to restore artifacts in Cambodia, aiding the cultural sector in Cambodia.
I expect that during Samdech Techo Hun Sen's upcoming visit to China, the two countries will announce a number of practical measures to strengthen cultural and tourism cooperation to further benefit the people. Citizens of both countries.
Q: On January 20, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will pay a visit to China. How do you expect this visit to contribute to Cambodia-China relations? What areas will be further promoted during the four-day visit?
I expect the leaders of the two countries to exchange views on regional and international cooperation. Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to China will be very fruitful, please wait and see.
Q: In recent years, the leaders of the two countries have exchanged visits frequently, how will this contribute to the development of bilateral relations?
Wang Wintian: The leaders of China and Cambodia have always met in bilateral and multilateral meetings, and we have always exchanged views on many important issues that are useful to guide the development of China-Cambodia relations. Cambodia.
As informed, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to China will fully promote the comprehensive strategic partnership and cooperation between China and Cambodia to reach a high level in history.
Q: What do you think about the Chinese people calling Cambodia a steel friend of China on social media?
Wang Winthean: The Chinese people consider Cambodia as a friend of steel. Meaning that the Chinese people feel that the friendship between China and Cambodia is as strong as steel, I think this is a vivid and accurate emphasis.
In recent years, Cambodia and China have a similar history and have experienced joint struggles to make the people of the two countries stand together. In particular, the relationship between China and Cambodia has undergone the experience of changing the international situation, and this longer and stronger experience proves that China-Cambodia relations are a steel friendship.
And it is not just the Chinese public on the Internet who sees Cambodia as a steel friend. President Xi Jinping and Samdech Techo Hun Sen have repeatedly said that China and Cambodia are steel friends. I feel that steel friend means friend in a very important situation, we are under pressure from the outside, but we still maintain the relationship, cooperation and key interests of each country.
The steel friendship between China and Cambodia will provide a strong guarantee that China and Cambodia can build a community of the same destiny.
Q: What are the factors that attract Chinese investors to invest in Cambodia? During your tenure, what will you do to attract Chinese investors as well as promote better Sino-Cambodian relations?
The third point is that Cambodia has a better environment to attract foreign investors and also has better policies. We also know that the Chinese and Cambodian governments have paid close attention to attracting Chinese investors to Cambodia, setting out a number of policies related to taxation and land.
I have always mentioned with the companies related to the three factors, the traditional friendship between China and Cambodia, and the good political stability and good environment for investors.
A few days ago I also met with many private companies in Cambodia, they also reported on the status of companies in Cambodia with a lot of experience. I feel that these companies are all very confident in investing in Cambodia. Many Chinese companies have invested in Cambodia, which is a good thing to strengthen and expand practical cooperation between the two countries.
I will stand by the work of the previous ambassadors and I will try to do some work such as deepening political trust between the two countries as well as expanding and strengthening practical cooperation between the two countries as well as enhancing cultural exchanges. Between the two countries to grow even stronger.
In particular, I want to increase cultural exchanges because I feel the need to deepen the friendship and make the people of the two countries understand each other more clearly and strongly. And improve people-to-people communication.
I am pleased to be a friend of journalists in Cambodia to deepen the cooperation between the two countries. Make the Chinese people more aware of Cambodia, as well as make the Cambodian people more aware of the Chinese people.
I would like to suggest that when Samdech Techo Hun Sen pays a successful visit to China, I will hold another press conference to promote Samdech Techo Hun Sen's achievements to China. Thank you. Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh will lead a high-level delegation to pay a three-day visit to Laos
