Speaking at the Closing Ceremony of the 27th Meeting of the APPF Forum on the evening of January 16, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin announced, "The Cambodian Parliament supports all initiatives aimed at finding a peaceful solution to avoid armed confrontation, in particular "Strengthen the role of parliament in reconciliation and regional and global peace efforts."
"Peace in the region and the world is a key factor in the development of the nation," he said. Starting from the importance of peace, we have decided to choose the core issue of strengthening parliamentary partnership for peace, security and sustainable development "as the theme for the 27th Annual Meeting as a basis for discussion and "Find solutions to regional and global challenges."
Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin continued that the pursuit of peace and long-term peace requires lasting resolution of conflicts, mutual trust without interfering in the internal affairs of sovereign states and based on principles. Equality is based on the UN Charter.
Australian Senate President Scott Ryan has expressed his commitment to further enhance parliamentary mechanisms to enhance cooperation with countries in the region and the world to bring peace and sustainable development.
It should be noted that the National Assembly of Cambodia has chaired the 27th meeting of the APPF Forum for 3 days from 14-16 January in Siem Reap under the theme "Strengthening Parliamentary Partnership for Peace, Security and Development. Sustainable ”with delegations from 21 countries: Cambodia, China, Australia, Laos, Russia, Malaysia, Indonesia, Philippines, Mongolia, New Zealand, Mexico, Japan, Thailand, South Korea, Chile, Papua New Guinea, Singapore and more.
The APPF was established in Tokyo, Japan in 1993 and currently has 27 full members. The Cambodian Parliament became a full member of the Parliamentary Forum in 1995 in a role to contribute to peace, prosperity and development in the region and the world.
The chief of Kakap II commune, Po Sen Chey district, who had a scandal by his ex-wife at work, has now officially divorced his ex-wife.
(Phnom Penh): Surprising story almost a year ago, the case of the chief of Kakap II commune, Po Sen Chey district, Mr. Mali Piseth, who stole a girl and was surprised by his ex-wife at that commune hall, so far he has achieved his goal through divorce Legal wife in Kampong Chhnang province has officially succeeded.
Ms. El Pisey, 39 years old, living in Trapeang Cheksa Village, Sangkat-Krong-Kampong Chhnang Province, has three daughters. To be tried by a court without her participation in absentia.
Ms. El Pisey continued that September 27, 2018 was the day of the verdict, but she did not attend the hearing and the verdict was delivered to her on December 12, 2018.
This means that Mr. Mali Piseth, 39 years old, the chief of Kakap II commune, filed for divorce in Kampong Chhnang province in order to take a wife after becoming a legal wife. The next wife is not married, but who continues to support Mr. Mali Piseth's livelihood, as well as bought a car for Mr. Mali Piseth to ride. This is according to information from people who know the commune chief confirmed this.
Please note that Mr. Mali Piseth and Ms. El Pisey were married without being married, but have been married for more than 10 years. El Pisey is a widow and Mali Piseth is a widower. They lived together and had another child. Mr. Mali Piseth also ordered Ms. El Pisey to delete the name of her ex-husband's child, replacing it with her own. This is the confirmation from Ms. El Pisey.
When the CNRP was dissolved, Mali Piseth automatically became the second Kabap commune chief. But he did not inform or inform his wife and children, instead he kept it a secret. In December 2018, Ms. El Pisey received a divorce application from the court.
Attempts by El Pisey to meet her husband were unsuccessful, with Maly Piseth trying to avoid meeting his wife. The fact that he did not meet his wife because he had a new girl was a businessman near Sangkat Kakap II.
