(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training in collaboration with the International Labor Organization (ILO) organized the Business Forum of Better Factories Cambodia (BFC) at the Raffles Royal Hotel on January 16, 2019 under the chairmanship of Mr. Heng Sour. Secretary of State, Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
Through this forum, Mr. Heng Sour expressed his belief that it will show the reality of working conditions in Cambodia, which will enable brand owners and international buyers to still trust Cambodia.
In an interview with the press, Mr. Heng Sour said that this business forum is an important opportunity for all brand owners and buyers who buy textiles, clothing, shoes and travel accessories from Cambodia to check what is Progress and standards of actual working conditions in Cambodia.
"According to the BFC report, working conditions in Cambodia have improved, which contradicts some of the statements that undermine Cambodia's working conditions and the freedom of professional organizations in Cambodia," he said. .
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor confirmed that Cambodia continues to support the presence of the BFC in Cambodia and continue to implement the joint action plan between the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and BFC for 2019, as well as prepare for the renewal of the Memorandum of Understanding to implement this project. For the new mandate.
