President Maduro warns of cracking down on opposition-controlled National Assembly for making fun of the constitution!
(Caracas): Venezuelan President Nicolas Maduro has warned that he will impose sanctions on the opposition-controlled National Assembly for making fun of the country's constitution. This was released by Sputnik on Wednesday, January 16, 2019.
Maduro's warning comes in response to the Venezuelan National Assembly's adoption of a statement calling him an outlawed president and that any decisions made by him and his government are invalid. Or to be followed. "Those who mock the country's constitution will face the law ... and the Supreme Court will take action against them," Maduro said.
It should be noted that the Venezuelan National Assembly issued the above statement based on Articles 233, 333 and 250 enshrined in the country's constitution. But the statement also came as the United States expressed support for the appointment of Juan Guaido, the current speaker of the National Assembly, as Venezuela's acting president.
