(Phnom Penh): Mr. Im Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, chaired a plenary meeting of the Constitutional Council this morning, January 16, 2019, to review and decide on the request of Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, to review the constitution on amendments. Two laws.
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News, the Constitutional Council unanimously approved by seven votes of the total number of members of the Constitutional Council (two absent) that the law amending the two laws was unconstitutional.
The two amendments to the law that the Constitutional Council has already reviewed include:
First, the law on the amendment of the law on the administration of the capital, province, municipality, district / khan. Second: the law on the amendment of the law on the election of the capital council, provincial council, municipal council, district council and Khan council.
