(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of January 16, 2019, Tuol Kork district police sent a Chinese officer to court, who was involved in a case of forcing a woman to have surgery and detaining a mother all night because she had no Medical expenses at Victoria Hospital as determined by the hospital.
It should be reminded that on the night of January 14, 2019, officials from the Ministry of Health and Tuol Kork District Authority, under the coordination of the prosecutor and under the direct command of the Minister of Health, searched the Victoria Hospital, calling some people for questioning and stepping forward. Arrested a Chinese foreman and cashier. Separately for others were released.
However, Ms. Seang Sokun, who was in charge of Victoria Hospital, was also questioned by the officials, but to no avail, because she did not know what to ask, and she was also a candidate. .
According to some reports, the Victoria Hospital was formerly known as "Xian Tai", but there was a scandal on medical treatment was closed by the Ministry of Health, but also asked to change the name of Victoria until the second scandal. . On the same day, the Minister of Health, Mr. Mam Bunheng, also issued a decision to officially close the hospital.
Please note that the above case occurred at around 8:00 pm on January 13, 2019 at Victoria Hospital, located at 61A, Street 592, Sangkat Boeung Kak II, Khan Toul Kork. Phnom Penh, owned by Dr. Seang Sokun, in charge of Victoria Hospital.
For this incident, the victim went to Victoria International Hospital with her mother for a gynecological examination. After the examination, the hospital told the victim to have surgery, otherwise she would have died.
The victim immediately said that she had no money, asked to go out and begged. However, the hospital forced the woman to have surgery immediately and did not even mention the cost of the surgery.
The hospital took a piece of paper, did not know what to write, gave the victim's mother a thumbprint. After the operation, the hospital gave him a bill to pay for the operation, which cost $ 2,000, $ 10 for examination and $ 46 for testing, and the operation is still unknown.
At that time, the victim's mother had only $ 600, the rest she asked for $ 100 in installments, but the hospital refused until another $ 500. Immediately, the hospital door was locked by security guards to prevent his family from leaving.
After the operation, the woman was in great pain and was taken by her family on a tricycle to the public hospital. This case also caused a surprise to the journalists who went to cover the event.
According to doctors at the city maternity hospital, the woman was released from the hospital as her condition improved and she was allowed to continue taking medication until she recovered. As for medical expenses, this public hospital is not required to pay.
