(Preah Vihear): The Director of the Department of Rural Development of Preah Vihear Province was transferred this morning, January 16, 2019, after nearly 25 years in office, Mr. Mop Thirith was appointed as the new Director of the Department, replacing Mr. Seng Sary, who has retired. .
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, and was attended by Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, as well as the leaders of the Armed Forces in the departments around the province and the governors of the eight districts. The commune chief as well.
Dr. Ouk Rabun expressed his pride in Preah Vihear province, which in a short period of time has changed its face and developed in almost all areas, from urban to rural areas. "In general, all provinces and cities in our country under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, have developed equally," he said.
At the same time, the Minister also instructed the newly appointed director of the department to work hard in accordance with the instructions of the head of the Royal Government of the Ministry of Rural Development of Preah Vihear Provincial Authority to make rural development a sector. Which is important to serve the real people.
Separately, Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, thanked Dr. Ouk Rabun for announcing the provision of 100 km of rubber roads in Preah Vihear Province in 2020.
The provincial governor considered this to be good news for the people of Preah Vihear province as a whole.
"Preah Vihear province is currently developing in all areas, not inferior to other provinces, which is under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen." He also thanked the leaders and civil servants of the Armed Forces in Preah Vihear Province for their cooperation and good work to make Preah Vihear Province more developed.
It should be noted that Mr. Mop Thirith, who announced his appointment as the new Director of the Department of New Rural Development in Preah Vihear Province today, is the former Deputy Director of the Provincial Department of Rural Development.
As for Mr. Seng Sary, the former director of the department who has retired, he has been in this position for almost 25 years, since 1994. However, Mr. Seng Sary is still destined to be appointed by Dr. Ouk Rabun as an advisor to be in charge in Preah Vihear province.
