Mr. Ly Vanna, Director of the Department of Preservation of Temples in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology, said that experts have now surveyed the damaged condition of the two missing Buddha images and assembled the found pieces to the body of the Buddha. And.
"For the lacquer and jewelry samples, the team tested them in Korea to find out the source and age and are currently waiting for the results," he said.
