(Phnom Penh): Finally, Mr. Kong Koam, former President of the Sam Rainsy Party and a close person of Mr. Sam Rainsy and Mr. Kong Bora, former Member of Parliament of the former National Rescue Party, was the King of Cambodia.
His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni issued a Royal Decree authorizing them to resume political activities after losing their rights by a Supreme Court ruling on November 16, 2017. This is according to the Royal Decree that Fresh News just received this morning, January 16, 2018.
The Royal Decree states that "Kong Koam, male, born on April 6, 1941, and Kong Bora, male, born on September 20, 1974, were rehabilitated, which was prohibited To carry out political activities for a period of 5 (five) years by the power of the judgment: 034 (g) dated 16 November 2019 of the Supreme Court.
The two politicians resumed their political rights after they applied to the Ministry of Interior for re-political rights after the amendment to the new Article 45 (Duplicate) Law on Political Parties. Effective.
Please be informed that Mr. Kong Koam and Mr. Kong Bora, including 118 former leaders of the former National Rescue Party, were sentenced by the Supreme Court to a five-year suspension on November 16, 2017 after the court believed that the former The opposition party conspired with foreigners to overthrow Cambodia's legitimate government.
