But for those who have a deeper understanding of the issue, it is the most accurate and up-to-date language for dealing with foreigners who nurture ambitions to take Cambodia hostage of its geopolitical interests.
Scholars of political science and international relations must have heard the saying, "No friend, no guide, only interest." On the other hand, they have also heard the saying, "There is nothing more grateful than geopolitical interests." Both of these clearly reflect what happened to Cambodia in the past and present.
In the past, the United States dropped nearly 3 million tons of bombs on Cambodia and eventually supported its nephew Lon Nol in a coup to oust Norodom Sihanouk as the legitimate head of state because Sihanouk refused to be his satellite. Body.
The United States then joined hands with China to support the Khmer Rouge, killing millions of Cambodians. In addition, to counter the influence of the former Soviet Union during the Cold War, the West, including the United States and the European Union, continued to support the Khmer Rouge for 12 years at the United Nations, torturing and killing them. The Khmer race is almost extinct.
Today the situation is not much different from the past. As the Phnom Penh government led by Hun Sen refuses to serve as a geopolitical satellite for itself, the United States and the European Union have resorted to the same old-fashioned approach: raising the nephew of the opposition led by Sam Rainsy to shake up the situation and find ways to do so. Overthrow a legitimate government that emerged from multi-party liberal democratic elections.
Their methods are varied, including the implementation of the color revolution movement and the incessant storms, with the support of foreign bosses under the pretext of two words: "democracy and human rights".
Did dropping millions of tons of bombs on Cambodian territory and killing hundreds of thousands of Cambodians who spoke out for human rights? Support for the Khmer Rouge to kill millions of Cambodians and continue to occupy Cambodia at the United Nations. Are Westerners talking about human rights?
First, it is a warning to foreigners who are the bosses of the Cambodian opposition that their sanctions on Cambodia are equivalent to handcuffs for their nephews, because the Phnom Penh government will not tolerate the group. Again, in the case of sanctions, because there is nothing more to lose.
Second, it is a message sent to the opposition to let them know that their attack on foreigners to impose any punishment on their country and its people is no different from setting fire to their own house. The strong position like the steel of the strong men of Cambodia is really admirable and valuable because Cambodia must not take national sovereignty "in exchange for any foreign geopolitical interests.
If the West wants equality with Cambodia and stands with China, it is not difficult because it just gives up its ambition to use Cambodia as a satellite to serve its geopolitical interests and turns to respect Cambodia's sovereignty like China. Well, it's done.
Faced with the current situation, Cambodia has no choice but to firmly defend its national sovereignty to counter the foreigners who are trying to pull Cambodia as a satellite. Without this firmness, Cambodia could face the same dangers as in the past.
By: Professor of Social Sciences, Kampong Cham University
