Mr. Toch Chao Koy, Head of Pursat Camcontrol Branch, said that during the inspection of Pursat Central Market, the specialized force conducted a preliminary test on prahok, sausage, soft fish, noodles, toast, noodles, dumplings, and desserts. As a result, the special forces found boracic acid in 11.5 kilograms of lattice.
Mr. Toch Chao Koy said that in the morning, the Camcontrol branch in Pursat province cooperated with the mobile laboratory staff to inspect the quality and quantity at 6 stations and depots (due to power outages). From Bakan district to Pursat city. As a result, we found only one Savimex depot that sells regular gasoline, super gasoline and not enough liters, we also contracted to modify.
"After finding out the results, the professional officers of the General Department of CamControl advised them and made a contract to stop such fraudulent activities," he said.
