As the government closes and chefs are suspended, Donald Trump is willing to spend his own money to buy ready-made food to eat together at the White House ...
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - US President Donald Trump has ordered hundreds of hamburgers for a White House dinner due to a shortage of chefs while government agencies remain closed. This was released by the BBC on Tuesday afternoon, January 15, 2019.
Partial operations in the U.S. federal government are currently stalled by part of Donald Trump's administration, while more than 800,000 state employees, including White House staffers, have been affected by the closure. Also, some of them have applied for temporary leave of absence and others are continuing to work without pay.
