Second, continue to push the development movement further, while continuing to push for in-depth reform in all areas in line with the set goals. But the implementation must involve all from all walks of life, including the Royal Government, the people and the private sector partners and civil society.
Fourth: Responding to the will and aspirations of the people through a landslide vote and especially the achievement of the four strategic goals and four priority areas as stated in the Rectangular Strategy - Phase 4 Which is the socio-economic policy agenda of the political program of the Royal Government of the 6th legislature of the National Assembly.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth said that Cambodia needs to achieve economic growth at an average annual rate of around 7% in the context of macroeconomic stability and increasing competitiveness and economic base development to serve the country's long-term development, especially progress. Achieve a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
He added that at the same time, we need to continue to strengthen governance and institutional capacity building in the public sector to build a clean, strong and intelligent public administration system. In addition, we must redouble our efforts to build more human capital in our society, both in the public and private sectors, in the context of the arrival of the Fourth Industrial Revolution.
