This evening, Samdech Techo Hun Sen officially announced the establishment of the Asian Cultural Council
(Siem Reap): As the Honorary Chairman of the Asian Cultural Council (ACC), Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, announces the official establishment of the Asian Cultural Council on the territory of Siem Reap Angkor, a cultural barn and tower. The temple of Cambodia on January 15, 2019.
After the roundtable discussion on these four key topics, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Honorary Founding President of the ACC, will address the evening to officially announce the establishment of the Asian Cultural Council, and he will preside over the banquet. At the Elephant Camp of Bayon Temple, with more than 800 guests from national and international executive and legislative bodies.
On January 16, the organizers of the ACC will organize a tour for guests wishing to visit the Angkor World Heritage Site, which is also listed as a UN World Heritage Site.
In addition to promoting mutual understanding and cultural exchange, the ACC event, the first of its kind in Cambodia, aims to promote unity in diversity and national integration. Among the member countries.
The event will also send a powerful and positive message to the outside world through the media and the experience that visitors have that the Kingdom of Cambodia has great potential for growth, tourism, culture and investment.
It should be noted that the "Asian Cultural Council" was renamed from the "ICAPP Cultural Council" at the 28th session of the ICAPP Standing Committee in July 2017 to expand the scope of work more widely and openly. The Asian Cultural Council was established on the initiative of Cambodia, China, Nepal and Russia, and this admirable partnership agreement is historic for the ICAPP and its political parties in Asia.
Cambodia, China, Nepal and Russia have been tasked with preparing the key documents for the Asian Cultural Council in accordance with the decision of the ICAPP Standing Committee held at its 27th meeting in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia in September 2016.
The Asian Cultural Council decided to establish a secretariat in Cambodia and elected Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, as the Honorary Founding Chairman, Ms. Khuon Sodary as Chairman and Mr. Sous Yara as Director General.
