The Prime Minister's heartfelt thanks to the King were made during the opening of the 27th Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum (APPF-27) held at the Sokha Hotel. Angkor, Siem Reap province, this morning, January 15, 2019.
Please be informed that the Cambodian Parliament is hosting the 27th APPF Annual Meeting from 14 to 17 January 2019 under the theme "Strengthening Parliamentary Partnership for Peace, Security and Sustainable Development".
Remarks by the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo and Member of the National Assembly, at the opening of the 27th Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum (APPF-27) held at the Sokha Angkor Hotel in Siem Reap.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "Currently, the Asia-Pacific region, including the world, is facing global problems such as trade wars, arms wars, cross-border terrorism, all kinds of illegal cross-border trade," he said. "Climate change, natural disasters, food insecurity and poverty are threatening global security and sustainable development."
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia said that the 27th Annual Meeting of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum is now important for countries in the region, including Cambodia. To strengthen the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Partnership to achieve peace, security and sustainable development.
The National Assembly President stressed that the mission of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum not only demonstrates the unity, friendship, solidarity and cooperation within the APPF family, but also the duty of the leadership of the legislature to create a clear vision for peace and prosperity. The next generation.
Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the 27th Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum, said this on the occasion of receiving the President of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum (APPF). APPF Annual Meeting paid a courtesy call on the morning of January 15, 2019 at Sokha Hotel and Conference Hall in Siem Reap.
The Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum was established in 1993 in Japan and currently has 27 members. The Cambodian Parliament, a member of the APPF, is hosting the annual meeting of the Parliamentary Forum in Angkor, Siem Reap from 14 to 17 January 2019.
