Samdech Techo Hun Sen also welcomed the delegation of APPF member countries, observer countries and all partner organizations, as well as national and international guests who arrived in Angkor, Siem Reap, a famous historical site of Cambodia. .
In addition to looking at these issues, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also gave important recommendations to the forum to discuss, in which Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted the win-win policy to provide light to the forum. Discussion to find a solution.
* First, to focus on the role of the United Nations, the role of ASEAN, the role of NGOs and the private sector, especially the goals of sustainable development, climate change, natural disasters, food security and poverty reduction. Issued by the United Nations.
* Second, to work together to promote respect for human rights and dignity as enshrined in the Charter and Charter of the United Nations, in particular not to interfere in the internal affairs of any country or to engage in illegal activities. Causing political instability or regional and global chaos.
* Third, to jointly resolve disputes arising through peaceful negotiations or based on the principles of international law or through win-win politics, which makes both parties to the conflict win-win or mutually acceptable. Peacefully.
* Fourth, to jointly and effectively prevent and crack down on terrorism and transnational crime of all kinds, drug trafficking, antiquities trafficking, crimes in telecommunications technology, infectious diseases of all kinds and trafficking in women between the countries in the region. Strengthen friendship and close cooperation between Asia-Pacific countries and children.
* 5: To jointly promote culture through change in order to maintain peace in the region and the world, leading to sustainable development.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that at present, the Asia-Pacific region, including the world, is facing global problems such as trade wars, arms wars, transnational terrorism, all kinds of illegal cross-border trade, climate change, natural disasters, food insecurity and Poverty is threatening global security and sustainable development of the world.
According to the Prime Minister, the meeting came at a time when Cambodia had just celebrated two major anniversaries: the 40th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day and the 20th anniversary of the end of the war through win-win politics. That Cambodia has solved national problems on its own.
In addition, Cambodia successfully ended the chronic war and brought complete peace, national unity, and complete territorial integrity by the end of 1998, without bloodshed, without weapons, and without foreign command or assistance. It is the first historical event in Cambodia that has not happened for more than 500 years.
He added that the structure of the Cambodian economy is changing from a country that relies on agriculture to a country that relies heavily on industry and services. The poverty rate also dropped from about 53.2% in 2004 to about 13.5% in 2014 and is expected to continue to decline to around 10% today.
Cambodia's strongmen point out that this makes Cambodia more ambitious, striving to become a high middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2050. This result clearly indicates that there is peace before there is development, there is strong development to ensure lasting peace. The 27th Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum officially opened in Angkor, Siem Reap
Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin expressed optimism that the meeting under the theme "Strengthening Parliamentary Partnership for Peace, Security and Sustainable Development" is another good opportunity to strengthen cooperation and increase mutual understanding. To visit and promote security, peace and sustainable development in Asia and the world by participating in the adoption of resolutions in response to the common aspirations of the Member States.
The Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum is a large parliamentary body with a vision to build peace and development in the region and the world. The forum was established in 1993 in Japan, which now has 27 members.
Cambodia was liberated from the Pol Pot regime on January 7, 1979, and since 1998, Cambodia has achieved real peace. The Prime Minister stated that through the win-win policy since 1998, Cambodia has become a country with a monarch, a constitution and a single government. Samdech emphasized that only peace can enable us to develop the nation.
The President of the Senate emphasized that in this regard, the Cambodian Parliament encourages the development of dialogue in the spirit of cooperation in both the legislative and executive frameworks, as well as relevant stakeholders on immigration security, trade disputes and other issues on the ground. Of international law and through existing mechanisms.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin stated that the Asia-Pacific is not only a multi-ethnic, multi-religious and multi-ethnic region with a long and prosperous civilization, but also a peaceful and prosperous region. Extensive, large markets and potential tourism poles in the world, a strong source of income for sustainable development.
