Spokesperson: Asian Cultural Council Forum demonstrates Cambodia's diplomatic success and promotes tourism to the world
(Siem Reap): Ek Tha, Vice Chairman of the Media and Media Committee of the Asian Cultural Council (ACC), said that hosting the first meeting of the Asian Cultural Council was a great achievement for the diplomatic community. Cambodia on the international stage and help promote Cambodia's cultural heritage, both tangible and intangible, to the world.
In an interview with reporters on the afternoon of January 14, 2019, Mr. Ek Tha said that as the host of the first meeting of the Asian Cultural Council, Cambodia has already prepared the qualifications.
"When we do that, it helps the international community see Cambodia as a model for preserving both tangible and intangible cultural heritage," he said. "It relates to cultural tourism through the media as a mirror to the outside world that Cambodia is a cultural, natural and historical tourism paradise."
The spokesman also claimed that as Cambodia receives more tourists, more investors will come to Cambodia.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia hosted the Asian Cultural Council Meeting in Angkor, Siem Reap Province from 14-16 January under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who was unanimously elected. Honorary Founder of the Asian Cultural Council at the International Conference of Asian Political Parties (ICAPP), which represents more than 350 political parties from 52 countries in the region.
The forum included a welcome message from the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, at the start of the meeting on the morning of January 15. Afterwards, there was a welcoming speech from Ms. Khuon Sodary, Second Vice President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, Chair of the ACC, followed by speeches by ICAPP and UNESCO representatives.
Mr. Ek Tha stated that this international meeting focused on four main topics, including: The emergence of a world with diverse perspectives and Asian identities. 2. The connection between culture and sustainable development. Using technology for the connection of civilization and 4. Building a community for a single destiny in Asia.
