Tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Attends the 27th Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum Meeting
Before the official opening tomorrow morning, January 14, 2019, Samdech Heng Samrin, Chairman of the 27th Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum, chaired a meeting of the Executive Committee of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum. The meeting was held to accomplish some important tasks of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum (APPF), especially the agenda for the 27th APPF Annual Meeting, which will officially open on January 15.
The APPF delegation, which is a member of the Executive Committee, attended this morning's meeting with Cambodia, Canada, Australia, Japan, Chile, Laos, Mongolia, Russia, Indonesia.
The Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum is a group of legislatures established to promote peace and sustainable development. APPF was established in 1993 in Japan and currently has 27 members. The Cambodian Parliament became a full member of the Parliamentary Forum in 1995 to seek peace, prosperity and development in the region and the world.
