Japan and Russia could not sign a peace treaty due to the Kuril Islands dispute. Tokyo claims that the archipelago was illegally occupied by Russia after Japan surrendered in 1945 during World War II, while Moscow urged Japan to recognize the consequences of the war. This includes Russia's sovereignty over the Kuril Islands.
