(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of January 14, 2019, the Court of Appeal organized a meeting with civil servants to provide the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) for civil servants for the purpose of health care and to show care. Pay attention to civil servants in sacrificing their physical and mental strength to serve the people and society.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. You Bunleng, President of the Court of Appeal, and Mr. Ouk Savuth, Attorney General of the Court of Appeal, and was attended by all officials of the Court of Appeal.
Mr. You Bunleng said that the Court of Appeal was very pleased that the Royal Government provided the National Social Security Fund for civil servants in ministries, institutions, national and sub-national units for the purpose of health care for all civil servants.
The President of the Court of Appeal stated that the implementation of the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which has been implemented continuously through the direct support of institutions such as civil servants with maternity leave, work accidents and deaths. Original. Past support based on national budget resources is still limited and therefore does not fully meet the needs of officials at risk.
He added that after the increase in national budget revenue, the Royal Government has implemented the social security system for occupational risk for public officials and health care for public officials, former civil servants and veterans to improve social welfare, and now civil servants Get social security for everyone. Spokesman of the Royal Government issued a statement congratulating Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the 34th anniversary of his tenure as Prime Minister
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Phay Siphan, Spokesman of the Royal Government of Cambodia, on January 14, 2019, issued a statement congratulating Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the 34th anniversary of his tenure as Prime Minister.
According to a statement obtained by Fresh News today, the appointment of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the head of the Royal Government has given the country and the people of Cambodia the warmest and most confident confidence.
The statement stated: "The Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as all the people, would like to express our gratitude and congratulations to Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the anniversary of receiving the position of Prime Minister from the people. "Cambodia through its parliament for 34 years, starting from January 1985 to the present."
"The position of Head of the Royal Government, which is the choice of the Cambodian people, is a testament to the effectiveness and power of Samdech Techo's leadership, which we have warmly and most confidently received," the statement said. Please read the following statement: Senior Minister Osman Hassan meets with the Vice President of the Malaysian Parliament
The Vice President of the Malaysian Parliament praised the good leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who has turned Cambodia into a country that has developed in almost all areas, almost unbelievable in all kinds of progress. To date, Cambodia has been recognized regionally and internationally as a model country that maintains peace and harmony.
Acting Minister of Tourism: Providing Social Security is the Royal Government's Care for Civil Servants
(Phnom Penh): On January 14, 2019, at the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia, Acting Minister, in the handing over ceremony of the Social Security System and the dissemination of the policy of implementing the social security system to the leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Tourism on January 14, 2019. The Ministry of Tourism, Mr. Tith Chantha, said that the provision of social security is the attention of the Royal Government to civil servants.
Mr. Meng Hong, Deputy Director of the National Social Security Fund, spoke about the social security system, occupational risk for public officials and health care for public servants, former civil servants and veterans.
Acting Minister Tith Chantha said that the above two social security regimes are good policies in response to maintaining the well-being and improving the living standards of civil servants, ex-civil servants and veterans. Up.
Mr. Tith Chantha believes that after receiving the membership card, officials of the Ministry of Tourism will have easy access to health care services at public hospitals and partner hospitals.
In addition, he also instructed all civil servants to contribute to the implementation of various reforms of the Royal Government and make efforts to continue to increase labor productivity for the new year to be better, especially to maintain peace in order to Continue sustainable development.
With this instruction, the Acting Minister of Tourism also continued that as long as there is peace, there will be development and the living standards of civil servants will continue to improve.
This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Attends the 27th Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum Meeting
On the morning of January 14, 2019, Samdech Heng Samrin, Chairman of the 27th Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum, chaired a meeting of the Executive Committee of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum. The meeting was held to accomplish some important tasks of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum (APPF), especially the agenda for the 27th annual APPF, which officially opens on January 15.
The APPF delegation, which is a member of the Executive Committee, attended the meeting with Cambodia, Canada, Australia, Japan, Chile, Laos, Mongolia, Russia, Indonesia.
The Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum is a group of legislatures established to promote peace and sustainable development. APPF was established in 1993 in Japan and currently has 27 members.
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree appointing six Secretaries of State and Undersecretaries of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts. This is according to the Royal Decree obtained by Fresh News on the night of January 14, 2019.
According to the Royal Decree, the six senior officials of the Ministry of Culture have the status of three Secretaries of State and three Undersecretaries of State.
The chairperson of the meeting said that the meeting of the Women's Parliament in Cambodia on this occasion is a historic meeting. Historically, the APPF has been established for 27 years, but the Women's Parliamentary Assembly has just become the first official APPF meeting in Cambodia.
Ms. Khuon Sodary said that the members of the meeting were very interested in the topic and they said that women are an important human resource that promotes peace. Peace and happiness in society, family and society. He stressed that inequality between men and women is ubiquitous, so it requires collective consideration for women to participate in decision-making in both the private and public sectors.
During the meeting, the Cambodian parliamentary delegation led by Ms. Kheng also mentioned the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to promote women, such as social protection for women. Women working in the garment and footwear industry in Cambodia during pregnancy and childbirth receive a special allowance and leave of 120% of their salary.
