Khashoggi was assassinated on October 2 in a murder case that shocked the world and posed a serious threat to relations between Riyadh and Washington. Two-year lease to open a club just 8 months, Long Chong also stopped renting, causing a dispute in Por Sen Chey
The dispute was caused by a Korean man who did not honor his contract and the contract was for two years. But after the lease had only been in operation for eight months, a Korean man, Long Chong, who lost more than $ 70,000, was forced to stop renting and move out, and the landlord turned it into a dispute.
The incident happened at 12:30 noon on January 14, 2019 in the disco club "Fan Club" in Chrey Kong village, Sangkat Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Sen Chey. The owner of the location is Sarath, while the tenant, Sin Chungfan, 65, is Korean and his wife is Tep Channarin, 33, a Cambodian.
According to the story, on May 1, 2018, a Korean man and his Cambodian wife rented the above location to open a disco club under the brand name "Fan Club". In this rental, $ 3,000 per month. Made a proper contract with each other. After renting for two years, the landlord required a one-month deposit of $ 3,000, and after the match, the Korean man opened the club every month.
The Korean man said he did not want to do this, but he ran out of more than $ 70,000 and was unable to continue his business. Now he wants to finish and ask for his equipment to be removed from the location separately, telling his employer to book one month in advance, so let's go.
After mediation, until 1:10 pm on the same day, the two sides agreed to end the story, with the Korean man agreeing to pay the water, electricity and $ 300 monthly salary. January 2019 to the owner of the location.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chheang Vun, Chairman of the Committee on Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information of the National Assembly of Cambodia, said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy has brought peace and development to Cambodia in all fields. Aims to share this experience with other MPs attending the APPF meeting.
Mr. Chheang Vun made this remark on January 14, 2019, when he attended the 27th Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum (APPF) Executive Committee Meeting at Sokha Hotel, Siem Reap. "The win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, regarding the solution in Cambodia, the conflict in Cambodia, the peace in Cambodia, the stability in Cambodia," he said.
Mr. Chheang Vun continued that this win-win policy is a contribution to build a road that can make Cambodia and the Asia-Pacific region to a goal until the solution to the living conditions of the Cambodian people to be as prosperous as today. So politics is very important for humanity.
He added that Cambodia has gone through many years of civil war, and this is a bitter experience for Cambodians as well as people around the world. Therefore, this bitter experience has made Cambodia peaceful, stable and have all kinds of developments.
Mr. Chheang Vun stated: "We want to share with the MPs of other countries to join them to understand you remember, and since 2015 in the field of parliamentary diplomacy, I have set a big goal. "And that goal is to follow the goal of Samdech Techo Hun Sen set by Samdech clearly: to promote the hiding of peace to have a strong opportunity to develop the country and provide opportunities for the people."
A senior official of the National Assembly added that for today, Cambodian MPs will also discuss the role of the Cambodian Parliament in promoting peace, stability and sustainable development.
Samdech Heng Samrin Provides Some Recommendations to APPF Women MPs to Promote Gender Equality
In this meeting, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin emphasized the importance of women in society, but also said that due to the rapid development of technology, extremist activities, racism, etc. have become obstacles to the work. Height of women and children.
He said that in such a global situation, the APPF must continue to focus and redouble our efforts to achieve peace, stability, global order and achieve sustainable development goals. Sustainability of the United Nations.
Samdech Heng Samrin continued that there should be a mechanism to monitor, evaluate and learn about gender equality in the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum to monitor the implementation of resolutions on women's empowerment and gender equality and provide mutual support. To achieve the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals, especially Goal 5.
On that occasion, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin made some recommendations to the meeting to consider, such as:
First, a working group should be set up to study the impact of the Industrial Revolution, fourth, especially on the impact on women and girls, and to develop a strategy that enables women to change their status according to the Industrial Revolution. The benefits of using those new technologies.
Second, to create a sustainable and comprehensive education policy and to allocate a large amount of state budget to promote the education of young women in science, technology, engineering and mathematics (STEM). Education is a powerful and powerful core tool that empowers and empowers women and girls in general to reach their full potential.
Third, pay more attention to promoting gender equality, especially basic education for girls living in remote and vulnerable areas in the Asia-Pacific region and globally.
Fourth, all social protection systems should increase funding and care for women and girls, and especially those affected by various powerful leaders.
After Samdech Ponhea Chakrei announced the opening of the APPF Women MPs' Meeting, the meeting was continued under the chairmanship of Ms. Khuon Sodary, Second Vice President of the National Assembly and Chair of the APPF Women MPs Meeting.
The APPF Women's Parliamentary Meeting discussed three topics: Topic 1: Strengthening the Asia-Pacific Partnership for Gender Equality and Empowering Women and Girls for Peace and Development By sustainability.
Topic 2: Ensuring equality between women and men in education, training, technology and information technology for peace and achieving the goals of sustainable development, and the third theme is to promote gender equality and empowerment. Women by increasing women's participation in decision-making at all levels.
The meeting, chaired by Ms. Khuon Sodary, discussed three topics, one at a time, giving member countries the opportunity to express themselves.
Ms. Khuon Sodary emphasized that in the 27th meeting, the women MPs received three draft resolutions from the Cambodian parliamentary delegation, two draft resolutions from the Russian Federation, and one draft resolution from Chile. Draft Resolution from Australia Draft Resolution from Malaysia.
These draft resolutions will be discussed further at the Plenary Session of the 27th Annual Meeting, which Cambodia is hosting now and at a later date. Australia successfully tests first unmanned train!
