The Cambodian leader has made it clear to the EU that in the past, the EU has made two mistakes against Cambodia, which has caused great pain to the Cambodian people. Europe must not make a third mistake.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that the first mistake is that the European Union, a democratic country, supported the coup to overthrow Prince Norodom Sihanouk. Democracies should condemn the coup plotters to overthrow Prince Norodom Sihanouk, but do not expect them to support Lon Nol against Prince Norodom Sihanouk, the legitimate head of state.
Second, the European Union has backed the genocidal regime of Pol Pot to sit on a UN seat 12 years after it killed more than 3 million people.
Samdech Techo continued that the day before, Samdech met with the Member of Parliament of the Republic of Ireland, who is also the former Prime Minister of Ireland and also the President of the European Union. The Irish MP expressed his regret and said in front of the Prince that the mistakes that the European Union had made against Cambodia in the past were very unfair to Cambodia.
Today, Cambodia adheres to democracy and builds a developing country. These developments also have the contribution of the European Union, but the EU itself must also consider whether it should maintain the achievements it has helped to build and continue to drive the process of improving the situation for a better economy, better democracy and better human rights. Or have to stop here?
(Kampong Cham): Dr. Ma Chhoeun, Member of Parliament for Kampong Cham Constituency, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Central Working Group for Choeung Prey District on January 14, 2019, said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister Of Cambodia is a patriotic hero and has built peace, making the people prosperous and prosperous as today.
