Mental education through meditation is a good cure for mental illness for the general public.
(Phnom Penh): Psychological problems have made some Cambodians face the problems of their lives to the point of committing inhumane acts or committing suicide by all these acts, and then all people need to be educated. Mental Meditation for mental health and as a natural remedy for mental illness is good for everyone to apply as well.
On January 13, 2019, Ieng Sotheara, President of the Ieng Foundation, organized a meditation session for mental health at the Cambodian Buddhist Center in Kien Svay District, Kandal Province. A total of 1,250 monks, government officials, civil society, private sector associations and students attended.
According to Ieng Sotheara, President of the Ieng Foundation, the "Meditation for Mental Health" program is organized for four main purposes, including: first, to promote the benefits of meditation; As a mental health and physical health aid for the general Cambodian population, the third is to help create harmony in the whole society, and the fourth is to promote national meditation in the coming years. .
It should also be noted that this event, which was attended by 1,250 people, refers to the day of the first meeting of the Samma Samputa with the monks, when he first attained enlightenment, which is the full moon day in March. There are also Buddhists celebrating Meak Bochea with 1,250 monks.
