(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kao Thach, General Director of Rural Development Bank, on January 14, 2019, attended a meeting to discuss the project to support financing for vegetable production and to find solutions to some problems that are the consequences for your vegetable farmers. Organized as a community and owned by a company that buys vegetables.
Mr. Kao Thach said that the purpose of the meeting was to boost the vegetable production of vegetable farmers in Cambodia, with the participation of private vegetable buyers and the Rural Development Bank. Preferential interest to communities or companies that buy vegetables in case of additional financial needs.
The Director General stated that the reduction of credit is part of ensuring the well-being of the people who eat vegetables and help reduce the import of vegetables, as well as improve the lives of people who are engaged in eating and growing vegetables and reduce the work. The migration of farmers went abroad.
As a result of the meeting, the Rural Development Bank will contribute:
* Work closely with the community of vegetable procurement companies to boost the vegetable supply of vegetable farmers, as well as support investment capital for farmers and community or vegetable procurement companies to increase vegetable procurement from farmers.
* Establish an independent vegetable quality laboratory.
Collaborate with the community of vegetable collection companies by setting up stalls selling Khmer vegetables every Sunday in Phnom Penh.
Coordinate with relevant institutions to help solve vegetable transportation.
Establish a vegetable procurement association in collaboration with the Rural Development Bank.
* Meet at least once a month with the community and the company to buy vegetables to monitor the progress of work and solve challenges.
