(Phnom Penh): Mr. Srun Pov, President of the Cambodian Breeders' Association, said that the price of live pigs has now risen, but despite the increase, people are still reluctant to return to raising again.
People's reluctance to re-raise pigs is due to other factors. In fact, in the past, they have faced the challenge of lowering the price of live pigs in Cambodia due to the import of Vietnamese pigs from the Cambodian market, which caused the price of pigs in Cambodia to fall sharply, causing pig farm owners and people to lose money. Subsequent collapses. This was confirmed by the president of the association.
He said that after gaining experience, people are reluctant to re-breed, even if they want to re-breed, they need to consider first, because raising pigs is not raising a month or four. 10 days for sale.
He added: "That is why the number of pigs in Cambodia has decreased, making Cambodia continue to depend on pig imports from Thailand and Vietnam. "Since I have been the president of the association for 10 years, I have seen that the import of every day, Cambodia imports at least 1-2 thousand pigs per day from neighboring countries."
"With this issue, I would like to urge the pig farms in Cambodia to expand to fill the market, because in the past, Cambodia was short and still short of and continue to import," he said.
