The speech of Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, was made on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the third ring road on Monday, January 9, 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that with the receipt of foreign funding, it is necessary for Cambodia itself to have a budget in hand to contribute to the implementation of the project.
Samdech Techo stated that during the construction of the third city road, up to four more flyovers will be built, crossing National Road 4, National Road 3, National Road 2 and National Road 21. Samdech further stated that in the future, Cambodia will build more roads under the river.
Samdech Techo considers that the third ring road is an important strategic road to facilitate traffic and trade, which provides benefits to the national economy. Samdech also asked for the understanding of the people who were disturbed by the construction of this ring road.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that Cambodia is studying the construction of roads and bridges to connect Kratie and Kampong Thom provinces and is also considering the construction of roads connecting Koh Kong to the border and connecting Samlot and Pailin.
