Volunteer doctors from France will bring more than 2.5 tons of medicine to treat people in 5 districts in Kampong Cham province for free for 10 days
(Kampong Cham): The Association of Volunteer Doctors of France will bring about 2.5 tons of medicine to treat people in 5 districts in Kampong Cham province. This is according to the representative of the French Medical Association, Ms. Xanda Damen, who met with Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham Province on January 14, 2019 at the sofa hall of Kampong Cham Provincial Hall.
Ms Xanderman said she would bring two and a half tons of medicine from France worth more than 40,000 euros and prepare another 80,000 euros for the mission. 10-day medical mission in 5 districts in Kampong Cham province.
She said that the visit to treat people made out of love and want to save the poor people. A team of 41 doctors will come from France on January 21, 2019, including 10 Cambodian doctors to help complete this mission.
On that occasion, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun expressed his warm welcome and cooperation in the mission of the French volunteer doctors who will bring medicine as well as other materials to treat the people in Kampong Cham. At the same time, the governor thanked the French team of volunteer doctors who have prepared a lot of medicine and a lot of money for this mission.
Please also note that the date of the medical examination of the people in the five districts is not yet known. The five districts that will be assigned to the mission are Prey Chhor, Stung Trang, Chamkar Leu, Koh Sotin and Kampong Siem districts.
