Journalists in Cambodia were so angry with the leaders of the Khmer Rouge Party that they used insulting words to journalists in Cambodia, calling the newspaper in Cambodia a "fried banana" newspaper. Outraged, the media planned to take action to get the party leaders to correct their words and publicly apologize for the insult.
A well-known former journalist, Neth Pheaktra, expressed regret over the insulting remarks of the Khmer Rouge party to Cambodian journalists and newspapers. Mr. Neth Pheaktra considers this insult to be a violation of the right to freedom of the press and freedom of expression.
Mr. Pheaktra said that the insult of the Khmer party arose that the newspaper wrapped bananas, the party is going against the truth and does not value the efforts of journalists. He suggested that the Khmer Rouge party should publicly apologize to Cambodian journalists rather than come out and clear their mistakes, as this Facebook account is a fake account to justify themselves and clean up its immoral arrogance.
Puy Kea, secretary general of the Club of Cambodian Journalists, expressed regret over the allegations. He considered the use of this statement to be a bit heavy and wanted the party's honorary president to use it more appropriately.
Second, it is a serious disgrace to journalists who have worked hard and are actively strengthening their professional capacity to better serve society. He can criticize and improve if he sees shortcomings, but he must not insult because it is not Khmer morality.
The president of the Club of Cambodian Journalists stressed that these two major mistakes indicate that the honorary president of the Khmer Rouge Party is not yet worthy of being a politician. Therefore, you should correct the words and try to prepare better.
He added that most journalists in Cambodia work out of their own free will, as this work is not funded by any state institution or citizen. The money comes from the media, which they exchange their physical and intellectual strength for.
He questioned the leadership of the Khmer Rouge Party, saying that journalists, although not living on national money and the people, but did a lot of work for the nation and the people, the Khmer Rouge Party rose as a member of the Supreme Advisory Council and Advise to spend the national money and the people for many months, what has been done for the benefit of the nation and the people? How long has the mission been to take Koh Tral?
