The commemoration of the 40th anniversary of the historic January 7 Victory Day was held on January 13, 2019 in Sen Monorom, with the participation of provincial councilors, departments around the province, the three forces, municipal / district authorities, people. Youth, Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Youth League for Peace, Youth of the Cambodian Red Cross, Youth, Scouts, Teachers and about 2,000 students.
Speaking at the meeting, Mr. Svay Sam Eang read the speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party, saying that without January 7, there would be no progress until now.
He said that due to the strength of national unity, the whole country was liberated from the brutal genocidal regime of Democratic Kampuchea, Pol Pot and brought peace, freedom, dignity, social progress on January 7, 1979, which Cambodians all over the country consider as the second birthday and will always remember and never forget.
The provincial governor also called on all people to work together to protect and maintain this most difficult peace to be stable and sustainable for the long term and to work together to promote the achievements of the Royal Government. Efforts have been made to reach the general public with a better understanding of the current progress of the nation.
