(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Land Forces and Chairman of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) Staff Selection Sub-Committee in 2019, said that the Cambodian Armed Forces are becoming more proud because of the younger generation. The number of applicants for the framework competition has increased from year to year.
Prior to the nationwide examination this morning, January 13, 2019, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, who visited the Phnom Penh Capital Center at Bak Touk High School, said that the candidates who have applied for the army exam at This year 2019 is an increase of more than 1,000 people in previous years.
Figures from the 2019 Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Sub-Committee on Recruitment Examination show that for the nationwide framework, there are a total of 8,352 candidates, 3,270 of whom are female, divided into 356 rooms. The Ministry decided to recruit 200 active officers, 250 infantry officers, 170 lieutenants and 60 technical officers.
At the same time, Mr. HUN Manet also instructed the Sub-Committee on Selection of Officers and the Selection Committee to keep the examination process running smoothly, accurately, transparently and fairly. This means that those who succeed after the exam in general knowledge, language and sports pass with their own ability, and those who do not pass the exam are exhausted on their own.
He stressed that "the sub-committee, as well as our selection committee, is to make the selection of our officers smooth, accurate, transparent and fair. "What we want is to be fair so that all of you can show your abilities."
At the same time, Lt. Gen. But Sopheap, Director of the School of Active Officers and Permanent Deputy Chairman of the Sub-Committee on Selection of Officers and Chairman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Examination Center, also told the media that for the number of candidates who participated in the exam. His constituency manages 3,777 people.
According to General But Sopheap, for general security and order in the examination center of Bak Touk High School and Primary School, it went smoothly without any problems, with the good cooperation of all relevant authorities.
He also instructed the candidates in Phnom Penh and all regional armies throughout the country to pay attention and show all their abilities to succeed in this exam because That the exam is not bribed or partisan, you have the ability to pass.
It should be noted that the recruitment of officers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, the 23rd generation of active duty officers, the 11th generation of infantry officers, the 12th generation officers and the 2019 military technical officers will be held at January 13-17, 2019, focusing on general knowledge, foreign languages and physical education.
