Regarding the Dar Lan festival, Minister Veng Sakhon briefly reminded the ceremony that the Dar Lan festival is a festival related to the religious beliefs of the Cambodian people, most of whom are farmers, always adhere to this tradition. After the rice harvest is finished and threshed, in order to preserve the identity of the Khmer soul, be grateful to the owner of the water, the owner of the land and the sacred objects.
He added that it also provides an opportunity for farmers to meet close relatives and friends to expand brotherhood, solidarity and friendship, and exchange ideas on farming and especially for recreation after spending physical and mental strength. All kinds of hearts under the heat of the sun and thunderstorms throughout the growing season.
