More than 700 Kamchay Mear residents gather to celebrate their second birthday in the shadow of peace and development
The meeting was held in the presence of Mr. Steng Sokhom, Chairman of the Central Working Group for Kamchay Mear District, and was attended by the leadership of Kamchay Mear District, the Central Working Group for the District, District Party Committees and Commune / Sangkat Councilors, District Party Youth, Retired School Director. Citizens' level and the armed forces of all kinds.
Mr. Steng Sokhom read the speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party on the occasion of the 40th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day to the participants, in which he highlighted some important points in the speech. "January 7 is the second birthday of the Cambodian people and January 7 is a symbol and spirit of salvation, unity and national development."
In this sense, he explained that the January 7 victory had saved the lives of millions of Cambodians who were still waiting for their deaths, devaluing all the spiritual and material values of the Khmer nation that had been built. In its thousands of years of history, it has collapsed and almost disappeared under the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
On January 7, 1979, the Khmer nation was revived, closed the darkest pages of Cambodian history, and ushered in a new era of independence, freedom, democracy, and social progress for our poor nation. Cambodia has every right to own its own destiny. In addition, the victory of January 7, 1979 also made an active contribution to peace and stability in the region.
The people of Cambodia have named January 7, 1979 as their second birthday. Without the victory of January 7, we would not have anything today, which is a historical fact that no one or force can distort or destroy.
The people of Kamchay Mear district have clearly determined that January 7 is their second birthday, January 7 has really brought about national unity, January 7 has really brought national development. The people of Kamchay Mear really gave the truth for January 7 and remembered it forever, so this historic day is forever remembered in the memory of all people of all generations who love peace, freedom and justice.
In this ceremony, Mr. Steng Sokhom also informed the meeting about the results of the 45th meeting of the CPP Committee, open to the members of the meeting that the meeting of the CPP in late December. Invited key representatives from all sub-national and national levels to participate.
