The following is the announcement of the Thai Trade Representative: This morning, the Ministry of National Defense conducted the 2019 military officer recruitment examination, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet inspected in Phnom Penh.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of January 13, 2019, the Ministry of National Defense started the competition for recruitment of military officers at the examination center in Phnom Penh and in each military region throughout Cambodia.
The exam focuses on general knowledge, foreign languages and physical education. For the nationwide framework, there are a total of 8,352 candidates, 3,270 of whom are female, divided into 356 rooms.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of National Defense, examination centers across the country include:
For the examination process this morning, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army and Chairman of the Sub-Committee on the 2019 Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Officer Selection Sub-Committee, inspected the Capital Examination Center. Phnom Penh, held at Bak Touk High School.
In order to ensure transparency, accuracy and fairness in the examination, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet has issued a strict order strictly restricting the examination rules, strictly prohibiting unauthorized persons from entering the examination center, including military officers who wear two or three stars.
On that occasion, General Phuong Siphan, Deputy Secretary of the Ministry of National Defense, also inspected the 5th Military Examination Center in Banteay Meanchey Province.
