China wants to dig deeper into the moon and then go to Mars!
Meanwhile, there are many more secrets about the moon, and future missions will be even more exciting. In addition, the lunar exploration program will continue to enhance China's image as a country that plays an important role in space exploration.
According to Wu, the Chinese space agency CNSA is discussing and preparing plans for the fourth phase of the lunar exploration program, including the launch of missions to the two poles of the planet. Scientists say that some places on the south pole of the moon receive sunlight for more than 180 consecutive days, while others surrounded by large asteroids are never exposed to sunlight. And may contain frozen water.
Wu revealed the vision of the Chinese space agency that a scientific research station will be able to appear on the moon's south pole and that it will be automatic and allow people to visit for a short time.
