(Damascus) - Israel continues to carry out air strikes on Syria, especially around the capital Damascus, but the Syrian missile defense system obtained from Russia can prevent this attack. This is according to the press release from Sputnik on Saturday, January 12, 2019.
The attack was carried out by Israeli warplanes, which fired missiles at the Syrian city of Damascus, but according to the Syrian military, most of the Israeli missiles were destroyed by Syrian air defense systems. When. A warehouse at Damascus airport was also damaged, but there were no obstructions to the international airport's operations.
Russia equipped the S-300 missile system with the Syrian military in September 2018 to protect Syrian air security, especially from repeated Israeli attacks, which Damascus claims were carried out with protracted targets. The war in Syria will last even longer.
