Yidup truck transporting potatoes was stopped by the Forestry Administration for stealing more than 30 cubic meters of rosewood
(Phnom Penh): A truck transporting cassava with license plate Kampong Cham 3A-6151 was cracked down by the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration in cooperation with the Southern Tonle Sap Forestry Administration Inspectorate for illegally storing more than 30 illegal rosewood trucks. Cubic meters.
The operation to crack down on forest crime took place at 5:10 pm on January 11, 2019 at a point along National Road 5 near the Men Sarun factory in Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Un Vannarith, Deputy Director of Phnom Penh Forestry Administration District, said that the crackdown on illegal forestry, after receiving confidential information from the people about the jeep transporting cassava hidden in the luxury wood, then the Forestry Administration Inspectorate under the Tonle Sap Lake. Cooperate with the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration to crack down.
He said that the confiscated wood was the first and second type of luxury wood, including four types: teal, thlong, Tbeng, Phteak, and more than 30 cubic meters. All of this illegal rosewood was smuggled out of Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province, with the intention of transporting it to a depot in Takeo province, but was defeated by forestry authorities.
The deputy director of the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration said that the operation to stop the forest crime did not stop people because the suspects escaped before the force arrived, so only cars and luxury wood were stopped. .
Both the car and all the luxury wood exhibits are currently being stored by the forestry authorities at the Prek Pnov Forestry Administration, located along National Road 5, Lime Village, Sangkat Svay Pak, Khan Russey Keo, to wait for the case to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action.
