Samdech Techo Hun Sen also told the Irish MP that the European Union should not make a third mistake on Cambodia. Europe's third mistake, he said, was to try to use the mechanism of removing Cambodia's preferential tariffs to the European Union to impose sanctions on Cambodia.
Samdech Techo, head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, said that the European Union has twice made mistakes against the country and the Cambodian people. The two mistakes first. Is to support the coup d'état to overthrow Samdech Norodom Sihanouk on March 18, 1970 and the second mistake. Supporting the Khmer Rouge seat at the United Nations for more than 12 years, ignoring the suffering and massacre of the Cambodian people under this regime.
The European Commission is considering removing preferential tariffs on Cambodian goods after allegations that Cambodia violated human rights and undermined democracy in the country. The Royal Government of Cambodia has repeatedly denied and commented on the European Commission's allegations and is continuing discussions with European countries on the issue.
However, for several months now, there has been no new information regarding the removal of the preferential tariff system, and until 2019, Cambodian goods will continue to be exported to Europe under the preferential tariff system.
