Preah Kosomak Hospital Celebrates the One-Year Anniversary of the Signing of the Cambodia-China Signature on the New Building Project of Preah Kosomak Hospital
(Phnom Penh): On January 11, 2019, Preah Kosomak Hospital celebrated the one year anniversary of the signing of the agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and China on the construction of a new building of Preah Kosomak Hospital with 11 floors, 132 rooms, size 28 900 square meters on a total area of 13,740 square meters, with a budget of more than $ 80 million under a grant from the Chinese friends.
Director of Preah Kosomak Hospital, Dr. Tan Sokun, said, "Today is also the day we celebrate the anniversary of the signing of the agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and China on the construction of the Cambodia-China Friendship Building of Preah Kosomak Hospital." January 2018-2019. "The reopening of the construction site took place on October 30, more than three months ago."
The construction process went smoothly, in accordance with the contract between Cambodia and China, which will be completed within 40 months, but according to the Chinese side, will try to speed up construction before the deadline 36 months. According to the doctor.
The Director of Preah Kosomak Hospital said that in order to meet the growth and the need for health care of the people who come to see and treat at this hospital, the Royal Government of Cambodia has proposed to the Government of the People's Republic of China and received the study approval. From the project at the end of 2015.
On January 11, 2018, Cambodia and China signed the above construction project and started to open the construction site at the end of October recently, and on January 11, 2019, celebrated the celebration. One year anniversary of the signing of this construction project.
To be informed that the building to be constructed has an average weight of 3 to 5 tons Helicopter Airport on the roof of the building in accordance with the additional request from the Cambodian side, and this building is divided into sections for a number of functions such as: outpatient, emergency Medical technology, general medicine, surgery and other support services.
Kosomak Hospital is a national public hospital in Phnom Penh, built in 1953 and completed and started operating in 1956 under the patronage of Queen Yani Kosomak, the mother of the King. He treated monks and operated until April 17, 1975, formerly known as "Kosomak Hospital" and was discontinued during the Pol Pot regime.
The hospital was reopened on June 16, 1979, with the Ministry of Health transforming it from a hospital for the treatment of monks to a polyclinic for people and monks, especially those requiring surgery by the ministry. The hospital is divided into 200 beds, divided into sections.
(Banteay Meanchey): General Ke Kim Yan, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Central Working Group for Banteay Meanchey Province, on January 11, 2019, presided over the dissemination ceremony of the spirit of the Central Committee Meeting. 41 Fifth mandate, Banteay Meanchey province, with nearly 1,200 members.
On that occasion, General Ke Kim Yan had a talk and brought greetings from the top leaders of the party: Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Party President Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Honorary President of the party Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Party Vice President Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Party Vice President.
General Ke Kim Yan stated that the Royal Government of the sixth mandate, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and President of the Cambodian People's Party, has continued its mission to serve the people towards prosperity in all aspects through a commitment to achieve great guarantees. The four things for people are:
1. Ensuring the protection of peace, stability, security and safety of villages and communes for the well-being of the people everywhere, protecting the independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity without being violated or destroyed by any force.
2. Ensuring continued economic and social development in all areas, focusing on governance reform to strengthen public institutions and build a clean administration, as well as increase efficiency and improve the quality of public services, strengthen a stable, resilient and resilient macroeconomic environment. Sustainable growth, environment and equity focus on investing in human capital and increasing attractiveness and supporting economic activity.
4. Ensuring social peace and stability in the lives of people both now and in the future through the development and strengthening of effective and sustainable social protection systems for all people, especially for the poor and vulnerable groups. Do not let any people suffer without attention.
At the same time, General Ke Kim Yan thanked the leaders and members at all levels for leading and serving the people faithfully and asked all to continue to unite to maintain peace, strengthen national unity and jointly maintain National achievements to be sustainable for the benefit of mankind for all generations forever. Tycoon Ly Hour continues as President of the Cambodian Housing Developers Association in the second mandate
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Oknha Ly Hour has been re-elected as the President of the Cambodian Housing Developers Association in the second mandate after being trusted by the members of the Association and re-elected Mr. Oknha Ly Hour this afternoon, January 11, 2019 in Opportunity for the Second General Assembly.
In response to the confidence of the members, Mr. Ly Hour said, "I would like to thank the leadership and members, and I would like to set seven strategic directions and strategic plans for the implementation of this second mandate."
1: Expand the prestige of the association for local and international construction investors to know more.
2: Attract new housing construction investment companies to become members of the association as much as possible.
3. Establish a local business forum to strengthen and expand relations with relevant institutions, including the framework of associations, public institutions and the local and international private sector.
4. Strengthen the internal association by organizing internal meetings, holding extraordinary meetings to discuss issues that affect the investment of members.
5: Establish a partnership mechanism between the Royal Government and the private sector with stakeholders in each sector, such as: Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Ministry of Economy and Finance, General Department of Taxation, General Department of Industry, Finance, Phnom Penh Capital Hall Electricite du Cambodge, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority and other institutions.
6: Establish a working group to study, research and compile real estate data in collaboration with relevant authorities.
