(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has announced 11 important work directions for implementation in 2019 related to the provision of public services to the people and in accordance with the recommendations of the Royal Government.
The work direction for 2019 was raised by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on the occasion of the closing meeting of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport at Chaktomuk Conference Hall on January 10, 2019. The ceremony was presided over by Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The 11 directions include:
1: Road transport: * Increase the relationship and cooperation between the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, General Department and Excise, General Department of Taxation and General Department of Identification to facilitate the provision of public services to the people. Special labels to raise funds for the state provide convenient options for vehicle owners and strengthen vehicle management.
4: Inland waterway transport and port (2019 is the year to promote water transport services): * Continue to finalize the draft law on ports and water transport law. * Study the procedure of Re-register the Cambodian flagship. * Promote efficient inland shipping.
8: Phnom Penh Port: * Promote the construction of the closed river port, the third phase of the container port development project and the construction of the river satellite port, the construction of the cargo port and the establishment of the dry storage port-cold storage area to increase capacity and facilitate Water transport service.
9: Sihanoukville Autonomous Port: * Ground construction of a 350-meter-long container port with a water depth of 14.5 meters, a container yard, pumping and restoring a 14.5-meter-deep tank with a Japanese loan ($ 203 million). * Learn more at Sihanoukville Port Special Economic Zone.
