Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges journalists to work together to prevent fake news by revealing true information (video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on January 11, 2019 All journalists join the fight against fake news, because in Cambodia, fake news is happening a lot, and in order to eliminate fake news, it is necessary to publish the real news together.
This encouragement of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made on the evening of January 11, 2019 on the occasion of presiding over a meeting with more than 5,000 journalists at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center. Samdech Techo also continued to call on journalists to cover the incident, not to try to be a judge, and journalists are not the judicial police to put a car parade.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia said: "Ask all journalists and all media institutions to join the fight against fake news, fake news, it is very common in Cambodia, happy Regarding myself, whether How many suddenly opened to see Mr. Hun Sen just died a little earlier, please join the mourning, it is like this.
In the third meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and journalists on the evening of January 11, 2019, Samdech Techo also disagreed with the idea of wanting to have international standards in the field of information, because this point is not consistent. No, only sports.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I want the media to contribute to the analysis of the strategic level in the country, region and internationally. "I watched a roundtable and I do not agree with the idea of having an international standard in the field of information, because only sports have an international standard."
According to the Prime Minister, if a common international standard is applied to politics, it is clearly impossible. In the world, all countries have different policies, some countries have democracies. There is a prime minister, and some countries practice liberal politics and some countries practice communist politics.
As for the media sector in Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised journalists to contribute to the analysis at the strategic level in the country, region and internationally, as he wanted the universities in Cambodia to participate in this issue as well.
In addition, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia would like to ask all journalists to join the fight against fake news, because in Cambodia, fake news is happening a lot, and in order to eliminate fake news, it is necessary to jointly publish true information.
The request was made during a meeting with nearly 5,000 journalists at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center in Phnom Penh on the evening of January 11, 2019.
On the other hand, the head of the Royal Government also forbade the advertisers and users of the social network Facebook, not to be a professor, interpret, analyze problems or nominate a judge or a court to try things that lead to misunderstanding or cause long problems. Farther.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also urged the media to stop broadcasting information that is insulting to each other because it is not beneficial to the media.
