Green (Cambodia) Plc. Ranks No. 1 in Cambodia as the largest exporter of rice in 2018
Green Company, which has the largest, most modern and most capable factory in Battambang province, started producing, processing and exporting rice to international markets from 2010 to the present.
Since 2008, the company has established "Green Community" farming communities in villages, communes, districts in Battambang, Pursat and Banteay Meanchey provinces. Through the establishment of this green community, all community members, who are local farmers, are very satisfied and supportive that the green company of Duke Phu Puy has helped solve many important issues, especially market and price issues.
The green company has established a market to collect from local community members, maintaining the balance of market demand for rice, as well as affordable prices for farmers. It should be noted that in November 2018, the green company also received the award "Best Rice Producer". 410 families in 2 Thnou commune agree to accept the distribution of 2 hectares of land per family and promise to stop protesting in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): 410 families in dispute with Memot Rubber Plantation Company in 2 Thnou Commune, Snoul District, Kratie Province agree to accept the distribution of 2 hectares of land per family to be managed according to the social land concession procedure and promise to stop Up to protest in Phnom Penh.
According to the press release, on January 11, 2019 at 10:30 am at Wat Samaki Rainsy, the working group of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Kratie Provincial Authority and Phnom Penh Capital Hall met with representatives of the people. 410 people came to protest the dispute related to the economic land concession that the Royal Government handed over to Memot Rubber Plantation Company in 2 Thnou commune, Snuol district, Kratie province.
Citizens' representatives agreed to return to the local level to cooperate with the working group and local authorities to inspect the location of land designated by the provincial authorities for distribution according to the social land concession procedure on Monday, January 14, 2019 and to accept the distribution Social land concession size of 2 hectares per family to be managed according to the social land concession procedure.
