Mr. Sam Virak also stated that due to the geography of Banteay Meanchey province in the past during the tripartite war, this area was a hot battle area of armed conflict between Cambodia and Cambodia, making the area with anti-personnel mines and anti-tank mines and weapons. Unexploded ordnance scattered in the ground, which poses a risk to our people.
On the occasion of inspecting demining activities in Pong commune, Malai district, Banteay Meanchey province, General Meas Sophea also praised the high level of self-sacrifice of the 1st CMAC demining force in Malai district to liberate Land to the people.
