(Sihanoukville): In 2018, exports from Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone amounted to about 372 million US dollars, an increase of about 68% compared to exports in 2017. This is according to the press release of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on January 11, 2019.
On the morning of January 10, 2019, in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, the third meeting of the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone Coordinating Committee was chaired by Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Development Council. Cambodia and Qian Keming, Chinese Deputy Minister of Commerce.
The third meeting of the Coordinating Committee was held within the framework of the Cooperation Agreement between Cambodia and China on the Development of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, signed on December 13, 2010.
Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone is located in Prey Nob District, Sihanoukville Province, approximately 13 km from Sihanoukville Port. 1,113 hectares.
At present, the company has set up local infrastructure on an area of 628 hectares, such as: roads, electricity, clean water, wastewater treatment system, administrative office building, vocational training center, etc.
Currently, in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, 161 companies have registered investments with a total capital of approximately 918 million US dollars and employed 22,495 people in various industries such as:
In 2018, exports from Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone amounted to 372 million US dollars, an increase of about 68% compared to 2017.
Readers' views: Journalists rush to buy coats to meet Prime Minister Hun Sen
(Phnom Penh): The third annual meeting between Prime Minister Hun Sen and journalists will take place at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center on the afternoon of January 11, 2019 under the coordination and organization of the Ministry of Information. According to a source from the Ministry of Information, about 4,500 journalists will attend the forum.
The third annual meeting highlighted Prime Minister Hun Sen's concern with journalists in the context of Cambodia's adherence to the path of liberal multi-party democracy, in which the media also has an important role to play in maintaining peace and political stability. This is a golden opportunity for building and developing the country's economy while Cambodia is focusing on industry, services, agriculture, especially tourism, which is a source of national income to boost economic growth.
On January 10, Prime Minister Hun Sen said on his personal Facebook page that the country's progress could not be separated from the participation of journalists. He said that Cambodia had lost the opportunity to build the country for many years due to the war. After the country is completely peaceful, Cambodia needs many tourists, traders and foreign investors to invest in Cambodia.
"Therefore, participating in the dissemination of real positive news is giving more confidence to foreign tourists and foreign investors. At the same time, the Prime Minister thanked all national and international journalists, including online media and all social media users who participated in disseminating Cambodia to the world in a positive way for Cambodia to grow faster. .
In terms of access to information, Cambodians today are a paradise of freedom. According to figures from the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, out of 16 million Cambodians, 27 million use mobile phones.
However, the third annual meeting between the press and the Prime Minister was expressed by the journalists who were supportive and proud to participate in this important forum. Therefore, on the morning of January 11, 2019, before the meeting with the Prime Minister, it was seen that many journalists rushed to buy clothes (jackets) in the markets and clothing stores to dress appropriately. Meet with the Prime Minister in the evening of the same day.
