The new website of Angkor Institute has been officially launched!
The official launch of the new Angkor Foundation website was presided over by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, after the Deputy Prime Minister chaired the 9th First Mandate Board Meeting. Angkor Institute this morning.
The press release states that the launch of the new website is intended to be attractive and provide a lot of additional information to the local and international public, and in particular provide immediate practical information on ticket sales at Angkor.
The new website of Angkor Institute will also provide some information on tourism in Angkor and temples to help promote tourism and make it easier for tourists to organize their trips.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Donates a School Building to Khmak Secondary School in Stong District, Kampong Thom Province
(Kampong Thom): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen donated a school building to Khmak Secondary School in Stong District, Kampong Thom Province. The school building that was handed over to Khmak Secondary School has 2 floors and 12 classrooms.
A school building was provided by Mr. Chea Chanto, Permanent Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the National Working Group to Assist Stong District as a New Commitment to Celebrate the 40th Anniversary of Victory Day January 7.
The new school building, a bond between Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, was announced by Mr. Chea Chanto during the celebration of the 40th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day, which was held in Santuk District on January 11, 2019. .
Mr. Theam Vuthea, Director of Khmak Secondary School, said that at present, the secondary school has 530 students, 327 of whom are female, and has 11 classrooms. He added that the school currently lacks one class and in the new school year may lack up to seven classes, although in mid-2016, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit provided a building with six rooms.
Mr. Chea Chanto said that the spirit of January 7 will remain immortal in the hearts of the Cambodian people and will be a solid foundation for peace and national development.
He continued that January 7 brings peace and development like today, and that is why the Cambodian people named January 7 as their second birthday, because without the January 7 victory, Cambodia would not have anything like today.
On that occasion, Mr. Chea Chanto called on the participants as well as all Cambodians to adhere to the spirit of national unity as a whole to develop the country to get more new development.
