(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, on Friday evening, January 11, 2019, will be honored to meet here And fresh solidarity meal with journalists at Koh Pich Center.
This evening's meeting is the third time, while the first meeting was held in January 2017. Mr. Phos Sovann, Director General of the General Department of Information and Audiovisual and spokesman for the Ministry of Information, said that the number of participants in the third meeting with Samdech Techo Prime Minister was about 4,500.
Mr. Phos Sovann confirmed that the third meeting of local journalists with Samdech Techo Prime Minister has increased more than the previous meeting because this meeting was attended by the governor of the capital-province, including ministers in some ministries. Also.
The fact that Samdech Techo Hun Sen was honored to meet with this group of journalists is a rare thing that no leader has ever done. Such a meeting is a demonstration of the Prime Minister of Cambodia's attention to the media, which is a huge space to share news and information to the people as well as to the international arena.
Yesterday, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that journalists are an indispensable partner of the Royal Government in national development. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called on the media to help promote Cambodia to the world to attract tourists and foreign investors to Cambodia.
On behalf of the Ministry of Information, which is the guardian of the media in Cambodia, Mr. Phos Sovann saw the meeting between the Prime Minister and the media as an opening of democracy and freedom of the press in Cambodia by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, regardless of tendencies. That.
During a meeting between the head of the Royal Government and journalists, Mr. Phos Sovann saw that the media sector is growing and improving because journalists have received some guidance and improvement from the country's top leaders.
Journalists were pleased to meet directly with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as an opportunity to receive some advice on the dissemination of the head of the Royal Government. At the same time, some journalists took this opportunity to propose to the Prime Minister to have better cooperation from the ministries and institutions of the state to facilitate the coverage.
Mondulkiri Cam Control Officer brought a mobile laboratory vehicle to inspect goods at Sen Monorom Market and exhibition hall, but did not find any products containing banned chemicals
(Mondulkiri): CamControl Branch, Mondulkiri Province, led by Mr. Chan Veasna, Branch Manager, in collaboration with the Department of Commerce and the Laboratory Team of the General Department of CamControl, this morning, January 11, 2019, brought a laboratory vehicle. Mobile food inspection at Sen Monorom Exhibition Center and Sen Monorom Market in Mondulkiri Province.
Mr. Chan Veasna, Head of Camcontrol Branch in Mondulkiri Province, said that the inspection team inspected 26 items at the exhibition venue and inspected them by mobile laboratory vehicles for banned chemicals. As a result, our officials did not find any products containing banned chemicals.
The branch manager continued that during the inspection of Sen Monorom market, CamControl officers took 46 samples and as a result, our officials did not find any products that contain banned chemicals. In addition to inspecting the food, officials confiscated a total of 38 kilograms of expired goods and burned them.
