The Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment said on January 10, 2019 that Boeung Lomkot is a natural lake rich in natural resources, forests, wildlife and beautiful scenery and other rich ecosystems. Is attracting tourists to visit there, which is why the Ministry of Environment proposed to designate this lake as a protected area.
According to the Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment, the current protected area system includes a total of nearly 60 protected areas and biodiversity corridors covering an area of 7.5 million hectares under the protection and conservation management of the Ministry of Environment. The Royal Government of Cambodia and the Ministry of Environment have taken the necessary measures to protect and conserve natural resources for generations to come.
