Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth: Preliminary estimate for 2018, Cambodia's economic growth rate can reach around 7.3%
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, said that the preliminary estimate of Cambodia's economic growth rate in 2018 could reach around 7.3%, which is derived from the increase. Strong growth in the construction sector, garments, tourism, including telecommunications and transportation.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth said this on the afternoon of January 10, 2019, when he presided over the closing ceremony of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. The ceremony was also attended by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, as well as many officials at all levels at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall.
Mr. Aun Porn Moniroth said that based on the results achieved above, Cambodia has set its aspirations higher to become a high middle income country by 2030 and become an income country. High by 2050.
He said that at the same time, Cambodia has been strengthening connections with countries in all polar regions and major economic corridors in the country and the launch of a local logistics system that will contribute more and more to the promotion. Competitiveness and local trade promotion further support Cambodia's economic growth.
Kampong Speu CamControl Branch Inspected Goods at 3 Markets and Shops on National Road 4
(Kampong Speu): CamControl Kampong Speu Branch on January 10, 2019, in cooperation with the officials of Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Commerce, inspected three markets: Prey Pdao Market, Trapeang Ampil Market, Samaki Market and shops along the National Road. No. 4, 9 shops.
In this operation, the technical staff inspected the compliance with the technical standards on the packaging products in order to ensure fair trade competition and consumer protection, and to ensure that traders stop selling pre-packaged food. With unbranded packaging, the correct address in accordance with technical standards will face revocation and legal liability.
In addition, officials explained to guide traders to understand the consequences of using banned chemicals on food products or food processing that endanger health. Understand the hygienic nature of the display and the legal responsibilities of food safety and be careful to avoid expired, damaged and counterfeit goods.
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia-Vietnam issued a joint press release after the 10th Meeting on Cooperation and Development of Cambodia-Vietnam Border Provinces on January 9-10, 2019 in Ho Chi Minh City, Social Republic. Vietnamese.
The meeting was chaired by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, with Mr. Pham Binh Minh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
The full text of the joint statement between Cambodia and Vietnam is as follows:
The two sides stressed the importance of maintaining friendly relations and cooperation in the Cambodia-Vietnam border provinces, as well as strengthening and expanding ties at the village level, as well as traditional friendship and cooperation in all fields. Between Cambodia and Vietnam
Both sides highly appreciated the exchange of visits between senior leaders of the two countries.
The two sides praised the efforts of the ministries and institutions of the two countries in actively cooperating in building the legal framework and implementing all cooperation mechanisms to facilitate the cooperation of border provinces. According to the direction set at the 9th Meeting on Cooperation and Development of Cambodia-Vietnam Border Provinces
Both sides praised the importance of national security cooperation in maintaining peace, stability and security of each country, and reiterated that no organization or individual should be allowed to use the territory. Of one country to endanger the national security and stability of the other country
* Both sides welcome the agreement to upgrade the Men Chey border checkpoint (Prey Veng province), Tan Nam (Tai Ninh province) to the international border gate and to complete the preparations for the official inauguration at the appropriate time as well as Completion of the procedure for upgrading the Bos Mon border gate (Svay Rieng province) - Phuoc Ton (Tay Ninh province) to a bilateral border gate
Both sides also agreed to push for the construction of roads and bridges across the border.
The two sides agreed to set common goals to strengthen and enhance cooperation in agriculture, forestry and fisheries.
* In the field of health, both sides praised the results of cooperation in the past.
Both sides praised the results of cooperation in the field of information and propaganda
The two sides agreed to hold the 11th Meeting on Cooperation and Development of Cambodia-Vietnam Border Provinces in the Kingdom of Cambodia in 2020.
Ms. Ke Leng was selected as the World's Best Patent Candidate for 2018, representing Cambodia to compete through online voting among many candidates from around the world. She is the only Cambodian heroine who has won the world gold medal in four patent competitions: 2013 in France, 2015 in Thailand, 2017 in China and 2018 in the country. French again.
Presiding over the press conference, Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, called on the people to vote together so that Ke Leng's heroic candidate can succeed in honor of this great Cambodian nation. He believes that unity will definitely make Cambodia raise the flag on the international stage.
At the same time, Ms. Keo Leng thanked the Royal Government for always supporting and giving her the opportunity to show her ability in many world-class competitions. She also urged all types of athletes to train hard to develop themselves to become the best athletes for the country.
* In 2017: Ms. Ke Leng won the World Patent Gold Medal in Scoring in the Republic of China for the third time. This is a record for Ms. Ke Leng to win three gold medals in a row.
* In addition: In 2018, France has organized a petanque competition among the strongest countries in the world. In this competition, Ms. Ke Leng won the first prize in 2 to 2 and 3 to 3 events by defeating the strong countries such as France, Thailand and Tunisia.
