In fact, a pit named Hoeun is digging more than 1 hectare behind Kampong Svay commune hall, Kien Svay district, Kandal province. There are no rules and the transport is not covered, not watered, and the dust affects people's homes and crops.
Residents said that despite their difficulties, the commune authorities did not care and even allowed the traders to drive the land truck through the commune hall gates, not knowing how much the commune authorities benefited from the traders. . Fresh News did not have the commune chief's phone number for comment. Direct flights between Beijing and Phnom Penh are launched for the first time!
Mr. Chea Oun further stated that the launch of the flight helped save time, which took only 6 hours from Phnom Penh to Beijing, which previously took up to 10 hours.
According to the senior official, the first flight from Phnom Penh to Beijing not only boosts economic growth, investment from China to Cambodia, but also attracts tourism between Cambodia and China. He said that initially, Air China flies only three flights a week, but in the future, the company will fly daily.
Please be informed that China and Cambodia are great friends who have been interested in diplomacy for more than 60 years. This close relationship has spurred Chinese investment as well as Chinese tourists in Cambodia. Due to the increase in investment and tourists, there have been a series of flights connecting Cambodia and China.
Kampong Cham Governor Welcomes Investors to Invest in the Province
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, on January 10, 2019, stated that the Kampong Cham Provincial Authority fully supports the legal status of investors who come to invest in Kampong Cham Province.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Kouch Chamroeun's participation in the meeting to prepare a guidebook for investment with relevant departments and units and with the participation of the Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association and Entrepreneurs in Kampong Cham, which organized At the small meeting hall of Kampong Cham Provincial Hall this morning, January 10, 2019.
The provincial governor said that in relation to the service, Kampong Cham provincial authorities already have three OWSOs to provide separate services, in 2019, the provincial authorities will establish three OWSOs. And in 2020, the OWSO will be established in all 10 cities and districts in Kampong Cham province.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun continued that Kampong Cham is a province with labor potential, which has a population of more than 1 million people. According to the provincial governor, in some provinces, there are many factories, but there is a shortage of labor, while in Kampong Cham, there is a crisis of labor.
He said that the current men in the factories are not accepted to work, that is, only women are hired to work, which makes a large number of male workers unemployed. And so much of the rest of the male workforce could result in them using drugs or resorting to violence or committing other crimes.
He added that on the other hand, if Kampong Cham province has a lot of factories and factory owners change their attitude to accept male labor to work, they will have responsibilities to do and have a salary and social problems. Reduction as well.
