Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign on January 9: 535 illegal vehicles found and 376 fines
(Phnom Penh): Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign For January 9, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 2,424 vehicles, found 535 vehicles violated the law (80% motorcycles), educated 159 vehicles and fined 376 This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 1,322 helmets and goggles were inspected on January 9, 110 education helmets and 225 glasses were fined.
Former Khmer Rouge soldiers in Oddar Meanchey province receive 7 houses from Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Oddar Meanchey): Former Khmer Rouge soldiers in Chongkal district, Oddar Meanchey province, most of whom were disabled due to the flames of war in the 1980s, received housing from the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. .
Seven houses made of 5 meters by 5 meters of galvanized iron and 3 meters of galvanized iron roof were handed over by Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, to veterans and former Khmer Rouge soldiers in Bat Thkov village, commune. Chongkal, Chongkal district, Oddar Meanchey province on January 9, 2019. The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey.
Speaking on that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim also brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to greet the veterans, then the Senior Minister instructed members who come to live here to keep clean to prevent disease and to take care of the house. Receive.
At the same time, the Senior Minister Secretary-General instructed the provincial governor to assign offices and offices around the province to support the veterans in their new arrival.
At the request of the members who came here without land to grow crops, Senior Minister Kun Kim requested Samdech Techo Hun Sen and was allowed to settle the existing land per family of 2 hectares.
By adhering to the three main policies of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy (securing life, securing a career and securing property), former Khmer Rouge soldiers in Oddar Meanchey province have retained their occupational positions and assets. After integration at the end of 1998.
To date, former Khmer Rouge soldiers who have been crippled by the flames of war and suffered various hardships have received high attention from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, such as providing housing and solving various difficulties.
The seven families of former Khmer Rouge soldiers who received housing and land for cultivation expressed their excitement and gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for always thinking of them.
Minister of Agriculture: Rosewood is a rare species, it is necessary to establish an additional institution to prevent deforestation and trafficking
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, has just decided to establish a new institution, the National Permanent Secretariat for the Prevention and Suppression of Logging, Transportation, Collection, Storage and Export of Rosewood. " The Minister said that the establishment of this Secretariat to prevent the destruction and trafficking of rosewood, a rare species in Cambodia to be more effective.
The minister added that the working group of the Secretariat is not only working on rosewood crimes, but also on other timber crimes.
Answer the question, to what extent will this new institution be able to crack down on rosewood crime? Mr. Veng Sakhon has not been able to confirm this, he pointed out that the crime of trafficking in luxury wood, including rosewood is complicated, traders have a lot of tricks. However, Mr. Veng Sakhon is determined to work hard to prevent the crime of rosewood as well as other luxury wood as much as possible.
Please note that the National Permanent Secretariat for the Prevention and Suppression of Logging, Transportation, Collection, Storage and Export of Rosewood is composed of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Ministry of National Defense, Ministry of Interior, Ministry of Environment, Ministry of Environment and Police. National Armed Forces and provincial governors as well.
