Cambodian, Thai military chiefs pledge to strengthen ties of solidarity and cooperation along the border for the prosperity of both countries
(Preah Vihear): The Chief of Staff of Cambodia and the Chief of Staff of Thailand on January 9, 2019, pledged to continue to strengthen the bonds of solidarity and good cooperation along the border line for the progress of both countries and peoples. The commitment of the commanders of the two countries was made at a meeting at An Ses Pass in An Ses Village, Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province.
The Cambodian side led the meeting, led by Lt. Gen. Srey Duek, Deputy Commander of the Army and Commander of the 3rd Intervention Brigade, Chairman of the 1st Battle Command, Preah Vihear Temple, and attended by Mr. Chea Kimseng, Governor of Choam Ksan District and leaders. Many members of the Armed Forces. The Thai side was led by Colonel Nat Sin, Deputy Commander of the Sura Neary Force and the Governor of Nam Yeun District, Ubon Ratchathani Province, as well as several other forces.
He said that the implementation of the principles of the two Prime Ministers announced the opening of international border crossings along the Cambodian-Thai border, including the An Ses international border crossing. He said that the committee of the Ministry of Cambodia, Thailand and the provinces and provinces have sent a team to measure and still proceed according to the law and decide later.
He stressed that the problem is not one year can open because it takes a long time, maybe a year or more to open before if it works well. At the same time, he urged the Thai side to do the same as before for the sale of the people, to do as before, not to limit the purchase of goods for the livelihood of the people on both sides.
Separately, Lt. Col. Nat Sien also agreed to the proposals made by the Cambodian side and urged the border forces to meet frequently to resolve various challenges, and to the Cambodian side's request not to limit trade issues. He will take this request to report to the Commander of the Thai Armed Forces to deal with later. More specifically, more profit for customers on the occasion of the 5th anniversary of BMW!
