Indonesian Ambassador: Indonesia-Cambodia trade ties increase by 10%
(Phnom Penh): The Indonesian Ambassador to Cambodia said that in terms of trade volume between Indonesia and Cambodia over the past 10 years, it has increased by about 10 percent, especially considering the trade volume between the two countries. During 2018, it was worth more than 600 million US dollars.
He said that day by day, the trade volume and the people of the two countries have a better relationship, and in particular, the two countries have also encouraged more investment. Apparently, now the Indonesian and Cambodian companies have jointly set up Dynamite Agen.
