(Phnom Penh): Mr. Takano Norima, Editor-in-Chief of the Japanese Business Magazine (CBP), said that while Cambodia is peaceful and politically stable, Cambodia's development is progressing in all areas, which is why foreign investors come to invest. Here more.
In fact, the number of Japanese investors is also higher, according to a report by the Ministry of Commerce, saying that in 2010, only 19 Japanese companies in Cambodia were registered with the Ministry of Commerce. But since 2014, more than 200 Japanese companies have registered to do business in Cambodia every year.
The editor-in-chief said that as of 2017, the number of Japanese people living in Cambodia was about 3,518 and will continue to increase in 2019. Therefore, Japanese investment will continue to increase. Especially when Japan received real and comprehensive information about investment potential in Cambodia.
In addition, Mr. Takano Norima said that because the Japanese people do not know a foreign language, so the five years of the establishment of the Japanese business magazine CBP in Japanese, he noted that the magazine has contributed to bring Real information from Cambodia to Japan and Japanese investors around the world to know and come to invest.
