The speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made this morning, January 9, 2019, on the occasion of opening the mission to meet with workers for 2019, a total of 18,273 people from 12 factories in Takeo province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "January 7 does not belong to the Cambodian People's Party. January 7 belongs to all Cambodians who want to live as human beings. So no one pays anyone, because January 7 is theirs, January 7 belongs to their ancestors, belongs to your parents, and it becomes your property to be kept.
In addition, the Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia also noted that the achievements of 40 years after the day of liberation are unimaginable, that is, Cambodia is now progressing in all areas and at the same time. That Cambodia continues to maintain the peace that was hard to find in the past.
Please be informed that the January 7 Victory Day, which Cambodia celebrated on the morning of January 7, 2019, is the 40th anniversary of the liberation of Cambodia from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, or simply called the 3rd regime. 8 months and 20 days that killed more than 3 million innocent Cambodians.
Forty years after the fall of the Killing Fields regime, if we look at Phnom Penh, it is crowded with more than 2 million people and people who come to do business and study. More than 1 million more. At the same time, they also observed the expansion of the area of the capital with the increase of small and large buildings high and low.
