The Royal Theater "Neang Vathana Tevy" will be performed to the public for the first time in history
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Ballet "Neang Vathana Tevy" appeared for the first time to His Majesty the King of Life and Her Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia in May 2018 at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall in Phnom Penh. Subsequently, Princess Ream Norodom Bopha Devi led this extraordinary royal play to be performed overseas: France, Switzerland and the United Arab Emirates.
"The performance of Neang Vathana Tevy will bring you to know more about the soul of the Khmer identity," said Princess Ream Norodom Bopha Devi, a famous former royal dancer in the 1960s.
"This performance, which is more than 100 years old, will give the audience an exciting experience, giving the audience the feeling that they are on a journey back to the past and discovering legends related to the origins of people and cultures. Khmer ”according to Samdech Preah Ream, who is the leader and trainer of dancers.
The Royal Ballet was inscribed on the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity list on November 7, 2003 by UNESCO. In particular, this time the performance will be in the form of a play because it is the story of "Neang Vathana Tevy" is not a form of royal dance like Tep Apsara Dance, Tep Monorom Dance, Sovanmacha Dance or Makar Dance.
Prince Sisowath Teso, special adviser to Princess Ream Bopha Devi, said that the Khmer Royal Theater was very special. French artist Ogos Rhodin became fascinated with Khmer drama and painted up to 150 Khmer dances everywhere during King Sisowath's visit in 1906.
Watch this rare performance of "Neang Vathana Tevy" to support the wonderful Khmer culture.
