(Phnom Penh): On January 9, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, opened a mission to meet with workers for 2019. For the first mission for 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with a total of 18,273 workers from 12 factories in Takeo province.
This morning's meeting took place in Champol village, Popel commune, Tram Kak district, Takeo province. According to Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that the meeting between Samdech Techo and workers today is the third meeting for Takeo province.
According to the Minister, the workers who met with Samdech Techo Hun Sen from three local factories were: Samrong, Bati and Tram Kak districts. The factories run five garments, four shoes, one bag, one mobile phone accessory and one artificial hair.
According to the Minister, these products are for export to international markets and supply to domestic markets. Minister Ith Sam Heng also mentioned the current working situation in Takeo province.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that at present, Takeo province has a total of 164 enterprises and establishments, with 48,168 workers earning a total of 163 million dollars per year. There are 51 garment and footwear factories with 39,943 workers with a total salary of nearly 135 million US dollars per year.
The Minister considered the optimal situation of the industrial sector in Takeo province as the success of the policy of attracting investment, the deployment of factories in the provinces, the national policy on employment and employment, the policy of industrial development in Cambodia, the policy. On Technical and Vocational Education and Training and the National Social Protection Policy Framework of the Royal Government of Cambodia led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Through the series of visits, the challenges have been solved and many benefits have been decided by Samdech Techo Hun Sen as a principle for workers.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training is also closely monitoring 10 jobs to ensure the benefits for workers. The 10 jobs include:
