Monivong Bokor National Park, the intersection of the tourist paradise and the vast ocean (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Monivong Bokor National Park, also known as Phnom Bokor, is designed to provide a series of infrastructure to serve the travel of tourists. As well as making existing tourism products more attractive, as well as creating many new tourism products to visit.
Today, on Bokor Mountain, there are five major tourist attractions that tourists can visit: cultural sites, ancient buildings, temples, shrines, a hundred rice fields, flower fields, natural lakes, mountains, entertainment at the Vihear Hotel Christianity, Chinese temples, etc. This is according to Mr. Soy Sinal, Director of Kampot Provincial Department of Tourism.
On October 9, 2017, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, publicly announced that visits to Monivong Bokor National Park and Thansur Bokor Resort are no longer required.
Bokor Mountain, later renamed Monivong Bokor National Park, was discovered in 1916 by a Frenchman named Roulous and was developed into a popular colonial resort. French, that is, during the reign of King Sisowath.
It was not until 1993 that the Cambodian government, which emerged from the UN-controlled elections, declared Bokor Mountain a national park called "Monivong Bokor National Park" and in 1997 it was opened to the public. Tourists come to visit again.
