Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of opening the mission to visit workers for the new year, meeting with nearly 20,000 workers in Takeo province
* As the beginning of this morning's conversation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen wished all workers happiness and prosperity in the new year.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that who would have thought that Takeo province has a factory that makes smartphone accessories. This is the achievement of Cambodia for 40 years after the liberation on January 7, 1979.
* Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, stated that the achievements of 40 years after the day of liberation were unexpected. Samdech Techo reminded that Phnom Penh without people after the day of liberation is more difficult than living in the mountains.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia has only 20 years to develop its nation, with attempts to prevent unscrupulous people by mobilizing foreigners from investing in Cambodia.
* The Prime Minister stated that Cambodia could not rely on agriculture alone, as in Pol Pot's policy, but on other sectors.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen described that Samdech did not expect that Cambodia can develop as it is now, because it does not know how to lead if the country has nothing after the day of liberation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the development of Cambodia's industry in the field of textiles, garments and footwear, with two countries with only four factories with more than 20,000 workers with a wage of $ 40 in 1997 to become a rich country About 12,000 factories, enterprises and workplaces employ 1.5 million workers with a wage of about $ 182.
* Samdech Prime Minister asked how many people can imagine that Tram Kak district as well as Takeo province has many such factories?
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order to succeed in the policy of attracting investors to invest in potential areas, the Royal Government has made great efforts to build roads and connect to the electricity grid.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has no problem in raising the salaries of civil servants every two weeks in 2019. Samdech Techo confirmed that the budget is ready.
* Samdech Techo stated that along with the increase in salaries, we must work together to stabilize the price of goods in the market so that the fruits of the increase in wages and salaries can reach the workers and civil servants.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that without the March 18, 1970 coup, Cambodia would have prospered. But this coup destroyed Cambodia. Samdech Techo thanked all the people for working together to preserve peace.
* Samdech Techo also thanked the people for choosing democracy and maintaining peace by going to the polls and voting for the Cambodian People's Party.
* Samdech Techo continues to call on employers and workers to unite to make peace in the factory.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the country that produces clothes and shoes is not only in Cambodia, and employers are more likely to invest in countries with lower wages than in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if the factory had to close, the first victims would be the workers. Samdech Techo confirmed that the Royal Government has released about 22 million dollars to solve the problem of salaries and seniority when the day of the factory.
* The Prime Minister stated that if the demands of the workers are followed, about two-thirds of the factories will be closed.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked workers to understand not to force factory owners to pay seniority by 2018. The Prime Minister said that the seniority money will not be lost, it will be open for six months from 2019.
* The Prime Minister called on the unions that are moving the workers to demand the payment of seniority pay by 2018 to stop their activities.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen appealed to workers that if any union leads to a bad situation, do not believe in the pull of the union.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces not to talk about the former CNRP. Samdech stated that whoever wants to go, go anywhere. Samdech Techo's remarks after the law amnesty for banned politicians came into force.
