Agriculture Minister Urges Thai Company to Invest in Cassava Processing Plant in Oddar Meanchey
The director of the company informed the Minister that the company originated from Thailand and has invested in the agro-industrial sector in Cambodia, the company has received the principle of establishing a cassava processing plant from the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts since the end of 2017. The company is currently completing the construction of the plant and is preparing for the processing process in the near future.
By 2020, the company plans to expand cassava processing from 40,000 to 50,000 tons and increase processing to 200,000 tons in the future. At the same time, the company also plans to establish cassava plantations and plantations on 4,000 hectares of land in Oddar Meanchey province's Samrong district to ensure sustainable supply.
On that occasion, the Minister expressed his congratulations to the companies that have invested in Cambodia, and the Minister also supported the establishment of cassava plantations and plantations in Cambodia.
The Minister instructed the company to implement contract production by identifying potential planting sites for cassava, while the provinces bordering Oddar Meanchey also have potential for this crop.
Finally, the Minister instructed the company to continue to cooperate with relevant officials to discuss procedures to support the successful investment.
