(Banteay Meanchey): The Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie on January 08, 2019 held a press conference on the crackdown on 1 kg of drugs and arrested two suspects. The crackdown was led by Lt. Col. Bun Soeung, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie, in charge of drug crime under the coordination of Ms. Chheng Hak Nging, Deputy Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
In a press conference held on January 8, 2019, Colonel Bun Soeung said that the crackdown on the Office of Anti-Drug Crimes on January 6, 2019 in cooperation with the force. The Poipet City Gendarmerie Base cracked down on drug trafficking and arrested two suspects at the northern point of the fishing pond in Sam Kik Meanchey Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Colonel Bun Soeung said that after receiving information about the drug trafficking, he reported to Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie, to ask for guidelines under the coordination of Ms. Chheng Hak Nging. He then led the crackdown until the arrest of two suspects.
He confirmed that the first suspect, Pek Sen Sovann, male, 39 years old, farmer, lives in Achar Lak village, Sangkat Prey Tahou, Steung Sen city, Kampong Thom province, and the second suspect, Pich Ratha, 23 years old, casino worker, living in a rented room in Kbal Spean village. 1 Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province. The force confiscated 1,015.2 grams of ice methamphetamine, two mobile phones and other related documents.
After interrogation, the suspect confessed that Pek Sen Sovann had ordered the drug from a Thai man named Chin to distribute it by making an appointment to receive the goods around the fishing pond. Meanwhile, Pich Ratha was used by a Thai man named Chin to take only one large package in a backpack and hand it over to the suspect, and she did not know that the package contained drugs.
He said that as for the suspect, Chin, a Thai national, the authorities are continuing to search for him and bring him to justice.
For the two suspects above, the specialized force has built a case to send the suspects along with the evidence to the court to deal with the legal process. Chairman of the 10th Senate Commission: Cambodia must work together to protect and maintain peace because peace brings development and prosperity
(Central): Mr. Mam Bunneang, Chairman of the 10th Senate Commission, said that Cambodia must work together to protect and maintain peace, because peace brings development and prosperity.
He said that in the sixth term of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, is committed to leading the Cambodian navy to achieve its vision, especially the protection and maintenance of peace and to continue to build physical infrastructure. To meet the living needs of the people, to take care of the vulnerable in various ways and to improve the lives of the people.
In addition to meeting with the people, Mr. Mam Bunneang met with the Kork Trop commune authorities to find out about the implementation of the commune safety policy and the challenges that the commune faces in the past and present.
He stressed that commune councils, village-commune protection guards and all working groups must pay attention to strengthening the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes, which must prevent and completely eliminate the traffic of distribution and distribution. Addiction to drugs, gambling of all kinds, big brother, big brother, gangster, domestic violence and crime to ensure the peace of the people.
He reminded all working groups and relevant authorities to pay close attention to providing good public services to the people, such as facilitating the issuance of various legal documents at the local level, identification, registration, birth certificate, death certificate.
On that occasion, Mr. Mam Bunneang inspected 2 newly built roads, the first road is 86 meters long and 3.5 meters wide, 1 meter thick concrete is located in Char village and the second road is long 2,080 meters, 4 meters wide, paved with a thickness of 1 meter, passing through 3 villages: Kork Pring village, Char village and Kraing Thmey village, which cost a total of $ 15,000, located in Kork Trop commune, Kandal Steung district, Kandal province.
During the meeting, Mr. Mam Bunneang brought the budget to the commune council, commune clerk, assistant village chief, administrative post, village protection and a total of 418 people, each received 20,000 Riels and other expenses. 10,200,000 Riels and bring 5,500 USD to hand over to the road construction technical team in the second phase with a total budget of 32,200,000 Riels.
