(Kandal): A truck with broken brakes came down from the Prek Samrong bridge and hit the fence of the school for children with intellectual disabilities, roaring like lightning this morning, January 08, 2019 in Takhmao city, province. The center causes the fence to be completely destroyed on one side and also affects the quality of the building.
Local sources said that prior to the incident, a truck with license plate number 3A-6694 was seen descending from the Prek Samrong Bridge at a reasonable speed and loudly honking the horn, which is suspected to be a car. Problems or broken brakes. Suddenly, the car crashed through the school fence, rumbling like lightning and shook the building where the disabled students were studying inside, causing a great shock.
The accident completely broke down one side of the school fence and may have affected the quality of the building, but did not injure any residents or students, just scaring them out of the school building.
After the incident, the traffic police measured and took the car to save for legal settlement, while the driver of the car escaped from the scene.
Please be informed that this building has just been renovated and inaugurated on September 20, 2018 with the help of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross.
Experts urge food industry owners to pay attention to quality and hygiene
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ou Serey Vuth, Deputy Director of the National Productivity Center of the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts, urged all food industry owners in Cambodia to pay attention to the quality of their food, especially to ensure Hygiene standards that give consumers confidence without worrying about health risks.
This statement was made on January 7, 2019 at the "Leang Leng" Enterprise Thanking Ceremony to the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts for helping to implement this enterprise to implement systematic standards. Successfully managed ISO food safety in the past, located in Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
At the same time, he also said that after the Royal Government of Cambodia has strengthened the quality of food for the well-being of the people, it is observed that the quality of food in Cambodia has been continuously improved.
In Cambodia, a number of enterprises have increased their capacity and been successful, with some reaching ISO certification for food safety, including Leang Leng Fish Sauce.
Mr. Ou Sereyvuth stated that in terms of obtaining quality, international standards are difficult to accept, in which it is necessary to recognize the national standard first before the international evaluation and recognition. In this regard, he said that in Cambodia, "Leang Leng" fish sauce enterprise, which has successfully achieved the ISO 9001 certification, not only gives confidence in the domestic market, even the overseas market is recognized.
He said that before reaching these certificates, his enterprise was well prepared and especially recognized a series of national standards. He called on other enterprises to consider food safety issues for consumers, and in particular, he wanted Cambodians to turn to eating more Cambodian products to promote the Cambodian economy to grow further.
