Heng Ratana Celebrates the 40th Anniversary of January 7 Victory Day in Leuk Dek District, Kandal Province
On that occasion, Mr. Heng Ratana read to the people, all party members, the full speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, who spoke at the celebration of the 40th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day (January 7). 1979-7 January 2019) held at the National Olympic Stadium on January 7, 2019 yesterday.
He said that January 7 is the second birthday of the Cambodian people, which is a historical fact that no one or force can distort or destroy.
Heng Ratana stated that it was January 7, 1979 that things were as they are today, and that January 7 was born out of the sacrifice of fresh flesh, fresh blood and courage of the Cambodian military leaders with the support of the army. Vietnam successfully conquers the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime. May the spirit of January 7 be immortal.
Mr. Heng Ratana added that the past 40 years are 40 years of unity, heroism and victory. The hard work of the Cambodian People's Party over the past 40 years has transformed the motherland of Cambodia from the ashes to the revival and growth with the greatest pride, which has strengthened the foundation for us to achieve the lofty goal: An independent, peaceful, free, neutral, democratic and progressive Cambodia.
He also called on all people to work together to ensure that the peace that is so hard to find today can be sustained for the long-term future of this poor Kingdom.
