Due to Donald Trump's anti-China policy, Chinese investment in the United States plummeted!
SAN FRANCISCO (Reuters) - US President Donald Trump's new policy aimed at preventing Chinese tech from invading the US market is undermining Chinese investment in US tech companies that have just opened and need investment. Necessary. This was released by Reuters on Monday evening, January 7, 2019.
Reuters, based on information obtained from several lawyers, said some Chinese investors, large and small, had walked out of the deal and canceled meetings with US companies that had just opened due to fears of overcrowding. Their investments or assets were confiscated or frozen under the new Donald Trump administration's policy, which aims to prevent Chinese technology from invading US markets and institutions.
Chinese investment in new US companies reached $ 3 billion in 2018. But that number has plummeted since Donald Trump signed a new law allowing US authorities to block foreign investment in US companies.
