(Phnom Penh): A group of robbers on two motorcycles, four of them, robbed a woman 24 days ago, on December 13, 2018 at 4 o'clock: 30 minutes at Trapeang Krasaing village, Sangkat Trapeang Krasaing, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Immediately after receiving complaints from the victims of the robbery, the Po Sen Chey District Police Force launched a vigorous search operation for 24 days, which led to the siege of the robbers. All 4 at once.
Colonel Yim Saran, police inspector of Por Senchey district, told Fresh News that the operation to arrest the robbers took place on January 6, 2019 at Tuol Sambo village, Prey Veng commune, Dangkor district, Phnom Penh, under his direct command. Lt. Gen. Thet, Phnom Penh Municipal Police, led the force by Mr. Leng Veasna, Chief of Criminal Division, Por Sen Chey District.
Inspector confirmed that the story before the incident at 4:30 am on December 13, 2018, the victim woke up to prepare and ride a motorcycle out of the house in order to open a fruit shop. At Chumpouvorn Market, when they arrived at the railway station, the scene suddenly appeared. The robbers appeared on two motorcycles, four of them robbed the victim and escaped. Missing.
Immediately after receiving this news, his forces launched a search operation, which took almost a month to reach the siege to arrest the four thieves. At the same time, Mr. Yim Saran also called on all people to be very careful.
These suspects are currently being processed by the criminal force of the Por Senchey District Inspectorate and sent to court.
