The standard of living of the general population has been steadily improving, reflected by an increase in the average per capita income from about $ 188 in 2000 to $ 1,563 in 2018. The poverty rate has dropped from about 53.2 percent in 2004 to about 13.5 percent in 2014 and is expected to continue to decline to around 10 percent today.
