"Until today, it has been very difficult. If we think about 1979, Cambodia is still empty-handed, in terms of the economy, it has dropped to zero," said Leng Phaly. "Samdech Techo Hun Sen has sacrificed and sacrificed a lot to liberate the people from the Pol Pot regime, a genocidal regime called the killing of people without mercy."
Mr. Ong Khon, a resident of Bor Seth district, Kampong Speu province, who came to receive this free medical service, also described the hardships that he personally lived under the Pol Pot regime.
"During the Pol Pot regime, it was very difficult to work from early in the morning until late at night," he said. As for the body of the people in the dark regime, the skin covering the bones is a thin body without proper and adequate diet. "The regime led by Pol Pot was a genocidal regime that caused many people to die, leaving their children behind."
Mr. Ong Khon thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for liberating Cambodia from the Pol Pot regime and even making Cambodia as prosperous as it is today.
