(Kep): This morning, January 7, 2019, the Rural Development Bank held a meeting to review the work results of 2018 and set the direction of the work plan for 2019 under the chairmanship of Mr. Kao Thach, General Director of Rural Development Bank. Board members, together with the Deputy Director General and all subordinate employees of the Rural Development Bank.
After listening to the report on the implementation results achieved by the relevant departments, Mr. Kao Thach praised and appreciated the results achieved from the internal reform of all relevant departments that made the mission of the Rural Development Bank. Successful and sustainable in line with the development of the banking and financial sector and the growth of the national economy.
At the same time, Mr. Kao Thach also reminded the results that the Rural Development Bank, a state-owned bank to serve the policy of the Royal Government in 2018 and is continuing to implement, including:
1: Expansion of mobile offices to provide micro-credit in Tbong Khmum and Battambang provinces to provide micro-credit with favorable interest rates to farmers in those areas.
2: Implementation of the Royal Government's special credit project to maintain the price of rice, in which the Rural Development Bank acts as the implementer of this project, and the result is a stable price of rice for farmers and the sale and purchase of rice in the market. Let there be congratulations from the farmers as well.
3. Implementation of the Royal Government's investment project on the construction of rice procurement centers and rice warehouses, in which the target areas are Battambang, Kampong Thom, Prey Veng and Kampong Speu provinces.
4: Develop policies to provide more effective credit in the agricultural sector.
5: Other projects that have been achieved and are being implemented with other partners of the Rural Development Bank, including the project of growing vegetables, raising pigs, etc., where the Rural Development Bank has played an important role in providing credit to farmers in the community and Help link the production of the head to the market.
In particular, for the direction of 2019, the Rural Development Bank will continue to implement, including:
1. Strengthen the dissemination of the Rural Development Bank as a state-owned bank to the general public.
2: Continue to strengthen the core banking system and the information technology system of the bank to modernize in response to the development of the national economy.
3. The Rural Development Bank will request the Royal Government to transform itself from a specialized bank to a commercial bank and serve the policies of the Royal Government.
4: Continue to strengthen good governance and effective training of human resources in the Rural Development Bank.
5: Continue to expand more mobile offices to provide micro-credit with favorable interest rates to farmers in Takeo, Prey Veng, Kampong Thom, Siem Reap, Preah Vihear, Banteay Meanchey and Pursat provinces.
6. The Rural Development Bank will examine the possibility of diversifying additional sources of capital through the Royal Government, concessional loans from financial institutions and development partners to expand loans at favorable interest rates to farmers, as well as help promote the implementation of policies. The government is more efficient and transparent.
7: Continue the mission in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government to provide credit and connect the agricultural community, producers, grow vegetables, livestock to the market. Hundreds of families in Leuk Dek district, Kandal province, cheated a group of land traders to get medals for standing as landowners for $ 50, the authorities are preventing this anarchic activity
The brokers told and lied to all the victims that once they had stamped the medals, they would have acquired a piece of land until they became the owners, which the company (anonymous) had arranged for That.
These anarchic activities also happened in the past, but after the action of the authorities and the authorities calmed down, suddenly at the end of December 2018, recently, this illegal activity occurred again in the commune. Kampong Phnom, Prek Tamlab Commune and Prek Dach Commune, Leuk Dek District, Kandal Province. However, both the authorities and the authorities, including the governor of Kandal province, Mr. Mao Phirun, have been working to prevent this from happening again.
According to reports from some local people, on December 26-27, 2018, brokers acted to inspire people to put money on five documents and make a copy of their ID cards. For $ 50, agree to sell the lake land west of National Road 1 in Kampong Phnom commune, Leuk Dek district, Kandal province.
This activity was ignored and prevented by the state authorities, Mr. Neou Touch, the chief of Kampong Phnom commune, the Leuk Dek district authority within its jurisdiction, saying that any people who take the money are responsible for themselves. Residents of Ampil Teuk village, Kampong Po village and Kbay Chroy village in Kampong Phnom commune say that they bring money and keep giving their thumbprints.
A resident of Koh Chamroeun village, Kampong Phnom commune, who was scared of being cheated by these traders on the morning of January 7, 2019, told Fresh News that he also received $ 50 from the broker. Also, by copying the ID card and going to stamp the medal on their documents because the broker said that he will stand as the owner of the lake land without any problem because the company has already prepared. In the future, the company will also make plans.
He said that not only did these activities happen to him, but also hundreds of other families went to receive $ 50 and stole medals at a broker's house in Soy Samu. Koh Chamroeun village, Kampong Phnom commune, on December 26-27, 2018, day and night.
However, Touch Chantha, Leuk Dek district police chief, also confirmed that this was indeed the case in his territory, but he took strong action and prevented it from happening again. Already have these targets.
Prek Dach commune chief Leuk Dek district Khmao Ron also said that recently there were brokers who wanted to operate in his commune, but the police and authorities did not allow that and also prevented activities. These do not happen again.
At the same time, the people who received $ 50 from these real estate agents were really scared of their actions that were overdone and that such over-stamping of medals was too short-sighted. In particular, he did not look at the contents of the documents to be printed, thinking only of wanting money and land.
When asked what to do so far, he said the group was also discussing plans to seek intervention from the authorities for its negligence.
It should be noted that at the end of September 2018, two ringleaders who used the image of buying people's hearts to collect ID cards to sign a contract to buy and sell wind land in Leuk Dek district, Kandal province were also arrested by the authorities and called to make a contract. Educate to stop these activities immediately as well.
According to reports, the reason why the traders formed such an anarchic movement is because they have already signed a contract with a Chinese company to arrange to buy land in those areas. They lost halfway through and had to face another Chinese company, which created a new trick to buy people's hearts as a barrier, creating a contract to sell land and air.
