(Riyadh): Women in Saudi Arabia will be notified via text message if divorced under a new law designed to prevent them from ending their marriage unknowingly. This is according to the release by Japan Times on Monday morning, January 7, 2019.
The new law, which came into force on Sunday, is also seen as a way to end a secret or unreported divorce that often occurs in society, as well as to ensure that Saudi women Fully aware of their family situation and able to protect some rights, including access to child support.
In addition, Saudi women can access their divorce information on the website of the Ministry of Justice of Saudi Arabia. In Saudi society, it is because men have the right to have more than one wife, and some men divorce one wife to another without informing the original wife about the divorce.
The new law comes into force as the Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman begins to grant greater rights to women, including allowing women to drive in local elections and enter the polls. In stadiums, etc., it was previously blocked.
