In a drinking dispute, the suspect pulled out a knife and stabbed the victim to death in Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province.
(Pursat): Four men, after being verbally abused, formed a drinking circle while drinking more and more alcohol. The victim was seriously injured until he died and then escaped into the forest (mountain area) and disappeared. This incident happened on the night of January 5, 2019 at the third dam in Veal village, Samrong commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province.
Sources from the police said that this case was caused by the suspect named Phuong Phen, alias Ken, male, 28 years old, living in Bao Puoy village, Leach commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province, to stay at the plantation at the scene. The victim, Ouk Sokhom, alias Nget, male, 25 years old, lives in Pich Ban village, Leach commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province.
