Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, CPP leaders and tens of thousands of people will celebrate January 7 Victory Day at the Olympic Stadium
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian People's Party, a party that has received support and sent the destiny of the people to lead for many years for the past 39 years, on the morning of Monday, May 2, Samreth Sak 2562. On January 7, 2019, tomorrow, the 40th Victory Day (January 7, 1979 - January 7, 2019) will be celebrated in the presence of tens of thousands of people at the National Olympic Stadium.
The Cambodian People's Party, as well as the Cambodian people throughout the country, considered January 7, 1979, the day of the historic victory of the Cambodian people who overthrew the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, ending the darkest period in Cambodia. Killed and killed nearly 3 million Cambodians. January 7, 1979 marked the reopening of a new era of independence, freedom, democracy and social progress.
People all over the country, especially in Phnom Penh, expect that the liberation of the country from General Lon Nol by the Khmer Rouge will end the war, bring peace and development to the country. Expectations were dashed after the new regime introduced a policy of evicting Cambodians from Phnom Penh and other towns to live and farm in various areas in Sre Chamkar district.
People are forced to live and work in groups, in rural cooperatives, forced to eat and sleep, and forced to work overtime, malnourished, and nearly 3 million Cambodians die. A large number of them were killed on charges of being traitors.
The suffering of the people in the black shirt regime ended after the patriotic forces of the Cambodian brave fighters united to form the National Salvation United Front on December 2, 1978 with the support of the Vietnamese army. And completely took the country out of the hands of Pol Pot on January 7, 1979.
Finally, through the win-win policy of the strong man, Techo Sen risked his life to enter the opposition camp, negotiate with the Khmer Rouge leaders in Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province, negotiate to take the Khmer Rouge army under the same government and end the war. Between Khmer and Khmer completely on December 29, 1998.
After the end of the war, Cambodia fully developed the country and made progress. Now, under the shadow of peace, Cambodia has gained more trade and foreign investment, Cambodia can maintain economic growth of around 7%, many national achievements have been highlighted in recent years.
Cambodia has moved from an impoverished country to a low-middle-income country today and is striving to become a high-middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country. 2050. Cambodia, once an isolated country, has become an actively integrated country in the world, has equal rights in the international arena and has hosted regional and international meetings.
