Mr. Veng Sakhon: January 7 Victory Day is a historic page in which the nation and its people were liberated from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Member of the Central Committee and Chairman of the Central Working Group for Kampong Siem District on January 6, 2019, said that the January 7 Victory Day is a new page in the history of the nation and its people. Liberated from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot (3 years, 8 months and 20 days) who slaughtered his own people.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Veng Sakhon presiding over the 40th Anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day and disseminating the results of the 41st General Assembly of the 5th CPP Central Committee at the hotel. January 7 in the provincial town of Kampong Cham this morning, January 6, 2019.
Mr. Veng Sakhon said that January 7 Victory Day is a new page in the history of the nation and its people being liberated from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot (3 years, 8 months and 20 days) that killed all its own people. More than 3 million people live through starvation, forced labor, disease, and a dark regime in which people live as cooperatives, collective owners, collective parks, and dictatorial organizations.
He continued that he clearly understood the catastrophe of the nation and the people and made people from all walks of life, heroes, heroines, young women, sacrificed their lives, stood up bravely, united and fought for the liberation of the motherland and The people left this genocidal regime until their victory on January 7, 1979.
He added that the page of the new historical era has reopened in the motherland of Cambodia, so that the nation and people of all walks of life, ethnic groups and religions throughout the country fully enjoy the rights, freedom, peace, stability and development. Continue to achieve great achievements in all areas, as we have seen as a testimony.
The national economy is growing, the population is growing, and the Royal Government is required to put in place plans and policies to further develop the country in response to global developments and the urgent needs of the nation and its people. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Veng Sakhon.
At the same time, he stressed that, of course, in order to maintain peace, stability, democracy and development, our people must work hard to support, protect and maintain all those achievements for a long time and let the spirit January 7 is immortal.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. Veng Sakhon also briefly commented to the ceremony on the development of the country as well as the international, economic, political, social and infrastructure development, which is a solid foundation for nation building and development.
Mr. Veng Sakhon brought the results of the 11-point General Assembly of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, along with the plan and strategic direction for implementation, along with the main recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party to disseminate and provide additional guidance. To members at all levels.
He added that, in particular, local authorities, teachers and the armed forces at all levels must be vigilant in protecting and maintaining peace, social stability, and resolutely oppose all forms of color revolution.
He said that it is necessary to take the spirit of responsibility to serve and provide services to the people honestly, fully, actively, comprehensively, responsibly and efficiently, and especially to continue to implement the K3 policy (birth, marriage and death). At the local level of Kampong Siem district more widely and more effectively.
In order to continue the development of both the realm and the realm of Buddhism, Mr. Veng Sakhon, together with the members of the working group, donated $ 5,000 to Wat Puthikaram in Krala commune, to support the district and commune party committees in each commune to receive 1 million riel and members of the organization Each ceremony 20,000 Riel and publicly announced that the party headquarters of Kampong Siem district will be built in the near future.
