The weapons that are mobile to participate in the above military exercises include warships, patrol boats, small ships equipped with anti-aircraft missiles and machine guns, as well as helicopters for maritime operations. The military exercise also includes live-fire exercises to strengthen the ability to work together in the army.
Seoul's military exercises took place in the South China Sea, which was formed near the maritime border between South and North Korea under a comprehensive military agreement signed by the defense chief. The two Koreas in September 2018 during a summit in Pyongyang between South Korean President Kim Jong Un and North Korean leader Kim Jong Un.
