(Battambang): A 2-storey school building with 12 classrooms worth more than 200,000 USD was donated by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior at Chrey High School in Chrey Village, Chrey Commune, Thmor Kol District, Battambang Province. Preliminary construction stone this morning, January 4, 2019.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Ouk Kimlek, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, Representative of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, and attended by Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang Province. Many teachers, students and citizens also participated.
Mr. Ouk Kimlek said that the younger generation is luckier than the older generation, which has many schools to study and all the schools are close to your house, it is very convenient. He urged students to study hard to apply the knowledge for their own benefit, as young people continue to be the successors of the country's bamboo vine and to have the opportunity to participate in building the nation for future social progress and progress. .
Mr. Ouk Kimlek confirmed that from the social security issue, only the Techo era had 100 peace. At the same time, there is peace, and we must prevent psychological warfare that has polluted the social environment through social media sites such as Facebook.
Mr. Ouk Kimlek also instructed all students to study hard for their future, to stay away from drugs, to respect traffic rules when traveling everywhere.
The ceremony was held in the presence of Lt. Gen. But Sopheap, Deputy Director of the Active Military Academy (Thmat Pong) and Chairman of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Sports Competition Commission at the Active Military Academy in Udong District, Kampong Speu Province.
On this occasion, Lt. Gen. But Sopheap stated that under the guidance of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army, the organization of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces sports competition showed Another great pride for the inauguration of the Victory Monument, which has recently been a great success and to join the national celebration of the 40th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day.
The lieutenant general said that for this year, civilians are not allowed to participate in the competition because the discipline is purely an army discipline and there are a lot of difficult jumps and fences, so the organization does not allow civilians to participate.
The lieutenant general stated that all subjects require candidates to be from 18 to 30 years old, and the subjects to be tested include: 4km armed run (combat uniform), K47 firearms, 25m hurdles, collective obstacles Etc. All disciplines should be shortened and allowed the masses of students to visit the same venue at the Koh Pich competition.
Lt. Gen. But Sopheap also requested all compatriots to join the defense sector to support the country to be strong and stable to develop under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister. Of Cambodia.
Separately, this afternoon, 3-star General Hun Manet will preside over the awarding ceremony and closing ceremony of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces sports competition.
The King of Cambodia issued a Royal Decree conferring the Royal Medal of Moha Sereyvath on the body of Senator Sok Chum, mother-in-law of General Hing Bun Heang
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree conferring the Royal Medal on the body of Senator Sok Chum, mother-in-law of General Hing Bun Heang. This is according to the Royal Decree obtained by Fresh News on January 4.
It should be noted that Rev. Sok Chum, mother-in-law of the Honorary General Hing Bun Heang, Deputy Chief of Staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Bodyguard Command, passed away at 8:25 AM. On the morning of January 3, 2019, at the age of 95, due to old age.
At present, the body is kept at the home of the Honorary General Hing Bun Heang in Prek Reang Village, Kampong Samnang Commune, Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
The Royal Government's decision to build a market to supply vegetables, fruits and a car park on the area of Boeung Ta Mok was decided by the Royal Government in June 2018, but the news of the construction has just been leaked recently.
Following the emergence of this new decision, traders across Doeum Kor Market and some circles are worried that the state will dismantle Doeum Kor Market so that they will no longer have shops.
This morning, January 4, 2019, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, led by Mr. Nuon Pharath, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, organized A press conference aims to confirm this case in detail.
He said that in the past, because we do not have a place to wholesale vegetables and fruits, some people have been selling vegetables and fruits on the streets and use the public sidewalks, which caused Traffic congestion as well as environmental issues, sanitation and other issues.
According to the Deputy Governor, the establishment of a wholesale fruit and vegetable market on 20 hectares of land in Ta Mok Lake so that businesses that do not have the right location to conduct their business in an orderly manner. In particular, for traders in the market can continue their business as usual without investing in Doeum Kor Market, do not worry about any comments that are contrary to the development plan of the Phnom Penh administration.
The Office of the Council of Ministers emphasized that the decision to establish a market for the supply of vegetables, fruits and car park in Boeung Ta Mok received a high note from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on June 08, 2018.
On August 2, 2018, the Office of the Council of Ministers also made a request to the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction for 20 hectares of land in Boeung Ta Mok to build a market for vegetables, fruits and parking.
It is noteworthy that on Monireth Street, south of Doeum Kor Market, especially in the early hours of the morning, traders often use these sidewalks as wholesale places to distribute fruits and vegetables from the beginning, but the traffic is almost impassable. Not only does it affect the environment, but traffic accidents are also sensitive points that can happen at any time.
