Today, five years ago, Cambodia was close to being hit by a violent riot plan to overthrow the legitimate government led by Sam Rainsy.
(Phnom Penh): On January 4, 2018 (2014-2019) is the 5th anniversary of the Royal Government of Cambodia considering that Cambodia is close to suffering from violent riots to overthrow the legitimate Royal Government under the pretext of demanding Raise wages led by Sam Rainsy, a former president of the former CNRP who lost the election and did not accept the results of the 5th parliamentary election.
The violent riots, attended by tens of thousands of people, used images of protesters demanding higher wages along Veng Srong Road, incited by Sam Rainsy and his accomplices, resulting in clashes that left four dead and several injured. Damage to public and private property. The violent riots took place in the middle of the night, which is not typical of non-violent protests by workers.
During the riots, protesters hurled sticks, stones and gas canisters at authorities, preventing them from moving forward. Seeing this abnormal situation, the competent authorities also cracked down until the corrupt plot was completely dissolved.
In the leaked video, Kem Sokha confessed at a forum in Australia on December 8, 2013 that the opposition party had followed the orders of the US superpower to plan to overthrow the Royal Government of Cambodia, following the example of the country. Yugoslavia and Serbia. While the governments of the two countries were overthrown by protests with foreigners behind them.
Sok Isan, spokesman for the ruling party, said that in the event of a violent incident on Veng Sreng Road, if not prevented and cracked down on in time, the risk of a peaceful Cambodia could be destroyed. Social unrest will ensue, and disasters of the past will return unpredictably.
"The leader who wants to bring Cambodia to disaster is none other than the traitor Sam Rainsy and his party," he said. "These people should be brought to justice in the most serious way to clear the grief of the dead and wounded."
CPP spokesman urges Sam Rainsy to be brought to justice as Sam Rainsy and his cronies staged a violent riot to overthrow the legitimate government on Veng Sreng Road five years ago. Many were killed and injured.
To this day, some unions continue to claim responsibility for the deaths as many public property was damaged without compensation. But those responsible for this should be the ones who used provocative tactics to lead the protesters to serve their ungodly ambitions.
