(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, has issued a notice banning his officials from using vehicles with state license plates outside of their working hours, especially all kinds of entertainment venues, including clubs, karaoke places, massage parlors and so on.
According to the announcement received by Fresh News on January 4, 2019, in order to ensure the effective management of state property and the dignity of state institutions and public servants of the Ministry of Rural Development, Introduce the officers who use motorcycles and vehicles of the Ministry in the following 3 points:
* 1: Must use motorcycles and vehicles with state license plates correctly, drive with dignity and respect the road traffic law properly.
* 2: Do not use motorcycles and vehicles with state license plates outside of their working hours, especially all kinds of entertainment, including clubs, karaoke, massage parlors and so on.
* 3: Do not allow others to use motorcycles and vehicles with state license plates for other purposes that are not related to the performance of their duties.
