Here are the statistics of international tourists buying tickets to Angkor 2018: The US government can finally revive after the draft budget was approved by Congress in the face of Mr. Tram's warning!
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The Democrat-controlled US House of Representatives has approved a draft budget aimed at ending the US government's shutdown in the face of threats from Donald Trump. This is according to a quote from the Russian newspaper Sputnik on Friday morning, January 4, 2019.
Under the draft budget, key institutions such as the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the Ministry of Commerce, the Ministry of Industry, the Ministry of Labor, the Ministry of Finance, the Ministry of Finance (Ministry of Treasury) and other federal agencies will be reimbursed until September 30. By the end of fiscal year 2019.
Prior to the approval, the White House said in a statement that the Democrats' draft budget overrides many unnecessary programs, including over-aid to foreign countries, such as Gaza. Syria, Pakistan, and UN programs.
The administration of US President Donald Trump has also warned against rejecting the draft budget, even though it aims to end the current government shutdown because Democrat officials are ignoring the urgent need for border security.
The US government has been in a state of complete closure since December 22, 2018, after Democrat lawmakers disagreed with Trump's demand for $ 5.6 billion to build a border wall. Between the United States and Mexico. A private company signed a memorandum of understanding with Life University to train trainees, students and workers to have the opportunity to study and work in Japan
