Death toll rises to 122 in typhoon, landslides in Philippines
MANILA (Reuters) - The death toll from rainstorms, landslides and floods in the Philippines has risen to 122, with dozens more reported dead. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Thursday night, January 3, 2019.
According to Philippine authorities, the deadliest area was 105 people in the central Bicol region, mostly due to severe landslides caused by heavy rains. Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte will visit Bicol on Friday to see firsthand the extent of the damage and to ensure that action is being taken to help the victims.
