The National Assembly closed the first session of the 6th legislature by approving 5 draft laws and 3 proposed laws
(Phnom Penh): On January 3, 2019, this is the closing day of the first session of the National Assembly, the sixth legislature, after running for more than three months. In this three-month session, the National Assembly approved five draft laws and three proposed laws.
The 1st session of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature achieved the following results:
First, decide on the validity of the mandate of 125 elected candidates of the National Assembly, 6th legislature of the National Assembly
Second: Approve the Internal Rules of the National Assembly of the 6th Legislature
Third: Vote in a package to elect the President, Vice-President of the National Assembly, Chairman of the Vice-Chairmen of all specialized committees of the National Assembly and give confidence to the Royal Government.
Fourth: Decided on the validity of the mandate of 38 elected candidates to replace the deposed MPs of the 6th legislature of the National Assembly.
Fifth: Election of additional members of the committees of the National Assembly
Sixth: Approved 5 draft laws proposed by the Royal Government
Seventh: Approve three proposed amendments to the law proposed by the signatory group of deputies.
For more details, please read the press release of the National Assembly, which has the following content: The Governor of Kampot Province requested his subordinates to continue to pay more attention in 2019 to jointly develop the province for further development.
(Kampot): In the meeting of Kampot Provincial Board of Governors on January 3, 2019, Mr. Chiao Tai, Provincial Governor, requested the municipal authorities, districts, departments and relevant units around the province to continue to pay more attention and cooperate better. Better in 2019 to jointly develop the province to further develop to meet the needs of the people.
The provincial governor praised and evaluated the results of the work in 2018, which the provincial administration has achieved many achievements in all areas, especially the provision of administrative services, public administration services and the development of infrastructure to serve the people proudly. .
This positive result comes from the efforts of all officials, including municipal, district, department and unit around the province, who have worked closely together in a spirit of high responsibility and good internal unity.
He added that on behalf of the provincial administration, he personally hopes that 2019 will continue to bring more achievements and results for our country as a whole and separately for Kampot under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The provincial governor also reminded and instructed the municipal authorities and departments and specialized units around the province to continue to pay more attention to cooperation in order to accelerate the development to serve the interests and improve the lives of the people. Even better in 2019.
Health official: People aged 25-64 are obese and have many diseases due to daily consumption of sweet drinks
(Phnom Penh): The director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Health Department, Dr. Ngy Mean Heng, said that people aged 25-64 years old are obese or overweight and have many diseases due to consuming sweet drinks every day.
This statement was made by the doctor on the occasion of opening the seminar on mainstreaming about reducing the consumption of sweet drinks through the practice of place welfare, this morning, January 3, 2019, there were participants from Sangkat councils, schools, public and private health centers. From 3 Khans: Chbar Ampov, Dangkor and 7 Makara, a total of 200 people.
Dr. Ngy Mean Heng stated that consuming sweet drinks every day causes us many diseases, especially in Cambodia, as well as in many countries around the world, there are many cases of non-communicable diseases caused by this sweet drink.
At the same time, one of the 200 participants said that for him, for the first time in this course, he provided knowledge as well as participants from other units to disseminate and apply to contribute to their well-being. To be better.
She stated that this is a collaboration between the Phnom Penh Capital Administration with the National Center for Health Promotion and the Ministry of Health, and this is one of the activities of the partnership for urban well-being, which is a global network of cities striving to reduce non-communicable diseases. Infections and injuries. Especially under the wise and skillful leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has made rapid growth and achievement in all areas.
She added that health issues are very important to reduce the risk of non-communicable diseases and injuries. Excessive consumption of sugary drinks can also cause health problems. The light of justice? Saudi prosecutors 'call for execution of five' conspiracy to kill journalist Khashoggi at Turkish consulate
