A group of Chinese robbers were seriously injured more than 10 days ago in Por Sen Chey district.
(Phnom Penh): A group of five thieves who robbed a Chinese man was seriously injured and stole $ 900, two mobile phones and some other items on December 20, 2018. At that time, the police force of Po Sen Chey district launched an operation to break up the case for only 13 days, arresting 4 suspects and leaving the other one, the force is still pursuing.
The operation to arrest the above suspects took place on January 3, 2019 at Chak Chrouk village, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Yim Saran confirmed that the four suspects were: first, Thon Van alias Bip, 19 years old, false occupation, staying near the scene, second, Mom Mengly, 19 years old, living together, third, Sambat Borin, 18, and fourth, An Mesa, 20. The victim, Chien Hanfeng, 40, a Chinese national, lived in a rented house in Chak Chrouk village, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey.
After the incident, the victim was taken to Chong Sing Stung Meanchey Polyclinic for treatment due to his serious condition and was sent to Calmette Hospital.
Mr. Chea Sovann confirmed that two suspects, Sambat Borin and An Mesa, after robbing the victim, came to perform an act of electric shock with eight other gang members who were arrested on January 31, 2018. Past that.
The four suspects are currently being investigated by the Po Sen Chey District Criminal Police Force, while the remaining members of the gang are still being investigated and arrested. Phnom Penh Police Detain 3-Day Student
