(Phnom Penh): Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign For January 3, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 6,104 vehicles, found 771 vehicles violated the law (76% motorcycles), educated 275 vehicles and fined 436 units, according to the official report of the Department of Traffic Police and Public Order of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 3,110 helmets and goggles were inspected on January 3, 133 education helmets and 421 glasses were fined.
(Korea): In order to promote ethnic culture and create a fun program for the Cambodian community in the Republic of Korea, the Cambodian Volunteer Youth Foundation in Korea, with the support of the Cambodian Embassy and the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, organized a night program. Happy New Year, the contest "Ability and Beauty of Cambodian Men and Women in Korea" and the song contest "Idol Workers of Cambodia" in 2018.
Both programs took place on the night of December 31, 2018 from 8:00 pm to 4:00 am under the presidency of Mr. Long Dimanche, Ambassador of Cambodia to the Republic of Korea.
