(China): The number of Chinese communities is growing in New York City, serving as a support network for Chinese immigrants and providing opportunities for Americans to get to know Chinese culture.
The Chinese city of Manhattan first appeared in the 1870s, and a century later it became the largest Chinese community in the United States.
(China): The use of online apps for group purchases such as groceries, beverages and services is becoming increasingly popular in China.
Over the years, the number of users of online shopping services has increased dramatically. In 2018, more than 300 million people will use the service to buy things in groups. Experts predict that the number of users will reach nearly 500 million by 2020.
Ms. Kong uses an online community app that offers group shopping services to purchase fruits and vegetables that will be delivered to your home the next day.
At the moment, traditional enterprises are looking to sell their products through this group buying service. According to Cao Qingxi, sales director of a wine supplier in Shenzhen, community-based wine sales and the use of group shopping services have helped boost the company's product sales. Fast.
Today, traditional retail businesses are finding it difficult to grow customers and orders, while group purchases are a new way of delivering goods directly to customers. And all this is possible due to the advancement of internet technology, which allows sellers to find a lot of resources or means to produce.
Mr. Mak Ngoy said that the project to improve higher education is a strong commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia to invest in higher education because it sees higher education as an important training ground. Human resources in Cambodia.
"The $ 92.5 million Higher Education Improvement Project will help the education, economy and society sector," said a senior education official. In that, it will help to improve the quality of education, because higher education is the production of human resources and training of human resources to serve the education sector in Cambodia.
Mr. Mak Ngoy added that if the universities in Cambodia improve well, our students who go out with full competence will help the education sector the most, especially human resources in teaching as well as serving other sectors in the education sector.
"When we produce good human resources, when they go out, the ability to work will make that work more efficient as well as boost the national economy," he said.
At the same time, the Director General of the General Department of Higher Education of the Ministry of Education and Sports also requested that all students who are studying higher education in their specialization must also focus on foreign languages, especially English and technology. Also.
It should be noted that this project to improve higher education is mainly focused on improving the quality of teaching and learning capacity, modernizing the curriculum and training teachers, building dormitories, improving resources to support Training and strengthening the internal education quality assurance system.
(Banteay Meanchey): The Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner on January 3, 2019, presented two Thai drug trafficking suspects, a man and a woman, who opened a shop to deceive the authorities and to smuggle drugs together. With 7 types of drugs, a total of more than 1 kg is located in the casino area of Poipet, Banteay Meanchey province.
The operation to crack down on drugs was carried out on New Year's Eve, January 1, 2019, in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province, under the leadership of Mr. Meas Chanpiseth, Prosecutor First, Banteay Meanchey Province and Brigadier General Chap Sophapthi, Deputy Commissioner for Crime Prevention.
Brigadier General Chap Sophabrith said that the operation to crack down on drugs leading to the arrest of the two suspects was in accordance with the order of Major General At Cam, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner on drug prevention and control measures.
After the police force, in cooperation with the Poipet City Police Force, received information that a Thai man had opened a shop and smuggled drugs at the above point, they searched and investigated until the target was identified and raided and raided. The suspect was a Thai national in Yiha 29 baht who was selling and distributing drugs.
Brigadier General Chap Sophapthi added that the two suspects are: Chhay Denmaha, male, 33 years old, Thai, Occupation: Worker, Hometown: Aranya Village, Aranya Commune, Aranya District, Sa Kaeo Province, Thailand. Arun Komanthi Chacha Viphananuvath, alias "Chacha", a 31-year-old Thai woman, is a saleswoman in her hometown of Sanaming Commune, San Sai District, Chiang Mai Province, Thailand.
According to the police, the Thai woman has been living in Cambodia for five years and has been selling goods at the Poipet casino for two years. From a Cambodian woman for resale to Chinese and Indonesian.
Currently, the two suspects and the above exhibits have been sent to court by the police force of the Office of Case Management for legal action.
