60 Factory Workers Injured in Traffic Accident in Svay Teap District, Svay Rieng Province
(Svay Rieng): At least 16 factory workers out of 60 victims were slightly injured when the driver of a truck carrying factory workers opened close enough, leaving insufficient safety space when the car in front of the floor The brakes of a truck carrying workers hit from behind, the brakes did not stick, but fortunately there was no danger to life.
The above accident happened at 6:30 AM on January 3, 2019 between km 139/140 on National Road 1 in Thnal Keng village, Kandieng Reay commune, Svay Teap district, Svay Rieng province.
After the accident, the sedan disappeared and the car caused the accident at the scene, with 60 workers traveling, causing 16 injuries, and is currently being treated at Svay Teap District Referral Hospital (all with minor injuries) and the driver. 32 people, 5 males. The truck carrying the workers was kept at the Svay Teap District Police Inspectorate.
According to the authorities, the cause of the accident was caused by driving close to each other, leaving insufficient safety space (when the car in front of the brakes, the car behind the brakes did not stick to the front of the car).
Russey Keo Police Detain Suspect and Confiscate 3 Packets of Drugs
(Phnom Penh): Police from Svay Pak Police Station arrested a suspect in a drug trafficking case and confiscated three packages of drugs and some bags for drug trafficking.
The arrest of the suspect took place at 1:00 pm on January 3, 2019 at the intersection of Group 7 Road, Lor Kambo Village, Sangkat Svay Pak, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
Svay Pak police told Fresh News that as a result of this search, police arrested a suspect named Saman Phen, male, 34 years old, a worker living on Concrete Road, Group 7, Kampor Village, Svay Pak Sangkat, Russey Keo District, Phnom Penh. The confiscated items included three small packages of white gram powder and some drug bags.
After detaining the suspect, the police sent him to the Russey Keo District Police Inspectorate to build a case to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
(Preah Sihanouk): The criminal police force of Preah Sihanouk province patrolled and arrested two suspects riding a motorbike suspected of being involved in aggravated theft (shock) and drug trafficking at 4:00 am On January 2, 2019, at the point of Street 502, Group 14, Village 4, Sangkat 4, Preah Sihanouk Province.
According to the provincial police, the two suspects are: Sao Tola, male, 28 years old, unspecified occupation, residing in O'Chamnar village, O'Oknha Heng commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province (motorcyclist) and 2: Name: Lat Phanit, Male, 21 years old, Unreal occupation, Real residence.
Please note that in the above case, the competent force has handed over to the Anti-Drug Office to continue the procedure to the provincial court.
The third ring road with an investment of $ 259 million near the new Phnom Penh Airport project is scheduled to officially open in mid-January!
This third ring road is an important strategic road for the Royal Government of Cambodia to facilitate traffic. In particular, this ring road is just over 1 km from the new Phnom Penh Airport project.
Please be informed that the third ring road project, which is scheduled to open on January 14, has been signed by the Royal Government of Cambodia to receive a concessional loan agreement of 259 million US dollars from the Chinese side for the construction project. On July 10, 2018.
The Ministry of Public Works and Transport, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, has signed a construction contract with a Chinese construction company, Shanghai, to carry out the construction of the third ring road, which will also be technically inspected by a Chinese company, Guangzhou Van An.
This Third Ring Road is a new road that connects Cambodia's main national roads, from Prek Pnov Bridge, National Road 5 to National Road 4 (this section has already been built by Phnom Penh Capital Hall). National Road No. 3, National Road No. 2, National Road No. 21 and National Road No. 1, connected to the new Phnom Penh Port, which was built under the concessional credit framework from the People's Republic of China.
The third ring road is just over a kilometer from the airport project. Namely, the Third Ring Road will play an important role in contributing to the facilitation of traffic in Phnom Penh and the implementation of Cambodia's industrial development policy and will be a new road after the Second Ring Road. Construction is underway.
The Concessional Loan Agreement for the Third Ring Road Construction Project is another fruitful fruit of the comprehensive strategic partnership between Cambodia and the People's Republic of China under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Daily Summary of National and International News on January 03, 2019
