(Oddar Meanchey): A woman died after giving birth at the Anlong Veng District Referral Hospital in Oddar Meanchey province on the night of January 1, 2019 due to bleeding from the uterus. After the incident, the victim's husband filed a complaint with the Anlong Veng District Police Inspectorate to seek justice and demand $ 15,000 in compensation for mental illness.
The director of Anlong Veng District Referral Hospital, Mr. Neou Sam An, told Fresh News on January 3, 2019, the family would like to express its condolences for the above tragedy, while the family of medical professionals has done their best. To rescue the woman above.
However, the victim's husband, Heng Kheng, 37, of Thmey village, Trapeang Prasat commune, Trapeang Prasat district, Oddar Meanchey province, confirmed that his dead wife was 28-year-old Khoem Sothea. Years.
Unfortunately, after about 40 minutes of rescue efforts, the woman died. According to the director of the hospital, women with endometriosis suffer from one in 1,000 women. He also described the postpartum woman's condition: her uterus was ulcerated and the placenta had an abnormal odor when mixed with the ulcer at the end.
In addition, Mr. Khlo Huot, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Health Department, also confirmed that the Anlong Veng District Office had also provided him with this information since the night of the incident. The contractions are weak and the doctors try their best to help with the blood transfusion and uterine contractions.
Mr. Khloe Huot added that he did not have the ability to pay up to $ 15,000 in compensation for mental illness, because every day he only serves the public service to the people. However, the medical family also attended the funeral and expressed their condolences to the family of the deceased. 3-Star General Hun Manet: Recruitment of officers must select officers who have real ability according to measures, transparency, efficiency and justice
(Phnom Penh): Lieutenant General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army and Chairman of the Sub-Committee on the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Recruitment Sub-Committee 2019, attended a meeting to disseminate and inspect the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces recruitment. 2019 This morning, January 3, 2019, at the General Command.
The General said that the recruitment of officers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in 2019 has increased compared to 2018, and this increase has increased in the regional armies. This is due to the fact that the recruitment of officers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in previous years has been accurate, fair and transparent.
He would also like to express his gratitude and appreciation and appreciation to the Central Working Group of the Sub-Committee on Recruitment Examination of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces 2019 and all relevant departments for their hard work in carrying out the task of organizing well. Succeed because we work together for success.
"Our main task in recruiting officers is to select truly capable officers in a transparent, efficient and fair manner," he said. This is a big goal that the leadership gives. "Hopefully, the commission will be more successful by studying the shortcomings of the past year and making clear plans, procedures, materials, time, accuracy and efficiency."
On behalf of the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense, the Commander-in-Chief would like to thank all the team for their dedication in organizing the recruitment competition smoothly, efficiently and transparently, as well as participating in strengthening and maintaining Maintain the trust of the people and the youth in our army to provide warmth and justice and trust only for the children of the people to serve the nation and the future of our army together.
It should be noted that the recruitment of officers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, the 23rd generation of active duty officers, the 11th generation of infantry officers, the 12th generation officers and the 2019 military technical officers will be held at On January 13-15, 2019, there will be 6 centers in Phnom Penh, 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th and 5th military districts, focusing on general knowledge, foreign languages and physical education.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: The rehabilitation of Mr. Kem Sokha depends on the court procedure (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, confirmed on January 3, 2019 that The rehabilitation of Kem Sokha, the former president of the former Cambodia National Rescue Party, may have the right to return to politics, depending on the court's procedures, because the court is working on this case.
In an interview with the media after the session of the National Assembly, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said, "We have to look at the problem from the beginning, why he (Mr. Kem Sokha) was detained by the authorities to see the reason We need to see why so far the court process is not over, he is still in court."
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also said that so far the Ministry of Interior has not received a request for rehabilitation from former CNRP leaders who have been deprived of their political rights due to amendments to Article New 45 (duplicate) of the Law on Political Parties has not yet entered into force.
Please be informed that the proposed law on the amendment of the law on political parties, which could pave the way for politicians who have been banned by the court to have the full right to resume politics, was fully supported by the Senate in its session on the morning of December 25. 2018, which will come into force soon.
Proposed Law Amending the Law on Political Parties was signed by 87 deputies, amending the new Article 45 (Duplicate) of the Law on Political Parties by adding a new paragraph in the new Article 45 (Duplicate) as follows: To:
The proposed law was fully approved by the National Assembly on December 13, 2018, after being reviewed by an expert committee.
It should be noted that the preparation of this law was made after the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, issued an important statement to ease the situation of opposition politicians who were banned by the court in the past. Such as facilitating foreign media in Cambodia, civil society organizations and unions. Amazing! Ancient Mexican sculpture found in human skins (Photo inside)
