Official: Thai goods are banned from being imported into Cambodia for sale if the Thai side still does not allow them to import goods from Cambodia to Thailand
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Chea Kimseng, Governor of Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province, on the morning of January 3, 2019, defended his strong position that if the Thai authorities at the An Ses border checkpoint continue to ban Cambodian traders from bringing goods Another 23 items to be sold in the Thai market, the Cambodian side also strictly prohibits many Thai goods into Cambodia.
The district governor further stated that the reason for blocking goods from entering Cambodia was that the Thai side blocked the Cambodian business from importing garlic tubers to sell in the Thai market.
