North Korea came to learn demining techniques in Cambodia, especially the US bomb disposal!
(Phnom Penh): The International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) has led a delegation of North Korean officials to learn about demining techniques in Cambodia, especially the removal of bombs from US aircraft.
The visit took place recently at the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC) in Phnom Penh.
Heng Ratana, Director General of SIMAC, stated, "The International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) has led a delegation from South Korea to study demining techniques and explosive remnants of war with SIMAC." "And what the North Korean delegation is most interested in is the bomb disposal technique."
Since operating more than 20 years ago, CMAC has destroyed 2.7 million landmines and unexploded ordnance, about 70 percent of the landmines left and 53 percent of the total land area. Mine. These include cluster munitions and bombs dropped on US aircraft.
