The following is the announcement of the National Assembly on the results of this plenary session: The Student Association of the Royal University of Agriculture organized a mixed arts performance to celebrate the 40th Victory Day on January 4.
(Phnom Penh): Students Association of the Royal University of Agriculture will organize a mixed arts program to celebrate the 40th Victory Day of the overthrow of Democratic Kampuchea under the theme "January 7, the Legacy of the Living Kingdom of the Kingdom of Cambodia II" At the Royal University of Agriculture in the hall of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen on January 4, 2019.
This program aims to promote the art form so that the younger generation can understand the art form and want to show to the younger generation as well as to show people around the world a greater understanding of the great values and merits of Victory Day. January 7 Without January 7, there would have been no resurrection of the Buddhist Empire and the Second Kingdom of Cambodia.
This scene also reflects that January 7 was celebrated by the leaders of the three princes who liberated the motherland from the dark genocidal regime and made progress in all areas should be proud until Currently.
In fact, on January 2, 2019, the Student Association of the Royal University of Agriculture organized a press conference on the organization of a mixed arts performance to celebrate the 40th Victory Day of the overthrow of Democratic Kampuchea under the theme "January 7, the legacy of the living Buddha. The Kingdom of Cambodia II.
The President of the Student Association of the Royal University of Agriculture, Mr. Kim Chan Roza, said that the organization of this program can enable young people to promote the arts through dance, singing and performing arts.
Mr. Kim Chan Rosa added that in part to commemorate the history that Cambodia went through the tragedy of the genocidal regime, but with the great merits of Victory Day on January 7, without January 7, there is no revival. The Buddhist Empire and the Second Kingdom of Cambodia.
Ung Ratana, Vice Chancellor of the Royal University of Agriculture, said: "We have this day because we have January 7, the day before we liberated millions of Cambodians from the genocidal regime or from the prison without walls. The next generation did not go through that. ”
Mr. Ung Ratana stated that the establishment of this program is a reminder of the history to the students to understand the efforts of the top leaders of the Cambodian People's Party, which has pushed the country to progress with equal rights. International stage. Apple's hit by Sino-US trade war amid earnings warnings
