(Phnom Penh): As of Thursday, January 3, 2019, workers at W&D factory in Sangkat Stung Meanchey, Phnom Penh, have been on strike for several days, demanding that the factory owner open Their seniority pay by 2018.
The factory side did not refuse to pay the seniority pay to the workers, but asked to pay in installments from 2019 to every 6 months, once in 6 months and 12 months, that is, until the seniority payment is paid. . This was confirmed by Mr. Heng Sour, spokesman for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
According to the workers, the W&D factory has never had a hard time paying their monthly salaries. But what they are demanding now is seniority money. Regarding the seniority pay, by explaining the reasons for the workers' desire for the seniority pay, it should be that the issue is resolved, there should be no protracted protests lasting more than half a month.
