(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Information, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, presented a plan to create three or four additional TV channels for the national media in order to disseminate information more widely, in addition to webcasts and audio broadcasts.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith made this statement in an interview with the Cambodian News Agency AKP and the National Radio of Cambodia on January 2, 2019 at the Ministry of Information.
In that interview, Mr. Khieu Kanharith pointed out that the TV stations that are planned to be added are for the Cambodian News Agency AKP and the National Radio of Cambodia, while currently both institutions only broadcast on the website and on the airwaves.
According to the Minister of Information, there are currently 512 newspapers, 72 news bulletins, online newsletters, more than 200 live and cable television stations, and more than 200 live and broadcast stations. There are five digital systems.
With the development of the media, the Minister also noted that Cambodian journalists also have professional development and some journalists can engage in journalism with foreign media by writing and analyzing well-known media. Of the world as well.
