Earlier this week, US President Donald Trump signed the law into full force, urging the United States to increase its involvement in Indo-Pacific affairs, as well as strengthen support for the region, including arms sales to the region. Washington's allies include Taiwan.
Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Jiang Yu's Regular Press Conference on March 20, 2012 Chinese Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Jiang Yu's Regular Press Conference on March 20, 2012 According to Lu, Beijing urges the United States to stop enforcing the law and resolve the Taiwan issue properly to avoid undermining bilateral relations and peace and stability in the Taiwan Straits.
On the same day, Chinese President Xi Jinping stressed that the Taiwan issue is an internal matter of China and does not allow any outside interference. The Chinese president also called on Taiwan to unite with Beijing to ensure lasting peace, while China also warned that the use of force is still possible in the event of any foreign attempt to secede from Taiwan. From mainland China.
More than 280,000 people and tourists participate in the Global New Year 2019 in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): More than 280,000 national and international tourists enjoyed the Global New Year 2019 celebration in Siem Reap.
The event was presided over by Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province on December 31, 2018 from 20:00 pm to 00:30 pm at the riverside park north of the Royal Stone Bridge. The administration of Siem Reap Provincial Hall has organized a colorful fireworks display, lighting decoration on some of the main streets and a new music venue in Siem Reap.
The total number of national and international tourists participating was 284 thousand, an increase of 7.96% compared to 2018, which was 263 thousand. Safety and order are also good.
Two Suspects Arrested in Drug Trafficking Case in Sangkat Svay Pak, Khan Russey Keo
(Phnom Penh): The Svay Pak Police Force, led by Lieutenant Colonel Koul Yi, Russey Keo District Inspector, arrested two suspects immediately after searching and found seven packages of drugs while continuing the operation. Road Traffic Law on National Road No. 5 at Group 1, Svay Pak Village, Sangkat Svay, Khan Russey Keo at 11:30 on January 2, 2019.
Russey Keo District Police Inspector confirmed that in the operation to enforce the road traffic law and to arrest the two drug trafficking suspects, in addition to finding drugs, the police confiscated a Nokia mobile phone (flashlight). ) A bag for some drugs and equipment with a blue MacSuru motorcycle with license plate Phnom Penh 1Y-7927.
According to the inspector, the suspects, Ny Rifin, male, 33 years old, and Sman Salim, male, 20 years old, unspecified occupation (drug traffickers), resided in Group 1, Village 1, Sangkat Chrang Chamres 1, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
After the arrest, the two suspects, along with exhibits related to drug trafficking activities, were taken into custody for further questioning at the Russey Keo District Police Inspectorate in order to build a case to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for processing.
