(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. San Xian Ho, Governor of Poipet City and Mr. Oknha Sok Huot, Deputy Director General of Cintri Company, about 100 students, civil servants, villagers, on January 2, 2019, launched a campaign to clean up the environment and welcome the new garbage collection company. Cintri.
San Xianhu said that 2019 is the new year and there is a new garbage collection company. A total of 17 garbage collection trucks are being tested in the garbage collection in Poipet city, if not more trucks have been added to make it easier for people to take the garbage.
Mr. Oknha Sok Huot said that the reason for investing in garbage collection in Poipet is because in the past saw a lot of garbage in Poipet, which caused serious damage.
Mr. Oknha added that at the request of the municipal authorities, the company requires a tricycle to facilitate the collection of garbage on the streets, while the landfill site, we have a land size of about 10 hectares, a distance of more. 10 km from the town does not cause harm to the people.
At the same time, the Governor of Poipet City, as well as Cintri Company, called on all citizens to store garbage properly, have a convenient place to pick up garbage and participate in regular payments.
Three More Chinese Arrested in Sihanoukville Murder Case
Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin confirmed that on December 31, 2018 at 19:50 at Group 6, Village 2, Sangkat 2, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province, there was a case of intentional (unsolved) homicide. Caused by four suspects, a Chinese man broke into the car of the same Chinese victim while the victim was getting in the car to drive home.
While they were beating and threatening the victim with a firearm in the car, the victim's workers saw and there was a commotion, then all four suspects escaped. After receiving the information, the criminal police planning force, in cooperation with the Sihanoukville Police Inspectorate and the Sangkat 2 police force, conducted a thorough search and arrested a number of suspects.
According to Major General Chuon Narin, in this case, the Office of Minor Criminal Police is building a case to be sent to the provincial court for legal action. International sanctions will cost Venezuela's "$ 20 billion" in 2018, but the president claims oil, gold, diamonds and steel can withstand it!
(Caracas): International sanctions cost Venezuela about $ 20 billion in 2018. This was confirmed by Venezuelan President Nicolas Maduro, quoted by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Wednesday afternoon, January 2, 2019.
According to Maduro, the multibillion-dollar loss due to international sanctions has prevented his country from buying the world's essential commodities such as food and medicine. The Venezuelan president added that the weak Latin American economy was suffering from financial blockade by the international community.
"Venezuela is capable of overcoming these obstacles due to its adequate resources, combined with Venezuela's efforts to increase oil, gold, diamonds and iron ore production," Maduro said.
In recent years, the international community, especially the United States, has lifted a series of sanctions on Venezuela, including Venezuela's digital currency settlement and a ban on gold imports from the South American nation.
A gas leak caused a fire in Tuol Kork district, an old man was rushed to hospital.
(Phnom Penh): A gas leak caused a fire that shocked the authorities to intervene immediately, in this incident caused a man to be injured and taken to the hospital by the people.
The fire occurred at 1:45 pm on January 2, 2019, along Kampuchea Krom Road, Sangkat Toek Laak I, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
Authorities said that before the incident, the owner of the house turned on the gas while boiling water, suddenly leaking gas pipe, causing a fire. The owner of the house immediately used fire hoses and called for a fire truck from the Phnom Penh Municipal Police to intervene.
Later, firefighters dispatched two vehicles to intervene.
In this firefighting operation, the police managed to control the situation one hundred percent by using many fire hoses. The two fire trucks that came to intervene were not used.
