According to Mr. Chea Ny, the inspection was conducted in accordance with the instructions of the General Department of CamControl and based on the law on quality control, safety of products, goods and services and duties. Facilitate trade by managing risk, controlling the general appearance of vegetables, fruits, food, on labels, packaging, dates, etc.
Experts also check the quality of compliance by conducting a preliminary analysis of the product using a test kit to find banned chemicals such as porcine and formalin. Camcontrol to identify risks.
Mr. Chea Ny said that as a result, CamControl branch and professional officers inspected vegetables, fruits and beverages that traders import at Cham Yeam International Gate, CamControl did not find any fruits and vegetables containing chemicals.
He said that in this regard, professional officers monitor and test continuously and responsibly, and traders have a higher awareness of this issue. The day-to-day inspections did not confiscate any vegetables, fruits and other items, as the traders were more knowledgeable. Koh Kong CamControl Branch Inspects Chemicals for Fruits and Vegetables Imported from Thailand through Cham Yeam International Gate
