SEOUL: North Korean leader Kim Jong Un has said he is ready to denuclearize and resume talks with the United States and South Korea to resolve tensions on the Korean Peninsula. But at the same time, Kim also warned that Pyongyang would retaliate if Washington refused to lift economic sanctions. This was released by Sputnik on Wednesday afternoon, January 2, 2019.
Kim Jong Un made the remarks at a celebration of the Global New Year 2019 on Tuesday this week. Responding to the message, US President Donald Trump on Wednesday also reiterated that he would like to meet with Kim Jong Un for a second time soon in response to the North Korean leader's expression of intent. Want to restore relations with the United States.
Donald Trump and Kim Jong Un met at a summit in June 2017 in Singapore with pledges that he remains committed to the elimination of nuclear weapons on the Korean Peninsula. But the denuclearization process has not progressed, and Washington has not eased economic sanctions and pressure on Pyongyang.
