National Defense Spokesman: In 2018, Cambodia-Vietnam found 590 remains of Vietnamese volunteer soldiers
(Phnom Penh): General Chhum Socheat, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense, said that in 2018, the Cambodian Army, in cooperation with the Vietnamese search team, found 590 more Vietnamese remains.
"The Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) has cooperated with the Vietnamese team to search for the remains of 590 Vietnamese volunteer soldiers, including those found by the regional army," a spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense said on his Facebook page. In particular, 52 items, 36 units of the 1st Zone, 207 units of the 2nd Zone, 135 units of the 3rd Zone, 92 units of the 4th Zone and 68 units of the 5th Zone.
During the 17 years (2000-2017) of this operation, the Commission on Special Affairs of the two governments signed 15 memoranda of understanding. With the strong cooperation of the Commission on Special Affairs, all levels of institutions and the support of the Cambodian people, to date, more than 17,850 remains of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army have been found and collected. Also repatriated to a cemetery in Vietnam.
At the same time, according to the report of the Special Committee for the Search for the Remains, the remains of nearly 4,000 Vietnamese people in Cambodia have not yet been found. Cambodia and Vietnam have set a goal of ending the search for the remains of all Vietnamese in Cambodia and repatriating them by 2020. Senior Minister Kun Kim Visits Veterans in Muk Kampoul District, Kandal Province
(Kandal): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, paid a courtesy call on Mr. Ly Saleh, a struggling veteran living in Chroy Metrey Leu village, Russey Chroy commune, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province, and was visited by Cambodian Muslims in several villages. People also came to participate on December 30, 2018.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, sent a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Association to all Khmer Muslims in Chroy Metrey Leu village and thanked them for their support. Vote for the CPP and ask to continue to support the CPP for the country to achieve peace and development.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kattipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, Senior Minister Kun Kim donated 1 million Riels and some other food items to Mr. Ly Saleh.
