Watch the detailed video below: Chinese President: Taiwan will get lasting peace if they come together peacefully
BEIJING (Reuters) - Chinese President Xi Jinping on Wednesday said Taiwan would receive a lasting guarantee of peace if it joins peacefully. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua in the morning of Wednesday, January 2, 2019.
Xi made the remarks on the occasion of the 40th anniversary of the message to the Chinese people in Taiwan in the new year 2019. The Chinese president called for more efforts to build the foundation for peaceful unity, stressing that the Chinese people should help each other.
According to Xi Jinping, both sides (mainland China and Taiwan) should promote free trade flows, connect infrastructure, exchange energy and resources, and share industry standards.
